window.COT_DATA = {"version":"dental-cot-47-v2-diagnostic-time","cases":[{"id":"PMC13242668","title":"Adenoid ameloblastoma of the mandible: report of a new case of a distinct type of odontogenic neoplasms.","category":"odontogenic_cyst_tumor","license":"cc by","authors":["Nourhan Abou Madawi","Ahmed Abdou","Nermine El Bahey","Magi Moussa"],"journal":"BMC oral health","year":"2026","citation":"Nourhan Abou Madawi, Ahmed Abdou, Nermine El Bahey, Magi Moussa. Adenoid ameloblastoma of the mandible: report of a new case of a distinct type of odontogenic neoplasms. BMC oral health. 2026. doi: 10.1186/s12903-026-08711-x.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/Open Access This article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, which permits use, sharing, adaptation, distribution and reproduction in any medium or format, as long as you give appropriate credit to the original author(s) and the source, provide a link to the Creative Commons licence, and indicate if changes were made. The images or other third party material in this article are included in the article’s Creative Commons licence, unless indicated otherwise in a credit line to the material. If material is not included in the article’s Creative Commons licence and your intended use is not permitted by statutory regulation or exceeds the permitted use, you will need to obtain permission directly from the copyright holder. To view a copy of this licence, visit http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.","copyright":["© The Author(s) 2026"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13242668/","doi":"10.1186/s12903-026-08711-x","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history|demographics|symptom]: 19岁男性，左下颌疼痛性肿胀4个月，无系统病史及牙科病史\n- E6 [clinical_exam]: 术前初步诊断包括成釉细胞瘤、牙源性角化囊肿、动脉瘤样骨囊肿\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Segmented panoramic view showing multilocular radiolucency in the left side of the mandible related to molar teeth and causing root resorption\n- [cbct/ct] Cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) of the skull demonstrating the extent of bone destruction in the mandible\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] A and (B) Clinical intraoral presentation of the studied case of adenoid ameloblastoma\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者为19岁男性，左下颌出现疼痛性肿胀4个月。 诊断意义：支持存在局部病变\n\n2. 术前初步诊断中包括了成釉细胞瘤作为可能的诊断之一。 诊断意义：支持腺样成釉细胞瘤的可能性\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于病史和临床表现以及术前初步诊断，腺样成釉细胞瘤是一个需要考虑的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；当前证据不足以完全区分腺样成釉细胞瘤与其他初步诊断如牙源性角化囊肿、动脉瘤样骨囊肿。\n","answer":"\n腺样成釉细胞瘤（Adenoid ameloblastoma）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Segmented panoramic view showing multilocular radiolucency in the left side of the mandible related to molar teeth and causing root resorption\n- [cbct/ct] Cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) of the skull demonstrating the extent of bone destruction in the mandible\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] A and (B) Clinical intraoral presentation of the studied case of adenoid ameloblastoma\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者为19岁男性，左下颌出现疼痛性肿胀4个月。 诊断意义：支持存在局部病变\n\n2. 术前初步诊断中包括了成釉细胞瘤作为可能的诊断之一。 诊断意义：支持腺样成釉细胞瘤的可能性\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于病史和临床表现以及术前初步诊断，腺样成釉细胞瘤是一个需要考虑的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；当前证据不足以完全区分腺样成釉细胞瘤与其他初步诊断如牙源性角化囊肿、动脉瘤样骨囊肿。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n腺样成釉细胞瘤（Adenoid ameloblastoma）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC13242668/12903_2026_8711_Fig2_HTML.jpg","name":"12903_2026_8711_Fig2_HTML.jpg","caption":"Segmented panoramic view showing multilocular radiolucency in the left side of the mandible related to molar teeth and causing root resorption","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"f1ae01c31da0ddf02f108f076a47021e4ec9b747935bbffd300adf645962eaf0","width":646,"height":471},{"src":"assets/PMC13242668/12903_2026_8711_Fig1_HTML.jpg","name":"12903_2026_8711_Fig1_HTML.jpg","caption":"A and (B) Clinical intraoral presentation of the studied case of adenoid ameloblastoma","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"364883db87b6b4a1e2401096b2d486984c8d8d0ea7155f5444688079ab0aa419","width":969,"height":330},{"src":"assets/PMC13242668/12903_2026_8711_Fig3_HTML.jpg","name":"12903_2026_8711_Fig3_HTML.jpg","caption":"Cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) of the skull demonstrating the extent of bone destruction in the mandible","types":["cbct","ct"],"sha256":"b010ba9b050b897f40c4b363d65b4a6e988c7d31f7396235d58bb96c74b611cd","width":646,"height":814}],"english":{"question":"A 19-year-old man presents with a four-month history of painful swelling on the left side of the mandible. CBCT shows a destructive mandibular lesion with resorption of the first- and second-molar roots. Histology shows an interlacing cribriform network, duct-like structures containing myxoid material, and morules; immunohistochemistry shows strong beta-catenin expression and faint BRAF staining, with a Ki-67 score of 15. Using the accompanying panoramic radiograph and intraoral photograph, describe the visible findings, compare the relevant differentials, and give the final diagnosis.","caption":"\nOPG:\n- A multilocular, honeycomb-like radiolucency occupies the left mandibular molar region, with resorptive changes affecting adjacent roots.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- The left mandibular molar region shows approximately 2.5 cm by 2 cm of buccal expansion with a continuous mucosal surface.\nCross-modal summary: Both modalities localize the abnormality to the left mandibular molar region: the panoramic image shows the intraosseous and root changes, while the clinical photograph shows the corresponding surface contour.\n","think":"\n1. Clinical problem representation: The patient is a 19-year-old man with four months of painful left mandibular swelling. The history establishes the patient, site, symptom, and duration, but it does not by itself determine the histologic nature of the jaw lesion.\n\n2. OPG and RGB interpretation: The OPG shows a multilocular radiolucency and adjacent root resorption, whereas the RGB photograph shows buccal expansion at the same site. Their spatial agreement establishes the location and visible extent of the process, but these appearances are not sufficient to assign a histologic subtype.\n\n3. Diagnostic work-up: CBCT further documents mandibular bone destruction and molar-root resorption. More importantly, the specimen shows the cribriform, duct-like, and morular combination described in the paper for this entity; beta-catenin staining is treated as ancillary evidence, while faint BRAF immunostaining is not interpreted as a genetic result.\n\n4. Differential diagnosis: The paper identifies conventional ameloblastoma and adenomatoid odontogenic tumor as the main differentials. Conventional ameloblastoma shares an ameloblastomatous component, and AOT can share duct-like structures; however, the combined cribriform, duct-like, and morular pattern in this specimen provides the distinction emphasized by the source.\n\n5. Integration and diagnostic boundary: The diagnosis is reached because the case-specific histology matches the defining combination described in the report, with beta-catenin immunohistochemistry serving only as supporting information. OPG and RGB are useful for localization and extent, but the subtype is established by tissue morphology rather than by the images alone.\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- Conventional ameloblastoma: Supporting features—Ameloblastomatous epithelial component ; Multilocular mandibular radiolucency; Opposing features—The specimen contains the combined cribriform, duct-like, and morular pattern emphasized for the final entity; Status—less_likely\n- Adenomatoid odontogenic tumor (AOT): Supporting features—Duct-like structures are shared with the final entity; Opposing features—The remaining histologic architecture distinguishes the final entity from AOT; Status—less_likely\nLimitations: OPG and RGB cannot independently determine the histologic subtype. ; BRAF protein immunostaining does not establish BRAF mutation status.\n","answer":"\nAdenoid ameloblastoma. The histologic pattern establishes the diagnosis; beta-catenin immunohistochemistry is ancillary.\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- A multilocular, honeycomb-like radiolucency occupies the left mandibular molar region, with resorptive changes affecting adjacent roots.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- The left mandibular molar region shows approximately 2.5 cm by 2 cm of buccal expansion with a continuous mucosal surface.\nCross-modal summary: Both modalities localize the abnormality to the left mandibular molar region: the panoramic image shows the intraosseous and root changes, while the clinical photograph shows the corresponding surface contour.\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. Clinical problem representation: The patient is a 19-year-old man with four months of painful left mandibular swelling. The history establishes the patient, site, symptom, and duration, but it does not by itself determine the histologic nature of the jaw lesion.\n\n2. OPG and RGB interpretation: The OPG shows a multilocular radiolucency and adjacent root resorption, whereas the RGB photograph shows buccal expansion at the same site. Their spatial agreement establishes the location and visible extent of the process, but these appearances are not sufficient to assign a histologic subtype.\n\n3. Diagnostic work-up: CBCT further documents mandibular bone destruction and molar-root resorption. More importantly, the specimen shows the cribriform, duct-like, and morular combination described in the paper for this entity; beta-catenin staining is treated as ancillary evidence, while faint BRAF immunostaining is not interpreted as a genetic result.\n\n4. Differential diagnosis: The paper identifies conventional ameloblastoma and adenomatoid odontogenic tumor as the main differentials. Conventional ameloblastoma shares an ameloblastomatous component, and AOT can share duct-like structures; however, the combined cribriform, duct-like, and morular pattern in this specimen provides the distinction emphasized by the source.\n\n5. Integration and diagnostic boundary: The diagnosis is reached because the case-specific histology matches the defining combination described in the report, with beta-catenin immunohistochemistry serving only as supporting information. OPG and RGB are useful for localization and extent, but the subtype is established by tissue morphology rather than by the images alone.\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- Conventional ameloblastoma: Supporting features—Ameloblastomatous epithelial component ; Multilocular mandibular radiolucency; Opposing features—The specimen contains the combined cribriform, duct-like, and morular pattern emphasized for the final entity; Status—less_likely\n- Adenomatoid odontogenic tumor (AOT): Supporting features—Duct-like structures are shared with the final entity; Opposing features—The remaining histologic architecture distinguishes the final entity from AOT; Status—less_likely\nLimitations: OPG and RGB cannot independently determine the histologic subtype. ; BRAF protein immunostaining does not establish BRAF mutation status.\n</Think>\n<Answer>\nAdenoid ameloblastoma. The histologic pattern establishes the diagnosis; beta-catenin immunohistochemistry is ancillary.\n</Answer>","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC13242668/12903_2026_8711_Fig2_HTML.jpg","name":"12903_2026_8711_Fig2_HTML.jpg","caption":"Segmented panoramic view showing multilocular radiolucency in the left side of the mandible related to molar teeth and causing root resorption","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"f1ae01c31da0ddf02f108f076a47021e4ec9b747935bbffd300adf645962eaf0","width":646,"height":471},{"src":"assets/PMC13242668/12903_2026_8711_Fig1_HTML.jpg","name":"12903_2026_8711_Fig1_HTML.jpg","caption":"A and (B) Clinical intraoral presentation of the studied case of adenoid ameloblastoma","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"364883db87b6b4a1e2401096b2d486984c8d8d0ea7155f5444688079ab0aa419","width":969,"height":330},{"src":"assets/PMC13242668/12903_2026_8711_Fig3_HTML.jpg","name":"12903_2026_8711_Fig3_HTML.jpg","caption":"Cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) of the skull demonstrating the extent of bone destruction in the mandible","types":["cbct","ct"],"sha256":"b010ba9b050b897f40c4b363d65b4a6e988c7d31f7396235d58bb96c74b611cd","width":646,"height":814}],"language":"en","label":"Earlier English sample","version":"qwen_cot_english_gold_samples_v1"}},{"id":"PMC12839816","title":"Dens Invaginatus-Mandibular Second Molar-Case Report.","category":"oral_maxillofacial_other","license":"cc by","authors":["Krystyna Pietrzycka","Natalia Lutomska","Cornelis H Pameijer","Monika Lukomska-Szymanska"],"journal":"Dentistry journal","year":"2026","citation":"Krystyna Pietrzycka, Natalia Lutomska, Cornelis H Pameijer, Monika Lukomska-Szymanska. Dens Invaginatus-Mandibular Second Molar-Case Report. Dentistry journal. 2026. doi: 10.3390/dj14010027.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland. This article is an open access article distributed under the terms and conditions of the Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) license.","copyright":["© 2026 by the authors."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12839816/","doi":"10.3390/dj14010027","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history|clinical_exam]: 24岁男性，主诉不可逆性牙髓炎；临床检查无冷热、电刺激反应，无叩痛及松动；3.7远中-舌侧牙周袋深8 mm\n- E2 [rgb]: 口内照显示3.7冠部异常：不对称延长、宽大、7个牙尖（图1）\n- E4 [clinical_exam]: 初诊根管探查发现：近中根双根管；远中根内见牙内陷结构紧贴远中壁，其前方存在两根管（一舌侧，一被DI冠阻塞）\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] (a) Preoperative Panoramic radiograph; (b) the magnified panel of tooth 3.7.\n- [radiograph] Tooth 3.7—Radiograph with five C-pilots size 10 (the first appointment).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral photographs of tooth 3.7: (left) occlusal and vestibular surfaces; (right) occlusal, lingual, and vestibular surfaces (first appointment).\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者3.7牙存在远中-舌侧8 mm深的牙周袋，提示该区域可能有解剖结构异常或病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内照显示3.7冠部不对称延长、宽大且有7个牙尖，表明牙齿形态发育异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 根管探查发现3.7远中根内存在牙内陷结构紧贴远中壁，其前方存在两根管（一舌侧，一被DI冠阻塞），进一步确认了牙内陷的存在。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据临床检查和影像学表现，3.7牙具有明显的解剖结构异常，结合根管探查结果，确诊为IIIb型牙内陷。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏直接提及具体牙内陷分型的证据；诊断基于观察到的特征与标准定义相匹配。\n","answer":"\n牙内陷（IIIb型），下颌第二磨牙（Dens invaginatus Type IIIb in mandibular second molar）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] (a) Preoperative Panoramic radiograph; (b) the magnified panel of tooth 3.7.\n- [radiograph] Tooth 3.7—Radiograph with five C-pilots size 10 (the first appointment).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral photographs of tooth 3.7: (left) occlusal and vestibular surfaces; (right) occlusal, lingual, and vestibular surfaces (first appointment).\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者3.7牙存在远中-舌侧8 mm深的牙周袋，提示该区域可能有解剖结构异常或病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内照显示3.7冠部不对称延长、宽大且有7个牙尖，表明牙齿形态发育异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 根管探查发现3.7远中根内存在牙内陷结构紧贴远中壁，其前方存在两根管（一舌侧，一被DI冠阻塞），进一步确认了牙内陷的存在。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据临床检查和影像学表现，3.7牙具有明显的解剖结构异常，结合根管探查结果，确诊为IIIb型牙内陷。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏直接提及具体牙内陷分型的证据；诊断基于观察到的特征与标准定义相匹配。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n牙内陷（IIIb型），下颌第二磨牙（Dens invaginatus Type IIIb in mandibular second molar）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12839816/dentistry-14-00027-g002.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00027-g002.jpg","caption":"(a) Preoperative Panoramic radiograph; (b) the magnified panel of tooth 3.7.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"2cf370bfc4b69047905d16fdf580e23efb97e8df1c72795a7b670458ea0dfb01","width":797,"height":294},{"src":"assets/PMC12839816/dentistry-14-00027-g001.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00027-g001.jpg","caption":"Intraoral photographs of tooth 3.7: (left) occlusal and vestibular surfaces; (right) occlusal, lingual, and vestibular surfaces (first appointment).","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"73e319fa2e51f899a191ec6a0ac1f7470448efc3a8f6132947c7cd3ef868a443","width":725,"height":272},{"src":"assets/PMC12839816/dentistry-14-00027-g003.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00027-g003.jpg","caption":"Tooth 3.7—Radiograph with five C-pilots size 10 (the first appointment).","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"24723d93f65e562b9b040bdd955c67ede85ee13217246064e551d5ccf0b6d0fc","width":788,"height":927}],"english":{"question":"A 24-year-old man with no significant medical history presents with irreversible pulpitis involving tooth 37. Microscopic and CBCT evaluation shows a crown-like calcified structure occupying the distal canal space, with two canals positioned in front of it and an associated distal-lingual inflammatory bone lesion. The structure extends through the root and communicates through the apical foramen. Using the accompanying panoramic radiograph and intraoral photograph, identify the developmental anomaly and its classification.","caption":"\nOPG:\n- Tooth 37 contains a tooth-like radiopaque structure within its distal root, with a radiolucent area along the distal root surface.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- Tooth 37 has a wide, asymmetrically elongated crown with seven cusps.\nCross-modal summary: The photograph demonstrates the abnormal external crown form, while the panoramic image demonstrates a second tooth-like structure within the distal root of the same tooth.\n","think":"\n1. Clinical problem representation: The patient is a 24-year-old man with irreversible pulpitis involving tooth 37. The task is to explain an abnormal crown and a complex internal root configuration rather than to infer a diagnosis from pulpitis alone.\n\n2. OPG and RGB interpretation: The RGB photograph shows a wide, asymmetric seven-cusp crown, and the OPG shows a tooth-like structure inside the distal root with adjacent radiolucency. The external and internal abnormalities involve the same tooth, so the images jointly define a developmental crown-root anomaly with associated periradicular change.\n\n3. Three-dimensional anatomy and classification: Microscopy and CBCT place the additional crown-like structure within the distal canal space and show how it obstructs the remaining endodontic anatomy. The reported extension through the root with apical-foramen communication matches the article's definition of the IIIb configuration.\n\n4. Differential diagnosis: Fusion and a supernumerary tooth are relevant because the crown is enlarged and the OPG can resemble an additional tooth; both are explicitly included in the article's differential list. CBCT instead localizes the structure inside tooth 37's distal root and canal system, favoring an invagination within one tooth over a separate adjacent tooth or union of two teeth.\n\n5. Integration and final diagnosis: The decisive sequence is an abnormal crown, a tooth-like structure invaginated into the distal root/canal system, and extension to the apical foramen. The first two findings establish the anomaly, while the apical communication assigns the IIIb class; CBCT is necessary because OPG and RGB do not fully resolve the canal pathway.\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- Fusion: Supporting features—An enlarged, unusual crown can mimic union of dental structures; Opposing features—CBCT localizes the additional structure within the distal root and canal system of tooth 37; Status—less_likely\n- Supernumerary tooth: Supporting features—The OPG initially resembles an additional tooth; Opposing features—The structure is contained within the distal root/canal anatomy rather than documented as a separate tooth; Status—less_likely\nLimitations: OPG and RGB demonstrate the external and internal abnormality but cannot fully map the canal system. ; The IIIb classification depends on the three-dimensional course and apical communication shown by CBCT.\n","answer":"\nDens invaginatus, Oehlers Type IIIb, involving mandibular tooth 37 (Dens invaginatus Type IIIb in mandibular second molar). The internal invagination establishes the anomaly, and apical-foramen communication establishes Type IIIb.\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- Tooth 37 contains a tooth-like radiopaque structure within its distal root, with a radiolucent area along the distal root surface.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- Tooth 37 has a wide, asymmetrically elongated crown with seven cusps.\nCross-modal summary: The photograph demonstrates the abnormal external crown form, while the panoramic image demonstrates a second tooth-like structure within the distal root of the same tooth.\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. Clinical problem representation: The patient is a 24-year-old man with irreversible pulpitis involving tooth 37. The task is to explain an abnormal crown and a complex internal root configuration rather than to infer a diagnosis from pulpitis alone.\n\n2. OPG and RGB interpretation: The RGB photograph shows a wide, asymmetric seven-cusp crown, and the OPG shows a tooth-like structure inside the distal root with adjacent radiolucency. The external and internal abnormalities involve the same tooth, so the images jointly define a developmental crown-root anomaly with associated periradicular change.\n\n3. Three-dimensional anatomy and classification: Microscopy and CBCT place the additional crown-like structure within the distal canal space and show how it obstructs the remaining endodontic anatomy. The reported extension through the root with apical-foramen communication matches the article's definition of the IIIb configuration.\n\n4. Differential diagnosis: Fusion and a supernumerary tooth are relevant because the crown is enlarged and the OPG can resemble an additional tooth; both are explicitly included in the article's differential list. CBCT instead localizes the structure inside tooth 37's distal root and canal system, favoring an invagination within one tooth over a separate adjacent tooth or union of two teeth.\n\n5. Integration and final diagnosis: The decisive sequence is an abnormal crown, a tooth-like structure invaginated into the distal root/canal system, and extension to the apical foramen. The first two findings establish the anomaly, while the apical communication assigns the IIIb class; CBCT is necessary because OPG and RGB do not fully resolve the canal pathway.\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- Fusion: Supporting features—An enlarged, unusual crown can mimic union of dental structures; Opposing features—CBCT localizes the additional structure within the distal root and canal system of tooth 37; Status—less_likely\n- Supernumerary tooth: Supporting features—The OPG initially resembles an additional tooth; Opposing features—The structure is contained within the distal root/canal anatomy rather than documented as a separate tooth; Status—less_likely\nLimitations: OPG and RGB demonstrate the external and internal abnormality but cannot fully map the canal system. ; The IIIb classification depends on the three-dimensional course and apical communication shown by CBCT.\n</Think>\n<Answer>\nDens invaginatus, Oehlers Type IIIb, involving mandibular tooth 37 (Dens invaginatus Type IIIb in mandibular second molar). The internal invagination establishes the anomaly, and apical-foramen communication establishes Type IIIb.\n</Answer>","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12839816/dentistry-14-00027-g002.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00027-g002.jpg","caption":"(a) Preoperative Panoramic radiograph; (b) the magnified panel of tooth 3.7.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"2cf370bfc4b69047905d16fdf580e23efb97e8df1c72795a7b670458ea0dfb01","width":797,"height":294},{"src":"assets/PMC12839816/dentistry-14-00027-g001.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00027-g001.jpg","caption":"Intraoral photographs of tooth 3.7: (left) occlusal and vestibular surfaces; (right) occlusal, lingual, and vestibular surfaces (first appointment).","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"73e319fa2e51f899a191ec6a0ac1f7470448efc3a8f6132947c7cd3ef868a443","width":725,"height":272},{"src":"assets/PMC12839816/dentistry-14-00027-g003.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00027-g003.jpg","caption":"Tooth 3.7—Radiograph with five C-pilots size 10 (the first appointment).","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"24723d93f65e562b9b040bdd955c67ede85ee13217246064e551d5ccf0b6d0fc","width":788,"height":927}],"language":"en","label":"Earlier English sample","version":"qwen_cot_english_gold_samples_v1"}},{"id":"PMC12939999","title":"Impacted Mandibular Third Molar Migration in the Presence of Idiopathic Osteosclerosis: A Rare Case Report.","category":"developmental_eruption","license":"cc by","authors":["Jure Martinić","Petra Stazić Kunčić","Tanja Gović","Ante Pojatina","Ante Mihovilović","Daniel Jerković"],"journal":"Dentistry journal","year":"2026","citation":"Jure Martinić, Petra Stazić Kunčić, Tanja Gović, Ante Pojatina, Ante Mihovilović, Daniel Jerković. Impacted Mandibular Third Molar Migration in the Presence of Idiopathic Osteosclerosis: A Rare Case Report. Dentistry journal. 2026. doi: 10.3390/dj14020104.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland. This article is an open access article distributed under the terms and conditions of the Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) license.","copyright":["© 2026 by the authors."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12939999/","doi":"10.3390/dj14020104","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 30岁女性，因右下唇及颏部麻木就诊；否认疼痛、肿胀、冠周炎；无系统病史或外伤史\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查：右侧下颌后区黏膜完整，无炎症或感染征象；47远中探诊见深牙周袋\n- E3 [rgb]: 口内照片（图1）显示右侧下颌后区无可见肿胀或炎症\n- E4 [clinical_exam]: 术前神经感觉检查：右侧下唇及颏部触觉与针刺觉减退，较对侧明显\n- E5 [opg]: 2022年4月OPG：右下颌第三磨牙（48）垂直阻生，距下牙槽神经管安全距离；其远中见小片边界清高密度影\n- E6 [opg]: 2025年6月OPG：48阻生深度增加，远中高密度影范围扩大（图2a,b）\n- E7 [other_imaging]: CBCT显示：48深位阻生，牙冠紧贴下牙槽神经管上壁；47远中根与48牙冠间见广泛骨性通道；48远中见大片均匀高密度影，延伸至下颌升支，边界清、无膨胀、皮质完整\n- E8 [other_imaging]: 影像特征排除恶性：边界清、非膨胀性、均质密度、皮质完整、无 periosteal reaction 或骨破坏\n- E9 [clinical_exam]: 临床无快速生长、疼痛或全身症状，支持良性病变\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [radiograph] Radiographic comparison of the condition from three years ago (April 2022) (a) and the current state (June 2025) (b), showing a difference in the depth of impaction of tooth 48 and the size of the bony lesion.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral view of the posterior right mandibular region showing no visible signs of swelling or inflammation.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者为30岁女性，因右下唇及颏部麻木就诊，否认疼痛、肿胀、冠周炎；无系统病史或外伤史。 诊断意义：支持特发性骨硬化症的临床表现\n\n2. 术前神经感觉检查显示右侧下唇及颏部触觉与针刺觉减退，较对侧明显。 诊断意义：支持下颌第三磨牙迁移可能引起的神经症状\n\n3. CBCT显示48深位阻生，牙冠紧贴下牙槽神经管上壁；47远中根与48牙冠间见广泛骨性通道；48远中见大片均匀高密度影，延伸至下颌升支，边界清、无膨胀、皮质完整。 诊断意义：支持特发性骨硬化症伴下颌第三磨牙迁移的影像学特征\n\n4. 影像特征排除恶性：边界清、非膨胀性、均质密度、皮质完整、无periosteal reaction 或骨破坏；临床无快速生长、疼痛或全身症状，支持良性病变。 诊断意义：排除恶性病变，支持良性病变如特发性骨硬化症\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床症状（E1, E4）、影像学特征（E7）以及良性的判断依据（E8, E9），支持特发性骨硬化症伴下颌第三磨牙迁移的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无法通过现有证据完全排除其他可能引起类似影像学改变的良性病变\n","answer":"\n特发性骨硬化症伴下颌第三磨牙迁移（Idiopathic osteosclerosis with migration of impacted mandibular third molar）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [radiograph] Radiographic comparison of the condition from three years ago (April 2022) (a) and the current state (June 2025) (b), showing a difference in the depth of impaction of tooth 48 and the size of the bony lesion.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral view of the posterior right mandibular region showing no visible signs of swelling or inflammation.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者为30岁女性，因右下唇及颏部麻木就诊，否认疼痛、肿胀、冠周炎；无系统病史或外伤史。 诊断意义：支持特发性骨硬化症的临床表现\n\n2. 术前神经感觉检查显示右侧下唇及颏部触觉与针刺觉减退，较对侧明显。 诊断意义：支持下颌第三磨牙迁移可能引起的神经症状\n\n3. CBCT显示48深位阻生，牙冠紧贴下牙槽神经管上壁；47远中根与48牙冠间见广泛骨性通道；48远中见大片均匀高密度影，延伸至下颌升支，边界清、无膨胀、皮质完整。 诊断意义：支持特发性骨硬化症伴下颌第三磨牙迁移的影像学特征\n\n4. 影像特征排除恶性：边界清、非膨胀性、均质密度、皮质完整、无periosteal reaction 或骨破坏；临床无快速生长、疼痛或全身症状，支持良性病变。 诊断意义：排除恶性病变，支持良性病变如特发性骨硬化症\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床症状（E1, E4）、影像学特征（E7）以及良性的判断依据（E8, E9），支持特发性骨硬化症伴下颌第三磨牙迁移的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无法通过现有证据完全排除其他可能引起类似影像学改变的良性病变\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n特发性骨硬化症伴下颌第三磨牙迁移（Idiopathic osteosclerosis with migration of impacted mandibular third molar）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12939999/dentistry-14-00104-g002.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00104-g002.jpg","caption":"Radiographic comparison of the condition from three years ago (April 2022) (a) and the current state (June 2025) (b), showing a difference in the depth of impaction of tooth 48 and the size of the bony lesion.","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"f69d29523f27bdf9fe3fe2d29a4cba67ec1ef306c041bb5a144841bbceb68bf2","width":730,"height":235},{"src":"assets/PMC12939999/dentistry-14-00104-g001.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00104-g001.jpg","caption":"Intraoral view of the posterior right mandibular region showing no visible signs of swelling or inflammation.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"48aa84650fb7d49a8e7d882739b304f1bf2ded63319b9d09512c5524b2337d25","width":667,"height":515}],"english":{"question":"A 30-year-old woman is referred after developing numbness of the right lower lip and chin. CBCT shows tooth 48 in direct contact with the superior border of the inferior alveolar canal and a homogeneous cortical-density area with intact margins, no expansion, and no radiolucent halo. Bone biopsy shows dense mature lamellar bone with minimal osteocyte lacunae and no inflammatory infiltrate, necrosis, or cellular atypia. Using the intraoral photograph and serial panoramic images, explain the diagnostic reasoning and provide the final diagnosis.","caption":"\nOPG:\n- The earlier panoramic image shows tooth 48 in a more superficial vertical position with a small distal radiopaque focus; the later image shows a larger radiopaque zone and a deeper tooth position.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- The posterior right mandibular region shows no visible facial asymmetry, swelling, or surface inflammatory change.\nCross-modal summary: The clinical photograph is externally subtle, whereas serial panoramic imaging demonstrates interval change in both the radiopaque area and the position of tooth 48.\n","think":"\n1. Clinical problem representation: The patient presents with right lower-lip and chin numbness, making the relationship between the posterior mandibular process and the inferior alveolar canal clinically important. The lack of visible swelling does not resolve the diagnosis because the key changes are intraosseous and temporal.\n\n2. Serial OPG and RGB interpretation: The earlier OPG shows a small, well-defined radiopaque focus distal to tooth 48, whereas the later OPG shows enlargement of the opacity and a deeper tooth position. This documents a temporal and spatial association; it does not by itself prove that the bone focus actively displaced the tooth.\n\n3. CBCT and tissue correlation: CBCT shows direct contact between tooth 48 and the superior border of the inferior alveolar canal and characterizes the bone focus as homogeneous, cortical-density, non-expansile, and without a radiolucent halo. Biopsy then shows dense mature lamellar bone without inflammatory infiltrate, necrosis, or atypia, providing tissue-level confirmation of a benign sclerotic process.\n\n4. Differential diagnosis: Condensing osteitis is less likely because the source associates it with a non-vital tooth or chronic infection and often an ill-defined opacity, while this case lacks inflammatory histology. Aggressive sclerotic disease such as osteosarcoma or metastatic carcinoma is also less likely because CBCT lacks expansion or periosteal reaction and biopsy lacks atypia; histology, rather than the negative imaging features alone, provides the decisive boundary.\n\n5. Integration and diagnostic boundary: The homogeneous non-expansile radiopaque focus and dense mature lamellar bone together establish idiopathic osteosclerosis, while the serial OPGs document concurrent deepening of tooth 48 toward the mandibular canal. The case supports an association between the sclerotic focus and tooth movement, but the images do not prove an active causal force; the final diagnosis combines the confirmed bone lesion with the observed migration.\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- Condensing osteitis: Supporting features—A localized radiopaque mandibular process can be inflammatory; Opposing features—No inflammatory infiltrate ; The opacity is homogeneous and well defined rather than an ill-defined reactive opacity; Status—less_likely\n- Aggressive or malignant sclerotic lesion: Supporting features—Paresthesia and interval change require exclusion of serious disease; Opposing features—No expansion or periosteal reaction ; Biopsy shows mature lamellar bone without atypia or necrosis; Status—less_likely\nLimitations: Serial association does not by itself establish that the sclerotic focus actively caused tooth displacement. ; Histopathology is required because several benign, inflammatory, and malignant jaw lesions can be radiopaque.\n","answer":"\nIdiopathic osteosclerosis associated with migration of tooth 48 (Idiopathic osteosclerosis with migration of impacted mandibular third molar). Histology confirms idiopathic osteosclerosis; serial panoramic imaging documents the associated change in tooth position.\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- The earlier panoramic image shows tooth 48 in a more superficial vertical position with a small distal radiopaque focus; the later image shows a larger radiopaque zone and a deeper tooth position.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- The posterior right mandibular region shows no visible facial asymmetry, swelling, or surface inflammatory change.\nCross-modal summary: The clinical photograph is externally subtle, whereas serial panoramic imaging demonstrates interval change in both the radiopaque area and the position of tooth 48.\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. Clinical problem representation: The patient presents with right lower-lip and chin numbness, making the relationship between the posterior mandibular process and the inferior alveolar canal clinically important. The lack of visible swelling does not resolve the diagnosis because the key changes are intraosseous and temporal.\n\n2. Serial OPG and RGB interpretation: The earlier OPG shows a small, well-defined radiopaque focus distal to tooth 48, whereas the later OPG shows enlargement of the opacity and a deeper tooth position. This documents a temporal and spatial association; it does not by itself prove that the bone focus actively displaced the tooth.\n\n3. CBCT and tissue correlation: CBCT shows direct contact between tooth 48 and the superior border of the inferior alveolar canal and characterizes the bone focus as homogeneous, cortical-density, non-expansile, and without a radiolucent halo. Biopsy then shows dense mature lamellar bone without inflammatory infiltrate, necrosis, or atypia, providing tissue-level confirmation of a benign sclerotic process.\n\n4. Differential diagnosis: Condensing osteitis is less likely because the source associates it with a non-vital tooth or chronic infection and often an ill-defined opacity, while this case lacks inflammatory histology. Aggressive sclerotic disease such as osteosarcoma or metastatic carcinoma is also less likely because CBCT lacks expansion or periosteal reaction and biopsy lacks atypia; histology, rather than the negative imaging features alone, provides the decisive boundary.\n\n5. Integration and diagnostic boundary: The homogeneous non-expansile radiopaque focus and dense mature lamellar bone together establish idiopathic osteosclerosis, while the serial OPGs document concurrent deepening of tooth 48 toward the mandibular canal. The case supports an association between the sclerotic focus and tooth movement, but the images do not prove an active causal force; the final diagnosis combines the confirmed bone lesion with the observed migration.\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- Condensing osteitis: Supporting features—A localized radiopaque mandibular process can be inflammatory; Opposing features—No inflammatory infiltrate ; The opacity is homogeneous and well defined rather than an ill-defined reactive opacity; Status—less_likely\n- Aggressive or malignant sclerotic lesion: Supporting features—Paresthesia and interval change require exclusion of serious disease; Opposing features—No expansion or periosteal reaction ; Biopsy shows mature lamellar bone without atypia or necrosis; Status—less_likely\nLimitations: Serial association does not by itself establish that the sclerotic focus actively caused tooth displacement. ; Histopathology is required because several benign, inflammatory, and malignant jaw lesions can be radiopaque.\n</Think>\n<Answer>\nIdiopathic osteosclerosis associated with migration of tooth 48 (Idiopathic osteosclerosis with migration of impacted mandibular third molar). Histology confirms idiopathic osteosclerosis; serial panoramic imaging documents the associated change in tooth position.\n</Answer>","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12939999/dentistry-14-00104-g005.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00104-g005.jpg","caption":"Six-month postoperative panoramic radiograph showing normal bone healing without radiographic evidence of lesion progression.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"b3de400cb9cfd60cf9309a8526e8f533cec408d177610c380e4a80e75cf67d72","width":746,"height":397},{"src":"assets/PMC12939999/dentistry-14-00104-g001.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00104-g001.jpg","caption":"Intraoral view of the posterior right mandibular region showing no visible signs of swelling or inflammation.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"48aa84650fb7d49a8e7d882739b304f1bf2ded63319b9d09512c5524b2337d25","width":667,"height":515},{"src":"assets/PMC12939999/dentistry-14-00104-g002.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00104-g002.jpg","caption":"Radiographic comparison of the condition from three years ago (April 2022) (a) and the current state (June 2025) (b), showing a difference in the depth of impaction of tooth 48 and the size of the bony lesion.","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"f69d29523f27bdf9fe3fe2d29a4cba67ec1ef306c041bb5a144841bbceb68bf2","width":730,"height":235}],"language":"en","label":"Earlier English sample","version":"qwen_cot_english_gold_samples_v1"}},{"id":"PMC13178942","title":"Central Giant Cell Granuloma Misdiagnosed as Mandibular Osteomyelitis: A Case Report.","category":"infection","license":"cc by","authors":["Emmanouil Chatzipetros","Zafeiroula Yfanti","Konstantina-Eleni Alexiou","Christos Angelopoulos"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2026","citation":"Emmanouil Chatzipetros, Zafeiroula Yfanti, Konstantina-Eleni Alexiou, Christos Angelopoulos. Central Giant Cell Granuloma Misdiagnosed as Mandibular Osteomyelitis: A Case Report. Cureus. 2026. doi: 10.7759/cureus.107107.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2026, Chatzipetros et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13178942/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.107107","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [demographics]: 60岁男性，无显著系统病史\n- E4 [opg]: 根尖片显示拔牙位点存留牙根断根（红箭），提示局部刺激与可能感染\n- E5 [opg]: 全景片显示左下颌第一磨牙区一透射影病变（黄箭）\n- E6 [other_imaging]: CBCT显示溶骨性病变，边界不清，伴皮质板侵蚀与破坏（蓝/绿/黄/红箭）\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [cbct/ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical and radiographic findings of the lesion.(A) Periapical radiograph showing a retained root fragment (red arrow) at the extraction site, suggestive of local irritation and possible infection. (B) Clinical image showing a well-defined, red, granular mass with elastic consistency and a pedunculated base located on the gingival tissue adjacent to the extraction site (blue arrow). (C) Periapical radiograph of the left mandibular first molar region (green arrow). (D) Panoramic radiograph demonstrating a radiolucent lesion in the left mandibular first molar region (yellow arrow). (E) Cone-beam computed tomography (CBCT) panoramic reconstruction showing an osteolytic lesion with ill-defined borders and cortical plate erosion (blue arrow). (F) Axial CBCT images of the lesion (green arrows). (G) Cross-sectional CBCT images (yellow arrows). (H) Three-dimensional CBCT reconstruction highlighting the lesion (red arrow).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [cbct/ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical and radiographic findings of the lesion.(A) Periapical radiograph showing a retained root fragment (red arrow) at the extraction site, suggestive of local irritation and possible infection. (B) Clinical image showing a well-defined, red, granular mass with elastic consistency and a pedunculated base located on the gingival tissue adjacent to the extraction site (blue arrow). (C) Periapical radiograph of the left mandibular first molar region (green arrow). (D) Panoramic radiograph demonstrating a radiolucent lesion in the left mandibular first molar region (yellow arrow). (E) Cone-beam computed tomography (CBCT) panoramic reconstruction showing an osteolytic lesion with ill-defined borders and cortical plate erosion (blue arrow). (F) Axial CBCT images of the lesion (green arrows). (G) Cross-sectional CBCT images (yellow arrows). (H) Three-dimensional CBCT reconstruction highlighting the lesion (red arrow).\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者为60岁男性，无显著系统病史。 诊断意义：支持最终诊断，但单项证据的特异性有限\n\n2. 根尖片显示拔牙位点存留牙根断根，提示局部刺激与可能感染。 诊断意义：支持最终诊断，但单项证据的特异性有限\n\n3. 全景片显示左下颌第一磨牙区存在一透射影病变。 诊断意义：支持最终诊断，但单项证据的特异性有限\n\n4. CBCT进一步证实该区域存在溶骨性病变，边界不清，伴有皮质板侵蚀与破坏。 诊断意义：支持最终诊断，但单项证据的特异性有限\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据影像学检查结果，发现左下颌第一磨牙区存在溶骨性病变，伴有皮质板侵蚀与破坏，支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有证据不能完全排除其他类似表现的疾病\n","answer":"\n中央性巨细胞肉芽肿（central giant cell granuloma (CGCG)）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [cbct/ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical and radiographic findings of the lesion.(A) Periapical radiograph showing a retained root fragment (red arrow) at the extraction site, suggestive of local irritation and possible infection. (B) Clinical image showing a well-defined, red, granular mass with elastic consistency and a pedunculated base located on the gingival tissue adjacent to the extraction site (blue arrow). (C) Periapical radiograph of the left mandibular first molar region (green arrow). (D) Panoramic radiograph demonstrating a radiolucent lesion in the left mandibular first molar region (yellow arrow). (E) Cone-beam computed tomography (CBCT) panoramic reconstruction showing an osteolytic lesion with ill-defined borders and cortical plate erosion (blue arrow). (F) Axial CBCT images of the lesion (green arrows). (G) Cross-sectional CBCT images (yellow arrows). (H) Three-dimensional CBCT reconstruction highlighting the lesion (red arrow).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [cbct/ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical and radiographic findings of the lesion.(A) Periapical radiograph showing a retained root fragment (red arrow) at the extraction site, suggestive of local irritation and possible infection. (B) Clinical image showing a well-defined, red, granular mass with elastic consistency and a pedunculated base located on the gingival tissue adjacent to the extraction site (blue arrow). (C) Periapical radiograph of the left mandibular first molar region (green arrow). (D) Panoramic radiograph demonstrating a radiolucent lesion in the left mandibular first molar region (yellow arrow). (E) Cone-beam computed tomography (CBCT) panoramic reconstruction showing an osteolytic lesion with ill-defined borders and cortical plate erosion (blue arrow). (F) Axial CBCT images of the lesion (green arrows). (G) Cross-sectional CBCT images (yellow arrows). (H) Three-dimensional CBCT reconstruction highlighting the lesion (red arrow).\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者为60岁男性，无显著系统病史。 诊断意义：支持最终诊断，但单项证据的特异性有限\n\n2. 根尖片显示拔牙位点存留牙根断根，提示局部刺激与可能感染。 诊断意义：支持最终诊断，但单项证据的特异性有限\n\n3. 全景片显示左下颌第一磨牙区存在一透射影病变。 诊断意义：支持最终诊断，但单项证据的特异性有限\n\n4. CBCT进一步证实该区域存在溶骨性病变，边界不清，伴有皮质板侵蚀与破坏。 诊断意义：支持最终诊断，但单项证据的特异性有限\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据影像学检查结果，发现左下颌第一磨牙区存在溶骨性病变，伴有皮质板侵蚀与破坏，支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有证据不能完全排除其他类似表现的疾病\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n中央性巨细胞肉芽肿（central giant cell granuloma (CGCG)）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC13178942/cureus-0018-00000107107-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0018-00000107107-i01.jpg","caption":"Clinical and radiographic findings of the lesion.(A) Periapical radiograph showing a retained root fragment (red arrow) at the extraction site, suggestive of local irritation and possible infection. (B) Clinical image showing a well-defined, red, granular mass with elastic consistency and a pedunculated base located on the gingival tissue adjacent to the extraction site (blue arrow). (C) Periapical radiograph of the left mandibular first molar region (green arrow). (D) Panoramic radiograph demonstrating a radiolucent lesion in the left mandibular first molar region (yellow arrow). (E) Cone-beam computed tomography (CBCT) panoramic reconstruction showing an osteolytic lesion with ill-defined borders and cortical plate erosion (blue arrow). (F) Axial CBCT images of the lesion (green arrows). (G) Cross-sectional CBCT images (yellow arrows). (H) Three-dimensional CBCT reconstruction highlighting the lesion (red arrow).","types":["cbct","ct","intraoral_photo","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"c545b5c973802cccd68db71fa890103df3a6792babf8e51b95bfbb83b8f46a64","width":750,"height":361}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC13022747","title":"Intraosseous Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma Mimicking a Periapical Lesion.","category":"endodontic_periapical","license":"cc by","authors":["Laryssa Thainá Mello Queiroz Cunha","Joab Cabral Ramos","Isabel Schausltz Pereira Faustino","Silvia Maria Paparotto Lopes","Alan Roger Santos‐Silva","Pablo Agustin Vargas","Márcio Ajudarte Lopes"],"journal":"Special care in dentistry : official publication of the American Association of Hospital Dentists, the Academy of Dentistry for the Handicapped, and the American Society for Geriatric Dentistry","year":"2026","citation":"Laryssa Thainá Mello Queiroz Cunha, Joab Cabral Ramos, Isabel Schausltz Pereira Faustino, Silvia Maria Paparotto Lopes, Alan Roger Santos‐Silva, Pablo Agustin Vargas, Márcio Ajudarte Lopes. Intraosseous Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma Mimicking a Periapical Lesion. Special care in dentistry : official publication of the American Association of Hospital Dentists, the Academy of Dentistry for the Handicapped, and the American Society for Geriatric Dentistry. 2026. doi: 10.1111/scd.70162.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/This is an open access article under the terms of the http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ License, which permits use, distribution and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["© 2026 The Author(s). Special Care in Dentistry published by Special Care Dentistry Association and Wiley Periodicals LLC."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13022747/","doi":"10.1111/scd.70162","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 44岁男性，主诉上颌左侧侧切牙区持续性根尖病变，对根管治疗及牙周治疗无反应\n- E5 [laboratory]: 细针穿刺涂片见大量圆形大细胞伴频繁核分裂象，提示淋巴瘤；活检组织病理见纤维结缔组织内密集单核淋巴细胞浸润\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Initial clinical and radiographic aspects. (A‐B) Initial clinical examination revealing mild facial asymmetry due to a localized swelling in the upper left lip region (yellow arrow). (C) Intraoral swelling in the anterior region of the left maxilla, resulting in a reduced maxillary vestibular fornix, with a purplish hue and a telangiectatic surface. A decrease in the interdental papilla is observed in the interproximal region between teeth lateral and central incisors (yellow arrow). (D) Swelling along the midline of the hard palate. (E) Periapical radiograph demonstrating a diffuse radiolucent area at the periapex of tooth #7. (F) Panoramic radiograph showing a poorly defined radiolucent image in the periapical region of teeth. Tooth lateral incisor presents previous endodontic treatment. (G) Axial slice of computed tomography (CT) revealing an expansile hypodense lesion in the anterior maxillary region, associated with cortical bone disruption. (H) Coronal CT reconstruction demonstrating hypodensity in the left maxillary sinus and the inferior portion of the nasal cavity, associated with bone destruction. (I) Sagittal CT reconstruction showing satisfactory endodontic treatment of tooth lateral incisor, associated with bone destruction, cortical disruption, and root resorption.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Initial clinical and radiographic aspects. (A‐B) Initial clinical examination revealing mild facial asymmetry due to a localized swelling in the upper left lip region (yellow arrow). (C) Intraoral swelling in the anterior region of the left maxilla, resulting in a reduced maxillary vestibular fornix, with a purplish hue and a telangiectatic surface. A decrease in the interdental papilla is observed in the interproximal region between teeth lateral and central incisors (yellow arrow). (D) Swelling along the midline of the hard palate. (E) Periapical radiograph demonstrating a diffuse radiolucent area at the periapex of tooth #7. (F) Panoramic radiograph showing a poorly defined radiolucent image in the periapical region of teeth. Tooth lateral incisor presents previous endodontic treatment. (G) Axial slice of computed tomography (CT) revealing an expansile hypodense lesion in the anterior maxillary region, associated with cortical bone disruption. (H) Coronal CT reconstruction demonstrating hypodensity in the left maxillary sinus and the inferior portion of the nasal cavity, associated with bone destruction. (I) Sagittal CT reconstruction showing satisfactory endodontic treatment of tooth lateral incisor, associated with bone destruction, cortical disruption, and root resorption.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 44岁男性，主诉上颌左侧侧切牙区持续性根尖病变，对根管治疗及牙周治疗无反应，提示可能有非典型病理性变化。 诊断意义：支持进一步检查以排除恶性病变\n\n2. 细针穿刺涂片见大量圆形大细胞伴频繁核分裂象，提示淋巴瘤；活检组织病理见纤维结缔组织内密集单核淋巴细胞浸润，证实了存在恶性淋巴增生过程。 诊断意义：支持弥漫大B细胞非霍奇金淋巴瘤的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者口腔内出现对抗常规治疗无效的持续性病变，结合细针穿刺与组织活检结果，指向弥漫大B细胞非霍奇金淋巴瘤。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏具体免疫组化标记物或分子生物学特征来进一步确认淋巴瘤亚型\n","answer":"\n弥漫大B细胞非霍奇金淋巴瘤（Diffuse Large B-Cell Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Initial clinical and radiographic aspects. (A‐B) Initial clinical examination revealing mild facial asymmetry due to a localized swelling in the upper left lip region (yellow arrow). (C) Intraoral swelling in the anterior region of the left maxilla, resulting in a reduced maxillary vestibular fornix, with a purplish hue and a telangiectatic surface. A decrease in the interdental papilla is observed in the interproximal region between teeth lateral and central incisors (yellow arrow). (D) Swelling along the midline of the hard palate. (E) Periapical radiograph demonstrating a diffuse radiolucent area at the periapex of tooth #7. (F) Panoramic radiograph showing a poorly defined radiolucent image in the periapical region of teeth. Tooth lateral incisor presents previous endodontic treatment. (G) Axial slice of computed tomography (CT) revealing an expansile hypodense lesion in the anterior maxillary region, associated with cortical bone disruption. (H) Coronal CT reconstruction demonstrating hypodensity in the left maxillary sinus and the inferior portion of the nasal cavity, associated with bone destruction. (I) Sagittal CT reconstruction showing satisfactory endodontic treatment of tooth lateral incisor, associated with bone destruction, cortical disruption, and root resorption.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Initial clinical and radiographic aspects. (A‐B) Initial clinical examination revealing mild facial asymmetry due to a localized swelling in the upper left lip region (yellow arrow). (C) Intraoral swelling in the anterior region of the left maxilla, resulting in a reduced maxillary vestibular fornix, with a purplish hue and a telangiectatic surface. A decrease in the interdental papilla is observed in the interproximal region between teeth lateral and central incisors (yellow arrow). (D) Swelling along the midline of the hard palate. (E) Periapical radiograph demonstrating a diffuse radiolucent area at the periapex of tooth #7. (F) Panoramic radiograph showing a poorly defined radiolucent image in the periapical region of teeth. Tooth lateral incisor presents previous endodontic treatment. (G) Axial slice of computed tomography (CT) revealing an expansile hypodense lesion in the anterior maxillary region, associated with cortical bone disruption. (H) Coronal CT reconstruction demonstrating hypodensity in the left maxillary sinus and the inferior portion of the nasal cavity, associated with bone destruction. (I) Sagittal CT reconstruction showing satisfactory endodontic treatment of tooth lateral incisor, associated with bone destruction, cortical disruption, and root resorption.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 44岁男性，主诉上颌左侧侧切牙区持续性根尖病变，对根管治疗及牙周治疗无反应，提示可能有非典型病理性变化。 诊断意义：支持进一步检查以排除恶性病变\n\n2. 细针穿刺涂片见大量圆形大细胞伴频繁核分裂象，提示淋巴瘤；活检组织病理见纤维结缔组织内密集单核淋巴细胞浸润，证实了存在恶性淋巴增生过程。 诊断意义：支持弥漫大B细胞非霍奇金淋巴瘤的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者口腔内出现对抗常规治疗无效的持续性病变，结合细针穿刺与组织活检结果，指向弥漫大B细胞非霍奇金淋巴瘤。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏具体免疫组化标记物或分子生物学特征来进一步确认淋巴瘤亚型\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n弥漫大B细胞非霍奇金淋巴瘤（Diffuse Large B-Cell Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC13022747/SCD-46-0-g004.jpg","name":"SCD-46-0-g004.jpg","caption":"Initial clinical and radiographic aspects. (A‐B) Initial clinical examination revealing mild facial asymmetry due to a localized swelling in the upper left lip region (yellow arrow). (C) Intraoral swelling in the anterior region of the left maxilla, resulting in a reduced maxillary vestibular fornix, with a purplish hue and a telangiectatic surface. A decrease in the interdental papilla is observed in the interproximal region between teeth lateral and central incisors (yellow arrow). (D) Swelling along the midline of the hard palate. (E) Periapical radiograph demonstrating a diffuse radiolucent area at the periapex of tooth #7. (F) Panoramic radiograph showing a poorly defined radiolucent image in the periapical region of teeth. Tooth lateral incisor presents previous endodontic treatment. (G) Axial slice of computed tomography (CT) revealing an expansile hypodense lesion in the anterior maxillary region, associated with cortical bone disruption. (H) Coronal CT reconstruction demonstrating hypodensity in the left maxillary sinus and the inferior portion of the nasal cavity, associated with bone destruction. (I) Sagittal CT reconstruction showing satisfactory endodontic treatment of tooth lateral incisor, associated with bone destruction, cortical disruption, and root resorption.","types":["ct","intraoral_photo","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"e7ef51e9b4bc8775534071d4aaa7a05ad74c47f0c4d606c62d4cc5d4b948235a","width":600,"height":868}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12662774","title":"Craniofacial fibrous dysplasia: a challenge for general dental practitioners.","category":"orthodontic_craniofacial","license":"cc by","authors":["Manuel W H Man","Roshni Ruparelia","Jasleen K Batra","Krupti Denhard","Ulpee R Darbar"],"journal":"British dental journal","year":"2025","citation":"Manuel W H Man, Roshni Ruparelia, Jasleen K Batra, Krupti Denhard, Ulpee R Darbar. Craniofacial fibrous dysplasia: a challenge for general dental practitioners. British dental journal. 2025. doi: 10.1038/s41415-025-9010-y.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"Open Access. This article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, which permits use, sharing, adaptation, distribution and reproduction in any medium or format, as long as you give appropriate credit to the original author(s) and the source, provide a link to the Creative Commons licence, and indicate if changes were made. The images or other third party material in this article are included in the article's Creative Commons licence, unless indicated otherwise in a credit line to the material. If material is not included in the article's Creative Commons licence and your intended use is not permitted by statutory regulation or exceeds the permitted use, you will need to obtain permission directly from the copyright holder. To view a copy of this licence, visit http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0.© The Author(s) 2025.","copyright":["© The Author(s) 2025"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12662774/","doi":"10.1038/s41415-025-9010-y","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 28岁白人男性，主诉前牙外观差及松动致咀嚼困难\n- E4 [clinical_exam]: 口内见上下前牙区骨膨隆、附着龈萎缩、全口牙龈炎症明显，11、21牙III度松动，42牙II度松动，牙龈薄生物型\n- E5 [opg]: 曲面体层片示典型‘磨砂玻璃样’与混合斑驳影、未萌牙、牛牙症磨牙、短根、牙周膜间隙模糊、下牙槽神经管边界不清\n- E6 [other_imaging]: CBCT显示上下颌骨膨隆及尖牙阻生位置\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Case 1: orthopantomogram showing the typical ‘ground-glass' and mixed mottled appearance (indicated with arrows), unerupted teeth, taurodont molars, short roots and poorly defined lamina dura and inferior dental canal\n- [cbct/ct] Case 1: cone-beam computed tomography scan. (A, B) Axial views of the maxilla and mandible showing the bone expansion and the position of the impacted canine teeth. (C) Sagittal view of the anterior maxilla and mandible showing the bone expansion and the position of the impacted canine tooth\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] Case 1: extra-oral smiling appearance\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者主诉前牙外观差及松动致咀嚼困难，提示存在口腔颌面部问题。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查发现上下前牙区骨膨隆、附着龈萎缩、全口牙龈炎症明显，多颗牙齿松动，表明存在广泛的骨质病变影响到牙周健康。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 曲面体层片中典型‘磨砂玻璃样’与混合斑驳影等影像学特征，进一步指向纤维结构不良的可能性。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. CBCT显示的上下颌骨膨隆及尖牙阻生位置，补充了对病变范围的理解，有助于确定颅面纤维结构不良（多骨型）诊断。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的临床症状和影像学表现，考虑颅面纤维结构不良（多骨型）。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理结果直接证实纤维结构不良\n","answer":"\n颅面纤维结构不良（多骨型）（polyostotic craniofacial fibrous dysplasia）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Case 1: orthopantomogram showing the typical ‘ground-glass' and mixed mottled appearance (indicated with arrows), unerupted teeth, taurodont molars, short roots and poorly defined lamina dura and inferior dental canal\n- [cbct/ct] Case 1: cone-beam computed tomography scan. (A, B) Axial views of the maxilla and mandible showing the bone expansion and the position of the impacted canine teeth. (C) Sagittal view of the anterior maxilla and mandible showing the bone expansion and the position of the impacted canine tooth\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] Case 1: extra-oral smiling appearance\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者主诉前牙外观差及松动致咀嚼困难，提示存在口腔颌面部问题。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查发现上下前牙区骨膨隆、附着龈萎缩、全口牙龈炎症明显，多颗牙齿松动，表明存在广泛的骨质病变影响到牙周健康。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 曲面体层片中典型‘磨砂玻璃样’与混合斑驳影等影像学特征，进一步指向纤维结构不良的可能性。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. CBCT显示的上下颌骨膨隆及尖牙阻生位置，补充了对病变范围的理解，有助于确定颅面纤维结构不良（多骨型）诊断。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的临床症状和影像学表现，考虑颅面纤维结构不良（多骨型）。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理结果直接证实纤维结构不良\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n颅面纤维结构不良（多骨型）（polyostotic craniofacial fibrous dysplasia）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12662774/41415_2025_9010_Fig3_HTML.jpg","name":"41415_2025_9010_Fig3_HTML.jpg","caption":"Case 1: orthopantomogram showing the typical ‘ground-glass' and mixed mottled appearance (indicated with arrows), unerupted teeth, taurodont molars, short roots and poorly defined lamina dura and inferior dental canal","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"822c5e0605d3d39ab01f5c749080ef78043c5134cbdfdf959059bac6081cf2e8","width":754,"height":394},{"src":"assets/PMC12662774/41415_2025_9010_Fig1_HTML.jpg","name":"41415_2025_9010_Fig1_HTML.jpg","caption":"Case 1: extra-oral smiling appearance","types":["extraoral_photo"],"sha256":"614ca1cf1bddf95d35a2f9c1a97ab07c5bc11f619fd79804062dcce8baeabcf7","width":707,"height":399},{"src":"assets/PMC12662774/41415_2025_9010_Fig4_HTML.jpg","name":"41415_2025_9010_Fig4_HTML.jpg","caption":"Case 1: cone-beam computed tomography scan. (A, B) Axial views of the maxilla and mandible showing the bone expansion and the position of the impacted canine teeth. (C) Sagittal view of the anterior maxilla and mandible showing the bone expansion and the position of the impacted canine tooth","types":["cbct","ct"],"sha256":"7115241b309d000fd30a5d8dd5d9c0ff1f94f2d1730b7b27a75738356a866566","width":716,"height":163}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC11988701","title":"Metastatic Renal Cell Carcinoma Presenting a Maxillary Mucosal Lesion as a First Visible Sign of Disease: A Case Report and Review of Literature.","category":"mucosal_oral_lesion","license":"cc by","authors":["Umma Habiba","Abu Faem Mohammad Almas Chowdhury","Rafiz Ahmed","Saiyka S Chowdhury","Raihanul Ferdoush","Koki Ise","Harun ur Rashid","Zillur Rahman","Zen-ichi Tanei","Shinya Tanaka","Asad-Uz Zaman"],"journal":"Diagnostics (Basel, Switzerland)","year":"2025","citation":"Umma Habiba, Abu Faem Mohammad Almas Chowdhury, Rafiz Ahmed, Saiyka S Chowdhury, Raihanul Ferdoush, Koki Ise, Harun ur Rashid, Zillur Rahman, Zen-ichi Tanei, Shinya Tanaka, Asad-Uz Zaman. Metastatic Renal Cell Carcinoma Presenting a Maxillary Mucosal Lesion as a First Visible Sign of Disease: A Case Report and Review of Literature. Diagnostics (Basel, Switzerland). 2025. doi: 10.3390/diagnostics15070938.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland. This article is an open access article distributed under the terms and conditions of the Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).","copyright":["© 2025 by the authors."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11988701/","doi":"10.3390/diagnostics15070938","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E2 [history]: 既往有髋部与背部疼痛、血尿史\n- E3 [laboratory]: 严重贫血（Hb 5.5 g/dL）\n- E5 [opg]: 曲面断层片示12至17牙间边界不清的透射影，提示骨溶解\n- E6 [rgb]: 口内照片显示右上颌双叶状结节（图1A）\n- E7 [other_imaging]: CT示右上颌窦软组织病变伴异质性强化及骨壁破坏\n- E8 [clinical_exam]: 初诊临床诊断为化脓性肉芽肿\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical, radiographical, and CT scans of the oral and maxillofacial region. (A) Intra-oral view of the initial lesion. A double lobe nodule is observed in the right maxilla. (B) A panoramic radiograph displays a radiolucent lesion with an indistinct margin, suggesting osteolysis between teeth 12 and 17. (C) A CT scan of the maxillofacial area shows a soft tissue lesion in the right maxillary sinus with heterogeneous enhancement and destruction of the bony wall.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical, radiographical, and CT scans of the oral and maxillofacial region. (A) Intra-oral view of the initial lesion. A double lobe nodule is observed in the right maxilla. (B) A panoramic radiograph displays a radiolucent lesion with an indistinct margin, suggesting osteolysis between teeth 12 and 17. (C) A CT scan of the maxillofacial area shows a soft tissue lesion in the right maxillary sinus with heterogeneous enhancement and destruction of the bony wall.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 口内照片显示右上颌双叶状结节。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. CT示右上颌窦软组织病变伴异质性强化及骨壁破坏。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 曲面断层片示12至17牙间边界不清的透射影，提示骨溶解。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 既往有髋部与背部疼痛、血尿史。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床表现（右上颌双叶状结节）、影像学特征（CT示软组织病变伴骨壁破坏、曲面断层片示骨溶解）以及病史（髋部与背部疼痛、血尿），支持转移性肾透明细胞癌（口腔颌面部）的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不能特异性排除其他可能引起类似症状和影像学表现的疾病。\n","answer":"\n转移性肾透明细胞癌（口腔颌面部）（Metastatic renal clear-cell carcinoma (ccRCC) to the maxillary mucosa）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical, radiographical, and CT scans of the oral and maxillofacial region. (A) Intra-oral view of the initial lesion. A double lobe nodule is observed in the right maxilla. (B) A panoramic radiograph displays a radiolucent lesion with an indistinct margin, suggesting osteolysis between teeth 12 and 17. (C) A CT scan of the maxillofacial area shows a soft tissue lesion in the right maxillary sinus with heterogeneous enhancement and destruction of the bony wall.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [ct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical, radiographical, and CT scans of the oral and maxillofacial region. (A) Intra-oral view of the initial lesion. A double lobe nodule is observed in the right maxilla. (B) A panoramic radiograph displays a radiolucent lesion with an indistinct margin, suggesting osteolysis between teeth 12 and 17. (C) A CT scan of the maxillofacial area shows a soft tissue lesion in the right maxillary sinus with heterogeneous enhancement and destruction of the bony wall.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 口内照片显示右上颌双叶状结节。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. CT示右上颌窦软组织病变伴异质性强化及骨壁破坏。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 曲面断层片示12至17牙间边界不清的透射影，提示骨溶解。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 既往有髋部与背部疼痛、血尿史。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床表现（右上颌双叶状结节）、影像学特征（CT示软组织病变伴骨壁破坏、曲面断层片示骨溶解）以及病史（髋部与背部疼痛、血尿），支持转移性肾透明细胞癌（口腔颌面部）的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不能特异性排除其他可能引起类似症状和影像学表现的疾病。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n转移性肾透明细胞癌（口腔颌面部）（Metastatic renal clear-cell carcinoma (ccRCC) to the maxillary mucosa）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC11988701/diagnostics-15-00938-g001.jpg","name":"diagnostics-15-00938-g001.jpg","caption":"Clinical, radiographical, and CT scans of the oral and maxillofacial region. (A) Intra-oral view of the initial lesion. A double lobe nodule is observed in the right maxilla. (B) A panoramic radiograph displays a radiolucent lesion with an indistinct margin, suggesting osteolysis between teeth 12 and 17. (C) A CT scan of the maxillofacial area shows a soft tissue lesion in the right maxillary sinus with heterogeneous enhancement and destruction of the bony wall.","types":["ct","intraoral_photo","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"bec08b66ffdd442e24f4eeab331d1e88a3bdfeb60a90a6e05de4630c7bf100e9","width":737,"height":157}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC9469393","title":"Mucoepidermoid Carcinoma of Minor Salivary Gland in a Patient with Asymptomatic Palatal Swelling - A Case Report.","category":"salivary","license":"cc by-nc-sa","authors":["Nada Ahmad Allan Al-Rabai","Khalil Ibrahim Assiri","Mohammed Ibrahim Al Almai","N.C Sandeepa","Muhammed Ajmal","Darshan Devang Divakar"],"journal":"Journal of pharmacy & bioallied sciences","year":"2022","citation":"Nada Ahmad Allan Al-Rabai, Khalil Ibrahim Assiri, Mohammed Ibrahim Al Almai, N.C Sandeepa, Muhammed Ajmal, Darshan Devang Divakar. Mucoepidermoid Carcinoma of Minor Salivary Gland in a Patient with Asymptomatic Palatal Swelling - A Case Report. Journal of pharmacy & bioallied sciences. 2022. doi: 10.4103/jpbs.jpbs_137_22.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/This is an open access journal, and articles are distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 License, which allows others to remix, tweak, and build upon the work non-commercially, as long as appropriate credit is given and the new creations are licensed under the identical terms.","copyright":["Copyright: © 2022 Journal of Pharmacy and Bioallied Sciences"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9469393/","doi":"10.4103/jpbs.jpbs_137_22","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 25岁女性，主诉左下后牙区疼痛1个月，伴冷热刺激痛，服止痛药可缓解\n- E3 [symptom]: 肿物为患者自述突发出现、1个月内大小稳定、完全无症状\n- E4 [opg]: 全景片示36、46牙根尖病变，余无异常；26–28牙区根尖片及上颌咬合片未见明显骨改变\n- E5 [laboratory]: 细针穿刺抽出淡血性液体，抽吸后肿物塌陷，1小时内复充盈呈穹隆状；细胞学初诊为多形性腺瘤\n- E6 [other_imaging]: CT显示无骨侵犯\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] (a) Solitary swelling at the left posterior maxilla. (b) Panoramic radiograph showing periapical lesion in relation to teeth number 36 and 46 with no other changes. (c) Intraoral periapical radiograph in relation to teeth number 26–28. (d) Occlusal radiograph of maxilla\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] (a) Solitary swelling at the left posterior maxilla. (b) Panoramic radiograph showing periapical lesion in relation to teeth number 36 and 46 with no other changes. (c) Intraoral periapical radiograph in relation to teeth number 26–28. (d) Occlusal radiograph of maxilla\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者自述出现无症状肿物，突发且在1个月内大小稳定 诊断意义：支持中间级黏液表皮样癌的诊断，因为这类肿瘤可能表现为缓慢生长的无痛性肿块\n\n2. 细针穿刺抽出淡血性液体，并且细胞学初诊提示为多形性腺瘤 诊断意义：尽管细胞学初诊指向多形性腺瘤，但黏液表皮样癌也可能表现出类似的临床特征，需要进一步组织病理学确诊\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的无症状肿物及细针穿刺结果，考虑到黏液表皮样癌与多形性腺瘤之间的鉴别诊断困难，最终诊断需依赖于组织病理学检查。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏特异性影像学或病理学证据直接支持中间级黏液表皮样癌的确诊。\n","answer":"\n中间级黏液表皮样癌（mucoepidermoid carcinoma of intermediate grade）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] (a) Solitary swelling at the left posterior maxilla. (b) Panoramic radiograph showing periapical lesion in relation to teeth number 36 and 46 with no other changes. (c) Intraoral periapical radiograph in relation to teeth number 26–28. (d) Occlusal radiograph of maxilla\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] (a) Solitary swelling at the left posterior maxilla. (b) Panoramic radiograph showing periapical lesion in relation to teeth number 36 and 46 with no other changes. (c) Intraoral periapical radiograph in relation to teeth number 26–28. (d) Occlusal radiograph of maxilla\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者自述出现无症状肿物，突发且在1个月内大小稳定 诊断意义：支持中间级黏液表皮样癌的诊断，因为这类肿瘤可能表现为缓慢生长的无痛性肿块\n\n2. 细针穿刺抽出淡血性液体，并且细胞学初诊提示为多形性腺瘤 诊断意义：尽管细胞学初诊指向多形性腺瘤，但黏液表皮样癌也可能表现出类似的临床特征，需要进一步组织病理学确诊\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的无症状肿物及细针穿刺结果，考虑到黏液表皮样癌与多形性腺瘤之间的鉴别诊断困难，最终诊断需依赖于组织病理学检查。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏特异性影像学或病理学证据直接支持中间级黏液表皮样癌的确诊。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n中间级黏液表皮样癌（mucoepidermoid carcinoma of intermediate grade）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC9469393/JPBS-14-1046-g001.jpg","name":"JPBS-14-1046-g001.jpg","caption":"(a) Solitary swelling at the left posterior maxilla. (b) Panoramic radiograph showing periapical lesion in relation to teeth number 36 and 46 with no other changes. (c) Intraoral periapical radiograph in relation to teeth number 26–28. (d) Occlusal radiograph of maxilla","types":["intraoral_photo","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"f65890006d5154cd5ee04ee7729d180982864790b8c9341693e0bb22bcb5bce4","width":539,"height":394}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC13262183","title":"Recurrent Ameloblastic Fibroma of the Posterior Maxilla With Radiopaque Foci: A Diagnostic Challenge Within the Odontogenic Tumor Spectrum.","category":"odontogenic_cyst_tumor","license":"cc by","authors":["Maria Sabbagh","Claude Chaanine"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2026","citation":"Maria Sabbagh, Claude Chaanine. Recurrent Ameloblastic Fibroma of the Posterior Maxilla With Radiopaque Foci: A Diagnostic Challenge Within the Odontogenic Tumor Spectrum. Cureus. 2026. doi: 10.7759/cureus.108780.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2026, Sabbagh et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13262183/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.108780","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [demographics|opg|other_imaging]: 16岁女性，因疑似阻生牙27的病变就诊；初诊影像显示后上颌单房透射影伴放射致密结构，间接干扰牙27萌出\n- E2 [rgb]: 术中见放射致密结构2枚及多个质地不一、易碎的胶冻样团块\n- E3 [laboratory]: 初次组织病理学检查报告为成釉细胞纤维瘤，无恶性证据\n- E4 [laboratory]: 因临床-影像与病理不符，行第二次病理复核，仍确诊为成釉细胞纤维瘤\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [cbct/ct/opg_panoramic] Panoramic view of a cone-beam computed tomography scan showing the radiolucent image that includes a radiopaque structure indirectly interfering with the evolution of tooth 27.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral photos showing multiple fragments of different consistencies.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者为16岁女性，因疑似阻生牙27的病变就诊，初诊影像显示后上颌单房透射影伴放射致密结构，间接干扰牙27萌出。 诊断意义：支持成釉细胞纤维瘤的可能性\n\n2. 术中见放射致密结构2枚及多个质地不一、易碎的胶冻样团块。 诊断意义：支持成釉细胞纤维瘤的可能性\n\n3. 初次组织病理学检查报告为成釉细胞纤维瘤，无恶性证据。 诊断意义：确诊为成釉细胞纤维瘤\n\n4. 因临床-影像与病理不符，行第二次病理复核，仍确诊为成釉细胞纤维瘤。 诊断意义：进一步确认成釉细胞纤维瘤的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床表现、影像学特征以及两次病理学检查结果，最终确诊为成釉细胞纤维瘤。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据表中的信息不足以判断该病例是否为复发性成釉细胞纤维瘤。\n","answer":"\n复发性成釉细胞纤维瘤（Recurrent Ameloblastic Fibroma）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [cbct/ct/opg_panoramic] Panoramic view of a cone-beam computed tomography scan showing the radiolucent image that includes a radiopaque structure indirectly interfering with the evolution of tooth 27.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral photos showing multiple fragments of different consistencies.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者为16岁女性，因疑似阻生牙27的病变就诊，初诊影像显示后上颌单房透射影伴放射致密结构，间接干扰牙27萌出。 诊断意义：支持成釉细胞纤维瘤的可能性\n\n2. 术中见放射致密结构2枚及多个质地不一、易碎的胶冻样团块。 诊断意义：支持成釉细胞纤维瘤的可能性\n\n3. 初次组织病理学检查报告为成釉细胞纤维瘤，无恶性证据。 诊断意义：确诊为成釉细胞纤维瘤\n\n4. 因临床-影像与病理不符，行第二次病理复核，仍确诊为成釉细胞纤维瘤。 诊断意义：进一步确认成釉细胞纤维瘤的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床表现、影像学特征以及两次病理学检查结果，最终确诊为成釉细胞纤维瘤。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据表中的信息不足以判断该病例是否为复发性成釉细胞纤维瘤。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n复发性成釉细胞纤维瘤（Recurrent Ameloblastic Fibroma）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC13262183/cureus-0018-00000108780-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0018-00000108780-i01.jpg","caption":"Panoramic view of a cone-beam computed tomography scan showing the radiolucent image that includes a radiopaque structure indirectly interfering with the evolution of tooth 27.","types":["cbct","ct","opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"65e692a621c3fa8eebc095f5226de423de1ae352408213e728151cb85162790f","width":750,"height":366},{"src":"assets/PMC13262183/cureus-0018-00000108780-i02.jpg","name":"cureus-0018-00000108780-i02.jpg","caption":"Intraoral photos showing multiple fragments of different consistencies.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"dcaeae32074e455a0fa1bf4a7b2f035539d5761f6329cc8eea501ec081c851e3","width":750,"height":753}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC13179519","title":"A Dentigerous Cyst Associated With a Developing Mandibular Premolar in a Pediatric Patient: A Case Report of a Rare Entity.","category":"oral_maxillofacial_other","license":"cc by","authors":["Debadrita Ghosh","Uday Mukherjee","Chitrita Gupta Mukherjee"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2026","citation":"Debadrita Ghosh, Uday Mukherjee, Chitrita Gupta Mukherjee. A Dentigerous Cyst Associated With a Developing Mandibular Premolar in a Pediatric Patient: A Case Report of a Rare Entity. Cureus. 2026. doi: 10.7759/cureus.107134.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2026, Ghosh et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13179519/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.107134","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口外检查见左侧面部下1/3轻度不对称、弥漫性肿胀；皮肤正常，无红肿窦道；触诊为质韧、非波动性、轻压痛肿块，无区域淋巴结肿大\n- E5 [rgb]: 图1A显示左下后牙区颊侧肿胀致前庭沟消失（黑箭头），位于乳第二磨牙处\n- E6 [opg]: 图1B显示2×3 cm透射性囊性区（黄箭头）、第二前磨牙牙胚移位（黑箭头）、感染性龋坏乳第二磨牙（红箭头）\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Intraoral exam and radiographic evaluation(A) Intraoral swelling in the posterior mandible obliterating buccal sulcus (black arrow) at the deciduous second molar. (B) Orthopantomogram showed a radiolucent cystic area of 2 x 3 cm in size (yellow arrow), a displaced tooth bud of the second premolar (black arrow), and an infected carious deciduous second molar (red arrow)Original images of the patient; used with the patient's permission\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Intraoral exam and radiographic evaluation(A) Intraoral swelling in the posterior mandible obliterating buccal sulcus (black arrow) at the deciduous second molar. (B) Orthopantomogram showed a radiolucent cystic area of 2 x 3 cm in size (yellow arrow), a displaced tooth bud of the second premolar (black arrow), and an infected carious deciduous second molar (red arrow)Original images of the patient; used with the patient's permission\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 口外检查发现左侧面部下1/3轻度不对称、弥漫性肿胀，触诊为质韧、非波动性、轻压痛肿块。 诊断意义：支持炎性含牙囊肿的临床表现\n\n2. 图1A显示左下后牙区颊侧肿胀致前庭沟消失。 诊断意义：进一步定位病灶位置\n\n3. 图1B显示2×3 cm透射性囊性区，第二前磨牙牙胚移位及感染性龋坏乳第二磨牙。 诊断意义：支持炎性含牙囊肿（累及发育中下颌第二前磨牙）的影像学特征\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者存在左侧面部下1/3轻度不对称、弥漫性肿胀，结合口腔内见左下后牙区颊侧肿胀和影像学上透射性囊性区与第二前磨牙牙胚移位，支持炎性含牙囊肿（累及发育中下颌第二前磨牙）的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不能完全排除其他类型的囊肿或病变。\n","answer":"\n炎性含牙囊肿（累及发育中下颌第二前磨牙）（dentigerous cyst of inflammatory origin associated with the developing mandibular second premolar）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Intraoral exam and radiographic evaluation(A) Intraoral swelling in the posterior mandible obliterating buccal sulcus (black arrow) at the deciduous second molar. (B) Orthopantomogram showed a radiolucent cystic area of 2 x 3 cm in size (yellow arrow), a displaced tooth bud of the second premolar (black arrow), and an infected carious deciduous second molar (red arrow)Original images of the patient; used with the patient's permission\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Intraoral exam and radiographic evaluation(A) Intraoral swelling in the posterior mandible obliterating buccal sulcus (black arrow) at the deciduous second molar. (B) Orthopantomogram showed a radiolucent cystic area of 2 x 3 cm in size (yellow arrow), a displaced tooth bud of the second premolar (black arrow), and an infected carious deciduous second molar (red arrow)Original images of the patient; used with the patient's permission\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 口外检查发现左侧面部下1/3轻度不对称、弥漫性肿胀，触诊为质韧、非波动性、轻压痛肿块。 诊断意义：支持炎性含牙囊肿的临床表现\n\n2. 图1A显示左下后牙区颊侧肿胀致前庭沟消失。 诊断意义：进一步定位病灶位置\n\n3. 图1B显示2×3 cm透射性囊性区，第二前磨牙牙胚移位及感染性龋坏乳第二磨牙。 诊断意义：支持炎性含牙囊肿（累及发育中下颌第二前磨牙）的影像学特征\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者存在左侧面部下1/3轻度不对称、弥漫性肿胀，结合口腔内见左下后牙区颊侧肿胀和影像学上透射性囊性区与第二前磨牙牙胚移位，支持炎性含牙囊肿（累及发育中下颌第二前磨牙）的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不能完全排除其他类型的囊肿或病变。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n炎性含牙囊肿（累及发育中下颌第二前磨牙）（dentigerous cyst of inflammatory origin associated with the developing mandibular second premolar）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC13179519/cureus-0018-00000107134-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0018-00000107134-i01.jpg","caption":"Intraoral exam and radiographic evaluation(A) Intraoral swelling in the posterior mandible obliterating buccal sulcus (black arrow) at the deciduous second molar. (B) Orthopantomogram showed a radiolucent cystic area of 2 x 3 cm in size (yellow arrow), a displaced tooth bud of the second premolar (black arrow), and an infected carious deciduous second molar (red arrow)Original images of the patient; used with the patient's permission","types":["intraoral_photo","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"e24b4b88e3814a779b086cb6ee9af504922e04e9ff172c1351ac80ad3490f9d1","width":750,"height":250}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12964317","title":"Multiple Impacted Supernumerary Teeth in a Non-syndromic Class III Malocclusion Patient: A Case Report.","category":"developmental_eruption","license":"cc by","authors":["Wissam El Hazzat","Nawal Bouyahyaoui","Fatima Zaoui"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2026","citation":"Wissam El Hazzat, Nawal Bouyahyaoui, Fatima Zaoui. Multiple Impacted Supernumerary Teeth in a Non-syndromic Class III Malocclusion Patient: A Case Report. Cureus. 2026. doi: 10.7759/cureus.102941.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2026, El Hazzat et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12964317/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.102941","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history|demographics|symptom|clinical_exam]: 21岁男性，主诉美观问题就诊；临床检查见Ⅲ类错𬌗、拥挤、44牙缺失、牙弓不对称\n- E2 [clinical_exam|rgb]: 口内检查：上下前牙-尖牙拥挤、前牙对刃、左侧尖牙与磨牙Ⅲ类关系、右侧尖牙Ⅱ类/磨牙Ⅲ类关系，因44牙缺失所致\n- E3 [opg]: 全景片显示44牙阻生及5颗多生牙：双侧上颌侧切牙与尖牙间各1颗补充尖牙，左下前磨牙区1颗额外磨牙，右下前磨牙区2颗额外磨牙\n- E4 [other_imaging]: CBCT证实6颗阻生牙（含5颗多生牙）：上颌2颗垂直阻生；下颌左侧前磨牙区1颗阻生，右侧前磨牙区3颗阻生（其中2颗水平位）；另见44牙阻生\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph showing impaction of tooth 44 and five supernumerary teeth: two supplementary canines between the lateral incisors and canines bilaterally, one left paramolar between the left mandibular premolars, and two right mandibular paramolars.\n- [cbct/ct] CBCT images illustrating multiple impacted supernumerary teeth.CBCT images show six impacted teeth, including five supernumerary teeth. Two vertically impacted teeth are observed in the maxilla. In the mandible, one impacted premolar is present in the left premolar region, while three impacted premolars are located in the right premolar region, two of which are horizontally oriented. The left and right panels show sequential sagittal CBCT slices of the anterior and posterior regions, while the central panel presents a 3D volume-rendered reconstruction of the jaws. Sagittal CBCT sections reveal the presence of five impacted supernumerary teeth, located in different regions and orientations, clearly identified and outlined in red. The 3D CBCT reconstruction confirms the spatial distribution, and anatomical relationships of these supernumerary teeth within the jaws. Additionally, an impacted mandibular right first premolar (tooth 44) is visible and circled in red on the sagittal CBCT images, showing an abnormal position within the mandibular bone.CBCT, cone-beam computed tomography; 3D, three-dimensional.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo/intraoral_photo] Extraoral (a, b, c) and intraoral (d, e, f, g, h) photographs at treatment initiation showing Class III occlusion, ectopic canines, missing tooth 45, and notable esthetic discrepancy.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者存在Ⅲ类错𬌗、拥挤及44牙缺失，提示骨性Ⅲ类错𬌗伴牙齿问题。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 上下前牙-尖牙拥挤、前牙对刃及特定牙齿关系的临床表现进一步支持了Ⅲ类错𬌗的存在。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 全景片显示多颗多生牙及44牙阻生，提供了额外的诊断依据。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. CBCT证实了6颗阻生牙（包括5颗多生牙）的具体位置和方向，进一步明确了诊断。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床检查结果以及影像学发现，可以得出非综合征型骨性Ⅲ类错𬌗伴多生牙及44牙阻生的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据表中未提供具体鉴别诊断信息，因此无法完全排除其他可能引起相似症状的情况。\n","answer":"\n非综合征型骨性Ⅲ类错𬌗伴多生牙及44牙阻生（Non-syndromic Class III malocclusion associated with multiple supernumerary and impacted teeth）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph showing impaction of tooth 44 and five supernumerary teeth: two supplementary canines between the lateral incisors and canines bilaterally, one left paramolar between the left mandibular premolars, and two right mandibular paramolars.\n- [cbct/ct] CBCT images illustrating multiple impacted supernumerary teeth.CBCT images show six impacted teeth, including five supernumerary teeth. Two vertically impacted teeth are observed in the maxilla. In the mandible, one impacted premolar is present in the left premolar region, while three impacted premolars are located in the right premolar region, two of which are horizontally oriented. The left and right panels show sequential sagittal CBCT slices of the anterior and posterior regions, while the central panel presents a 3D volume-rendered reconstruction of the jaws. Sagittal CBCT sections reveal the presence of five impacted supernumerary teeth, located in different regions and orientations, clearly identified and outlined in red. The 3D CBCT reconstruction confirms the spatial distribution, and anatomical relationships of these supernumerary teeth within the jaws. Additionally, an impacted mandibular right first premolar (tooth 44) is visible and circled in red on the sagittal CBCT images, showing an abnormal position within the mandibular bone.CBCT, cone-beam computed tomography; 3D, three-dimensional.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo/intraoral_photo] Extraoral (a, b, c) and intraoral (d, e, f, g, h) photographs at treatment initiation showing Class III occlusion, ectopic canines, missing tooth 45, and notable esthetic discrepancy.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者存在Ⅲ类错𬌗、拥挤及44牙缺失，提示骨性Ⅲ类错𬌗伴牙齿问题。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 上下前牙-尖牙拥挤、前牙对刃及特定牙齿关系的临床表现进一步支持了Ⅲ类错𬌗的存在。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 全景片显示多颗多生牙及44牙阻生，提供了额外的诊断依据。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. CBCT证实了6颗阻生牙（包括5颗多生牙）的具体位置和方向，进一步明确了诊断。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床检查结果以及影像学发现，可以得出非综合征型骨性Ⅲ类错𬌗伴多生牙及44牙阻生的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据表中未提供具体鉴别诊断信息，因此无法完全排除其他可能引起相似症状的情况。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n非综合征型骨性Ⅲ类错𬌗伴多生牙及44牙阻生（Non-syndromic Class III malocclusion associated with multiple supernumerary and impacted teeth）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12964317/cureus-0018-00000102941-i02.jpg","name":"cureus-0018-00000102941-i02.jpg","caption":"Panoramic radiograph showing impaction of tooth 44 and five supernumerary teeth: two supplementary canines between the lateral incisors and canines bilaterally, one left paramolar between the left mandibular premolars, and two right mandibular paramolars.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"e0546945213d7f6f8a9884edc930d43efb7e265742b879f1e1d94087203b4225","width":750,"height":363},{"src":"assets/PMC12964317/cureus-0018-00000102941-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0018-00000102941-i01.jpg","caption":"Extraoral (a, b, c) and intraoral (d, e, f, g, h) photographs at treatment initiation showing Class III occlusion, ectopic canines, missing tooth 45, and notable esthetic discrepancy.","types":["extraoral_photo","intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"42913cc1180a70d78174f9eef9e20ea883c1193c4188dba321c5aba39b1bb033","width":750,"height":433},{"src":"assets/PMC12964317/cureus-0018-00000102941-i03.jpg","name":"cureus-0018-00000102941-i03.jpg","caption":"CBCT images illustrating multiple impacted supernumerary teeth.CBCT images show six impacted teeth, including five supernumerary teeth. Two vertically impacted teeth are observed in the maxilla. In the mandible, one impacted premolar is present in the left premolar region, while three impacted premolars are located in the right premolar region, two of which are horizontally oriented. The left and right panels show sequential sagittal CBCT slices of the anterior and posterior regions, while the central panel presents a 3D volume-rendered reconstruction of the jaws. Sagittal CBCT sections reveal the presence of five impacted supernumerary teeth, located in different regions and orientations, clearly identified and outlined in red. The 3D CBCT reconstruction confirms the spatial distribution, and anatomical relationships of these supernumerary teeth within the jaws. Additionally, an impacted mandibular right first premolar (tooth 44) is visible and circled in red on the sagittal CBCT images, showing an abnormal position within the mandibular bone.CBCT, cone-beam computed tomography; 3D, three-dimensional.","types":["cbct","ct"],"sha256":"2c08c1c82ef87b7bc9d96fea868bcb8dde07aa7244fc6dc6cc141d58d7316228","width":750,"height":181}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC11929591","title":"Peripheral Odontogenic Keratocyst Presenting as a Gingival Nodular Mass in the Anterior Mandible: A Case Report.","category":"periodontal","license":"cc by","authors":["Itsuki Hayashi","Makoto Toida"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2025","citation":"Itsuki Hayashi, Makoto Toida. Peripheral Odontogenic Keratocyst Presenting as a Gingival Nodular Mass in the Anterior Mandible: A Case Report. Cureus. 2025. doi: 10.7759/cureus.79382.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025, Hayashi et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11929591/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.79382","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 73岁男性，左下中切牙拔除多年后，前牙区牙龈出现持续3个月、渐进性增大的结节性肿物\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查见左下中切牙区牙龈有1.5 cm暗红色结节状肿物，质软，表面光滑无溃疡\n- E3 [opg]: 曲面断层片显示左下中切牙缺失区存在边界清楚的椭圆形透射影，伴局部骨吸收\n- E4 [other_imaging]: CT显示前下颌骨区病变致牙槽嵴压迫性骨吸收\n- E5 [clinical_exam]: 临床鉴别诊断包括间叶源性肿瘤、牙源性肿瘤及牙源性囊肿（如残余囊肿）\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Preoperative panoramic radiographA panoramic radiograph shows a well-defined mass with bone resorption localized in the missing left mandibular central incisor region (arrowhead).\n- [ct] Preoperative computed tomography imageA computed tomography image shows compressive bone resorption of the alveolar ridge owing to a lesion in the anterior mandibular region (arrow).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n","think":"\n1. 患者为73岁男性，左下中切牙拔除多年后前牙区牙龈出现持续3个月、渐进性增大的结节性肿物。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查见左下中切牙区牙龈有1.5 cm暗红色结节状肿物，质软，表面光滑无溃疡。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 曲面断层片显示左下中切牙缺失区存在边界清楚的椭圆形透射影，伴局部骨吸收；CT显示前下颌骨区病变致牙槽嵴压迫性骨吸收。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 老年男性患者左下中切牙拔除多年后出现渐进性增大且无痛性的前牙区牙龈结节，结合影像学上边界清晰的透射影及局部骨吸收表现，提示外周型牙源性角化囊肿可能。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；鉴别诊断包括间叶源性肿瘤、牙源性肿瘤及其他牙源性囊肿（如残余囊肿），当前证据不足以完全排除其他可能性。\n","answer":"\n外周型牙源性角化囊肿（Peripheral Odontogenic Keratocyst）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Preoperative panoramic radiographA panoramic radiograph shows a well-defined mass with bone resorption localized in the missing left mandibular central incisor region (arrowhead).\n- [ct] Preoperative computed tomography imageA computed tomography image shows compressive bone resorption of the alveolar ridge owing to a lesion in the anterior mandibular region (arrow).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者为73岁男性，左下中切牙拔除多年后前牙区牙龈出现持续3个月、渐进性增大的结节性肿物。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查见左下中切牙区牙龈有1.5 cm暗红色结节状肿物，质软，表面光滑无溃疡。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 曲面断层片显示左下中切牙缺失区存在边界清楚的椭圆形透射影，伴局部骨吸收；CT显示前下颌骨区病变致牙槽嵴压迫性骨吸收。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 老年男性患者左下中切牙拔除多年后出现渐进性增大且无痛性的前牙区牙龈结节，结合影像学上边界清晰的透射影及局部骨吸收表现，提示外周型牙源性角化囊肿可能。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；鉴别诊断包括间叶源性肿瘤、牙源性肿瘤及其他牙源性囊肿（如残余囊肿），当前证据不足以完全排除其他可能性。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n外周型牙源性角化囊肿（Peripheral Odontogenic Keratocyst）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC11929591/cureus-0017-00000079382-i02.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000079382-i02.jpg","caption":"Preoperative panoramic radiographA panoramic radiograph shows a well-defined mass with bone resorption localized in the missing left mandibular central incisor region (arrowhead).","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"87fffddeab89314bf283240f531d8aa09bd3a016d21b01da8408f36285653b39","width":750,"height":274},{"src":"assets/PMC11929591/cureus-0017-00000079382-i03.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000079382-i03.jpg","caption":"Preoperative computed tomography imageA computed tomography image shows compressive bone resorption of the alveolar ridge owing to a lesion in the anterior mandibular region (arrow).","types":["ct"],"sha256":"5b2587579015246581b51991a652ef6c630bedb49b6381b15e5f7686cf7d596b","width":750,"height":422}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12032624","title":"Buccal Abscess With Dystrophic Calcification: A Case Report.","category":"infection","license":"cc by","authors":["Mai Kobayashi","Yasuyuki Fujii","Hinano Oda","Ayano Hatori","Daichi Chikazu"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2025","citation":"Mai Kobayashi, Yasuyuki Fujii, Hinano Oda, Ayano Hatori, Daichi Chikazu. Buccal Abscess With Dystrophic Calcification: A Case Report. Cureus. 2025. doi: 10.7759/cureus.81272.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025, Kobayashi et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12032624/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.81272","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 54岁男性，主诉右侧颊部疼痛与肿胀，病程始于10月底；初诊于当地牙医未明确病因\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 体格检查见右侧颊部至下颌区域肿胀，颊黏膜近下颌前磨牙区充血、肿胀伴内出血；肿胀位于咬合平面附近，可见牙压痕\n- E3 [laboratory]: 血常规示白细胞升高（18.0 × 10³/µL），CRP升高（1.62 mg/dL）\n- E4 [opg]: OPG显示无明显异常\n- E5 [other_imaging]: 超声显示右侧颊部一约21×10 mm低回声区，中央高回声区，伴血流信号；提示脓肿及异物存在\n- E6 [clinical_exam]: 术中切开引流获得3枚约3 mm长、黄白色、骨样质地、无周围组织粘连的硬质碎片\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] OPG showing no apparent abnormalitiesOPG: orthopantomography\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Physical findings of the patient(A) Facial appearance showing swelling extending from the right buccal region to the right mandible. (B) Intraoral photograph revealing internal bleeding and swelling of the buccal mucosa near the lower premolars.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者主诉右侧颊部疼痛与肿胀，提示存在局部炎症或感染。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 体格检查发现右侧颊黏膜区域充血、肿胀伴内出血，且可见牙压痕，进一步证实了该部位的急性炎症表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 实验室检查显示白细胞和CRP升高，结合超声影像学特征（低回声区中央有高回声及血流信号），提示存在感染性脓肿。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 术中切开引流获得硬质碎片，其性质符合营养不良性钙化灶，这解释了感染源可能为异物刺激导致的局部反应。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的临床症状、体征以及辅助检查结果，可推断出患者患有由营养不良性钙化引起的感染性颊脓肿。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；OPG未见明显异常，不能直接提供关于钙化灶的具体信息。\n","answer":"\n颊黏膜营养不良性钙化伴感染性颊脓肿（Dystrophic calcification in the buccal mucosa with concurrent buccal abscess）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] OPG showing no apparent abnormalitiesOPG: orthopantomography\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Physical findings of the patient(A) Facial appearance showing swelling extending from the right buccal region to the right mandible. (B) Intraoral photograph revealing internal bleeding and swelling of the buccal mucosa near the lower premolars.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者主诉右侧颊部疼痛与肿胀，提示存在局部炎症或感染。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 体格检查发现右侧颊黏膜区域充血、肿胀伴内出血，且可见牙压痕，进一步证实了该部位的急性炎症表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 实验室检查显示白细胞和CRP升高，结合超声影像学特征（低回声区中央有高回声及血流信号），提示存在感染性脓肿。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 术中切开引流获得硬质碎片，其性质符合营养不良性钙化灶，这解释了感染源可能为异物刺激导致的局部反应。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的临床症状、体征以及辅助检查结果，可推断出患者患有由营养不良性钙化引起的感染性颊脓肿。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；OPG未见明显异常，不能直接提供关于钙化灶的具体信息。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n颊黏膜营养不良性钙化伴感染性颊脓肿（Dystrophic calcification in the buccal mucosa with concurrent buccal abscess）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12032624/cureus-0017-00000081272-i02.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000081272-i02.jpg","caption":"OPG showing no apparent abnormalitiesOPG: orthopantomography","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"3998ba1ab73e2e39edc7a3cde6a60b6fbb1617f081115a734153ae9a1f700025","width":750,"height":393},{"src":"assets/PMC12032624/cureus-0017-00000081272-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000081272-i01.jpg","caption":"Physical findings of the patient(A) Facial appearance showing swelling extending from the right buccal region to the right mandible. (B) Intraoral photograph revealing internal bleeding and swelling of the buccal mucosa near the lower premolars.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"3aac27e89cff743774ccc38e60aed7294a787990277bb92f21e8c6ce1080710f","width":750,"height":320}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC9756689","title":"Severe alveolar bone resorption in Felty syndrome: a case report.","category":"trauma_resorption","license":"cc by","authors":["Satoru Morikawa","Yoko Miyashita","Mana Nasu","Shunichi Shibazaki","Satoshi Usuda","Kazuyuki Tsunoda","Taneaki Nakagawa"],"journal":"Journal of medical case reports","year":"2022","citation":"Satoru Morikawa, Yoko Miyashita, Mana Nasu, Shunichi Shibazaki, Satoshi Usuda, Kazuyuki Tsunoda, Taneaki Nakagawa. Severe alveolar bone resorption in Felty syndrome: a case report. Journal of medical case reports. 2022. doi: 10.1186/s13256-022-03703-1.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"],"licenseText":"Open AccessThis article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, which permits use, sharing, adaptation, distribution and reproduction in any medium or format, as long as you give appropriate credit to the original author(s) and the source, provide a link to the Creative Commons licence, and indicate if changes were made. The images or other third party material in this article are included in the article's Creative Commons licence, unless indicated otherwise in a credit line to the material. If material is not included in the article's Creative Commons licence and your intended use is not permitted by statutory regulation or exceeds the permitted use, you will need to obtain permission directly from the copyright holder. To view a copy of this licence, visit http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. The Creative Commons Public Domain Dedication waiver (http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/) applies to the data made available in this article, unless otherwise stated in a credit line to the data.","copyright":["© The Author(s) 2022"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9756689/","doi":"10.1186/s13256-022-03703-1","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [symptom]: 55岁女性，主诉牙齿松动加重、不适及自发性牙龈出血\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口腔卫生差，下颌磨牙修复体不良\n- E4 [opg]: OPG显示双侧上下颌磨牙区水平与垂直型骨吸收，部分达根尖区；对比17个月前影像显示快速进展\n- E6 [laboratory]: 白细胞减少（0.6 × 10³/µL），中性粒细胞12%，贫血（Hb 7.4 g/dL），血小板减少（103 × 10³/µL）\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic oral radiographs reveal rapid alveolar bone loss after onset of Felty syndrome. a Panoramic radiograph taken 1 year and 5 months before the initial visit to our department. b Panoramic radiograph at the time of initial examination. Significant progression of alveolar bone resorption in a period of 1 year and 5 months is observed\n- [radiograph] Initial periapical radiographs. Radiographs reveal widespread horizontal bone loss extending to the root apex\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n","think":"\n1. 患者主诉牙齿松动加重、不适及自发性牙龈出血，提示存在牙周问题。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. OPG显示双侧上下颌磨牙区水平与垂直型骨吸收，部分达根尖区；对比17个月前影像显示快速进展，表明牙周炎处于严重阶段且进展迅速。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 实验室检查发现白细胞减少（0.6 × 10³/µL），中性粒细胞比例低至12%，贫血（Hb 7.4 g/dL）以及血小板减少（103 × 10³/µL），符合Felty综合征的血液学特征。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的症状、影像学表现及实验室检查结果，支持诊断为Felty综合征伴广泛性重度牙周炎（IV期C级）。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；未提供直接证据证明口腔卫生差和下颌磨牙修复体不良与当前诊断之间的关系。\n","answer":"\nFelty综合征伴广泛性重度牙周炎（IV期C级）（Felty syndrome with generalized severe periodontitis (Stage IV Grade C)）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic oral radiographs reveal rapid alveolar bone loss after onset of Felty syndrome. a Panoramic radiograph taken 1 year and 5 months before the initial visit to our department. b Panoramic radiograph at the time of initial examination. Significant progression of alveolar bone resorption in a period of 1 year and 5 months is observed\n- [radiograph] Initial periapical radiographs. Radiographs reveal widespread horizontal bone loss extending to the root apex\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者主诉牙齿松动加重、不适及自发性牙龈出血，提示存在牙周问题。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. OPG显示双侧上下颌磨牙区水平与垂直型骨吸收，部分达根尖区；对比17个月前影像显示快速进展，表明牙周炎处于严重阶段且进展迅速。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 实验室检查发现白细胞减少（0.6 × 10³/µL），中性粒细胞比例低至12%，贫血（Hb 7.4 g/dL）以及血小板减少（103 × 10³/µL），符合Felty综合征的血液学特征。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的症状、影像学表现及实验室检查结果，支持诊断为Felty综合征伴广泛性重度牙周炎（IV期C级）。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；未提供直接证据证明口腔卫生差和下颌磨牙修复体不良与当前诊断之间的关系。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\nFelty综合征伴广泛性重度牙周炎（IV期C级）（Felty syndrome with generalized severe periodontitis (Stage IV Grade C)）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC9756689/13256_2022_3703_Fig1_HTML.jpg","name":"13256_2022_3703_Fig1_HTML.jpg","caption":"Panoramic oral radiographs reveal rapid alveolar bone loss after onset of Felty syndrome. a Panoramic radiograph taken 1 year and 5 months before the initial visit to our department. b Panoramic radiograph at the time of initial examination. Significant progression of alveolar bone resorption in a period of 1 year and 5 months is observed","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"c8b0e912b982170855a51426670a9cb4ff27ccfd6a781443d80894d7cb3d3444","width":896,"height":1025},{"src":"assets/PMC9756689/13256_2022_3703_Fig3_HTML.jpg","name":"13256_2022_3703_Fig3_HTML.jpg","caption":"Initial periapical radiographs. Radiographs reveal widespread horizontal bone loss extending to the root apex","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"f6012db43680620d3fa977f7063c5b9b662c4081e9c71f84c24ad54ba88bb790","width":1959,"height":625}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC9287005","title":"Maxillary Fungal Osteomyelitis Mimicking and Treated as Endodontic Pathosis.","category":"endodontic_periapical","license":"cc by","authors":["Sarang Suresh Hotchandani","Feroze Ali Kalhoro","Priya Rani Harjani","Mahwish Memon"],"journal":"Case reports in dentistry","year":"2022","citation":"Sarang Suresh Hotchandani, Feroze Ali Kalhoro, Priya Rani Harjani, Mahwish Memon. Maxillary Fungal Osteomyelitis Mimicking and Treated as Endodontic Pathosis. Case reports in dentistry. 2022. doi: 10.1155/2022/1976352.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2022 Sarang Suresh Hotchandani et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9287005/","doi":"10.1155/2022/1976352","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E3 [opg]: 初诊OPG无明显异常；20天后OPG显示2号牙近中透射线及邻牙根尖周透射影；6–7号牙充填，8–11号牙仅见高密度充填物而根管空虚\n- E4 [other_imaging]: CBCT三维重建显示右侧上颌牙槽突至左侧前磨牙区呈斑片状溶骨性改变；轴位见右侧上颌窦完全模糊、右侧上颌骨呈虫蚀样破坏\n- E5 [laboratory]: 实验室检查：HbA1c 6.53%，CRP 3.341 mg/dl，血小板正常；无显著系统性疾病史\n- E6 [history]: 既往有登革热感染史致血小板减少并住院；近期无症状，否认糖尿病史\n- E7 [clinical_exam]: 面部右侧弥漫性肿胀；颞下颌关节检查正常；无颈淋巴结肿大\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] OPG of case 1 obtained at 15 days' gap.\n- [cbct/radiograph] 3D CBCT view of case 1 showing resorption over the maxillary alveolus region on the right side.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Clinical photographs of case 1: (a) frontal view, (b) right maxillary view showing the ulcer, (c) palatal view, and (d) right maxillary view showing normal gingiva.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者初诊OPG无明显异常，20天后OPG显示2号牙近中透射线及邻牙根尖周透射影，提示存在局部骨质破坏。 诊断意义：支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\n\n2. CBCT三维重建进一步显示右侧上颌牙槽突至左侧前磨牙区呈斑片状溶骨性改变，右侧上颌窦完全模糊、右侧上颌骨呈虫蚀样破坏，符合真菌感染导致的骨质破坏特点。 诊断意义：支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\n\n3. 实验室检查HbA1c为6.53%，提示可能存在糖尿病前期或未被识别的糖尿病状态，这是毛霉菌病的一个重要危险因素。 诊断意义：支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\n\n4. 临床检查发现面部右侧弥漫性肿胀，结合影像学和实验室检查结果，考虑为毛霉菌病所致。 诊断意义：支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据影像学证据(E3, E4)显示的骨质破坏特征，结合实验室检查(E5)发现的潜在糖尿病前期状态以及临床表现(E7)，支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏直接病理学或微生物学证据来确诊毛霉菌病；仅凭现有证据不能完全排除其他类型的感染或疾病。\n","answer":"\n上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）（Maxillary fungal osteomyelitis (mucormycosis)）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] OPG of case 1 obtained at 15 days' gap.\n- [cbct/radiograph] 3D CBCT view of case 1 showing resorption over the maxillary alveolus region on the right side.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Clinical photographs of case 1: (a) frontal view, (b) right maxillary view showing the ulcer, (c) palatal view, and (d) right maxillary view showing normal gingiva.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者初诊OPG无明显异常，20天后OPG显示2号牙近中透射线及邻牙根尖周透射影，提示存在局部骨质破坏。 诊断意义：支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\n\n2. CBCT三维重建进一步显示右侧上颌牙槽突至左侧前磨牙区呈斑片状溶骨性改变，右侧上颌窦完全模糊、右侧上颌骨呈虫蚀样破坏，符合真菌感染导致的骨质破坏特点。 诊断意义：支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\n\n3. 实验室检查HbA1c为6.53%，提示可能存在糖尿病前期或未被识别的糖尿病状态，这是毛霉菌病的一个重要危险因素。 诊断意义：支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\n\n4. 临床检查发现面部右侧弥漫性肿胀，结合影像学和实验室检查结果，考虑为毛霉菌病所致。 诊断意义：支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据影像学证据(E3, E4)显示的骨质破坏特征，结合实验室检查(E5)发现的潜在糖尿病前期状态以及临床表现(E7)，支持上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏直接病理学或微生物学证据来确诊毛霉菌病；仅凭现有证据不能完全排除其他类型的感染或疾病。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n上颌真菌性骨髓炎（毛霉菌病）（Maxillary fungal osteomyelitis (mucormycosis)）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC9287005/CRID2022-1976352.002.jpg","name":"CRID2022-1976352.002.jpg","caption":"OPG of case 1 obtained at 15 days' gap.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"60c6bc6efb27b2766a30eb332846d5651936c19458300046c5aab9f3a2f41645","width":643,"height":164},{"src":"assets/PMC9287005/CRID2022-1976352.001.jpg","name":"CRID2022-1976352.001.jpg","caption":"Clinical photographs of case 1: (a) frontal view, (b) right maxillary view showing the ulcer, (c) palatal view, and (d) right maxillary view showing normal gingiva.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"c3d68c1a52bafbcf78997c7380dadf525044bb09e474c2e7a70fd066569b668a","width":789,"height":685},{"src":"assets/PMC9287005/CRID2022-1976352.003.jpg","name":"CRID2022-1976352.003.jpg","caption":"3D CBCT view of case 1 showing resorption over the maxillary alveolus region on the right side.","types":["cbct","radiograph"],"sha256":"b1d0b9605d9c24c0bbdde00478dff58dc7a6a9415e2f2dc57b8b6592b261e4ea","width":384,"height":217}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12554343","title":"Parry-Romberg Syndrome: A Rare Case with Diagnostic Challenges and Orthodontic Implications.","category":"orthodontic_craniofacial","license":"cc by","authors":["Shubham Patel","P Narayana Prasad","Tarun Sharma","Anupa Rawat","Amit Agarwal"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2025","citation":"Shubham Patel, P Narayana Prasad, Tarun Sharma, Anupa Rawat, Amit Agarwal. Parry-Romberg Syndrome: A Rare Case with Diagnostic Challenges and Orthodontic Implications. Cureus. 2025. doi: 10.7759/cureus.93225.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025, Patel et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12554343/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.93225","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E3 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查：双颌轻度前牙拥挤、左侧前牙反𬌗、下前牙龈退缩、双颌右侧明显缩窄\n- E4 [opg]: OPG显示右侧下颌升支与体部长度减小，右侧第三磨牙阻生；患者自述患侧牙齿萌出延迟\n- E5 [other_imaging]: 头影测量：骨性III类（SNA=82°, SNB=86°, ANB=–4°），软组织轮廓凹面型，下颌基骨相对上颌延长（1.8:2.2）\n- E10 [history]: 家族史无遗传倾向，经系谱分析与遗传咨询排除遗传性\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic evaluation of the patient(A) Orthopantomogram showing reduced ramus and corpus length on the right side along with an impacted third molar; (B) Lateral cephalogram demonstrating a skeletal Class III jaw relationship with a concave soft tissue profile (SNA=82°, SNB=86°, ANB=–4°); (C) Posteroanterior cephalogram confirms facial asymmetry.SNB: Sella-Nasion-Point B angle; ANB: Point A-Nasion-Point B angle.\n- [ct] Computed tomography (CT) of the craniofacial skeletonCT imaging demonstrating atrophy of the right zygomatic, maxillary, and mandibular bones, with inferior positioning of the right orbital floor compared to the left.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] Extraoral clinical photographs of the patient(A) Frontal view showing right-sided hemifacial atrophy with lip deviation, hyperpigmentation, and a scar-like depression in the symphyseal region (coup de sabre); (B) Smiling view demonstrating exaggerated shrinkage of the skin on the affected side, consistent with subcutaneous fat and soft tissue loss; (C) Worm’s-eye view highlighting prominent superficial veins due to thinning of overlying soft tissues.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 口内检查发现双颌轻度前牙拥挤、左侧前牙反𬌗、下前牙龈退缩及双颌右侧明显缩窄，提示面部一侧发育异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. OPG显示右侧下颌升支与体部长度减小，以及第三磨牙阻生和牙齿萌出延迟，进一步表明存在单侧面部骨质发育不良。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 头影测量分析显示骨性III类咬合关系，软组织轮廓呈凹面型，且下颌基骨相对上颌延长，这些都符合帕里-罗姆伯格综合征的特征。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 家族史无遗传倾向，排除了其他可能的遗传性疾病作为病因。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者表现出典型的面部半侧萎缩症状，包括口内检查所见的不对称发育、影像学上的骨骼异常以及排除遗传因素后，高度怀疑帕里-罗姆伯格综合征。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；提供的证据不能完全排除其他可能导致类似临床表现的情况。\n","answer":"\n帕里-罗姆伯格综合征（Parry-Romberg Syndrome）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic evaluation of the patient(A) Orthopantomogram showing reduced ramus and corpus length on the right side along with an impacted third molar; (B) Lateral cephalogram demonstrating a skeletal Class III jaw relationship with a concave soft tissue profile (SNA=82°, SNB=86°, ANB=–4°); (C) Posteroanterior cephalogram confirms facial asymmetry.SNB: Sella-Nasion-Point B angle; ANB: Point A-Nasion-Point B angle.\n- [ct] Computed tomography (CT) of the craniofacial skeletonCT imaging demonstrating atrophy of the right zygomatic, maxillary, and mandibular bones, with inferior positioning of the right orbital floor compared to the left.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] Extraoral clinical photographs of the patient(A) Frontal view showing right-sided hemifacial atrophy with lip deviation, hyperpigmentation, and a scar-like depression in the symphyseal region (coup de sabre); (B) Smiling view demonstrating exaggerated shrinkage of the skin on the affected side, consistent with subcutaneous fat and soft tissue loss; (C) Worm’s-eye view highlighting prominent superficial veins due to thinning of overlying soft tissues.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 口内检查发现双颌轻度前牙拥挤、左侧前牙反𬌗、下前牙龈退缩及双颌右侧明显缩窄，提示面部一侧发育异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. OPG显示右侧下颌升支与体部长度减小，以及第三磨牙阻生和牙齿萌出延迟，进一步表明存在单侧面部骨质发育不良。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 头影测量分析显示骨性III类咬合关系，软组织轮廓呈凹面型，且下颌基骨相对上颌延长，这些都符合帕里-罗姆伯格综合征的特征。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 家族史无遗传倾向，排除了其他可能的遗传性疾病作为病因。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者表现出典型的面部半侧萎缩症状，包括口内检查所见的不对称发育、影像学上的骨骼异常以及排除遗传因素后，高度怀疑帕里-罗姆伯格综合征。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；提供的证据不能完全排除其他可能导致类似临床表现的情况。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n帕里-罗姆伯格综合征（Parry-Romberg Syndrome）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12554343/cureus-0017-00000093225-i07.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000093225-i07.jpg","caption":"Radiographic evaluation of the patient(A) Orthopantomogram showing reduced ramus and corpus length on the right side along with an impacted third molar; (B) Lateral cephalogram demonstrating a skeletal Class III jaw relationship with a concave soft tissue profile (SNA=82°, SNB=86°, ANB=–4°); (C) Posteroanterior cephalogram confirms facial asymmetry.SNB: Sella-Nasion-Point B angle; ANB: Point A-Nasion-Point B angle.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"71de79876d86fb469f4e5bc7b7ad8b846dec744d2c2282007158018024b671e3","width":750,"height":842},{"src":"assets/PMC12554343/cureus-0017-00000093225-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000093225-i01.jpg","caption":"Extraoral clinical photographs of the patient(A) Frontal view showing right-sided hemifacial atrophy with lip deviation, hyperpigmentation, and a scar-like depression in the symphyseal region (coup de sabre); (B) Smiling view demonstrating exaggerated shrinkage of the skin on the affected side, consistent with subcutaneous fat and soft tissue loss; (C) Worm’s-eye view highlighting prominent superficial veins due to thinning of overlying soft tissues.","types":["extraoral_photo"],"sha256":"246f57803ddc64a79889d23b9381f0f0fce05b83e6bf93267125429468dd39ba","width":750,"height":279},{"src":"assets/PMC12554343/cureus-0017-00000093225-i08.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000093225-i08.jpg","caption":"Computed tomography (CT) of the craniofacial skeletonCT imaging demonstrating atrophy of the right zygomatic, maxillary, and mandibular bones, with inferior positioning of the right orbital floor compared to the left.","types":["ct"],"sha256":"95e6451f56946ce9ba87cf47be86be00581d48cc99c3ba3b2578602a15f8a2a5","width":750,"height":326}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC5012755","title":"Adenoid cystic carcinoma of the palate: case report and review of literature.","category":"mucosal_oral_lesion","license":"cc by","authors":["Uday Shankar Yaga","Nishanth Gollamudi","Ashwini Kumar Mengji","Radhika Besta","Prashanth Panta","Bhanu Prakash","Edunuri Rajashekar"],"journal":"The Pan African medical journal","year":"2016","citation":"Uday Shankar Yaga, Nishanth Gollamudi, Ashwini Kumar Mengji, Radhika Besta, Prashanth Panta, Bhanu Prakash, Edunuri Rajashekar. Adenoid cystic carcinoma of the palate: case report and review of literature. The Pan African medical journal. 2016. doi: 10.11604/pamj.2016.24.106.8596.","license_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/","licenseUrls":["http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/The Pan African Medical Journal - ISSN 1937-8688. This is an Open Access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["© Uday Shankar Yaga et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5012755/","doi":"10.11604/pamj.2016.24.106.8596","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 35岁女性，主诉上颌后部肿物8个月，伴咀嚼及吞咽困难；肿物起始小，渐进性增大\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查见单发、边界清楚肿物，前后径自右上中切牙至左第二磨牙，跨中线，充满腭穹隆，累及硬腭与软腭；无牙齿松动，无表面溢脓；触诊质硬、固定、无压痛、无波动感\n- E4 [opg]: 上颌咬合片与全景片均未见骨质改变\n- E5 [history]: 既往史：5年前因龋拔除26牙\n- E6 [laboratory]: 常规血液检查正常\n- E7 [clinical_exam]: 初步诊断为小唾液腺肿瘤\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] (A) maxillary occlusal radiograph; (B) panoramic radiograph\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intra-oral picture showing swelling extending from right central incisor to left second molar\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 35岁女性，主诉上颌后部肿物8个月，伴咀嚼及吞咽困难；肿物起始小，渐进性增大。 诊断意义：支持腺样囊性癌的临床病程特点\n\n2. 口内检查见单发、边界清楚肿物，前后径自右上中切牙至左第二磨牙，跨中线，充满腭穹隆，累及硬腭与软腭；触诊质硬、固定、无压痛、无波动感。 诊断意义：支持腺样囊性癌的临床表现\n\n3. 上颌咬合片与全景片均未见骨质改变。 诊断意义：排除了骨质破坏性疾病\n\n4. 初步诊断为小唾液腺肿瘤。 诊断意义：支持腺样囊性癌的可能性\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者有典型的腺样囊性癌病程和临床表现，影像学未见骨质改变，初步诊断考虑为小唾液腺肿瘤。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理学证据以明确腺样囊性癌的具体类型\n","answer":"\n腺样囊性癌（硬腭及软腭）（Adenoid Cystic Carcinoma (cribriform pattern)）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] (A) maxillary occlusal radiograph; (B) panoramic radiograph\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intra-oral picture showing swelling extending from right central incisor to left second molar\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 35岁女性，主诉上颌后部肿物8个月，伴咀嚼及吞咽困难；肿物起始小，渐进性增大。 诊断意义：支持腺样囊性癌的临床病程特点\n\n2. 口内检查见单发、边界清楚肿物，前后径自右上中切牙至左第二磨牙，跨中线，充满腭穹隆，累及硬腭与软腭；触诊质硬、固定、无压痛、无波动感。 诊断意义：支持腺样囊性癌的临床表现\n\n3. 上颌咬合片与全景片均未见骨质改变。 诊断意义：排除了骨质破坏性疾病\n\n4. 初步诊断为小唾液腺肿瘤。 诊断意义：支持腺样囊性癌的可能性\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者有典型的腺样囊性癌病程和临床表现，影像学未见骨质改变，初步诊断考虑为小唾液腺肿瘤。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理学证据以明确腺样囊性癌的具体类型\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n腺样囊性癌（硬腭及软腭）（Adenoid Cystic Carcinoma (cribriform pattern)）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC5012755/PAMJ-24-106-g002.jpg","name":"PAMJ-24-106-g002.jpg","caption":"(A) maxillary occlusal radiograph; (B) panoramic radiograph","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"82e2c40472099fc009025c11db836536d9fb70192da502886639bbb92bd9e777","width":552,"height":309},{"src":"assets/PMC5012755/PAMJ-24-106-g001.jpg","name":"PAMJ-24-106-g001.jpg","caption":"Intra-oral picture showing swelling extending from right central incisor to left second molar","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"6c36c5f564f9b5e30b2a41694683099e112242937541eda4e384dbc21a166851","width":616,"height":447}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC11880773","title":"A Novel Variant in Dentin Sialophosphoprotein (DSPP) Gene Causes Dentinogenesis Imperfecta Type III: Case Report.","category":"salivary","license":"cc by-nc","authors":["Yan Wang","Ximin Xu","Yuzhe Ding","Guohua Yuan"],"journal":"Molecular genetics & genomic medicine","year":"2025","citation":"Yan Wang, Ximin Xu, Yuzhe Ding, Guohua Yuan. A Novel Variant in Dentin Sialophosphoprotein (DSPP) Gene Causes Dentinogenesis Imperfecta Type III: Case Report. Molecular genetics & genomic medicine. 2025. doi: 10.1002/mgg3.70087.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/This is an open access article under the terms of the http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ License, which permits use, distribution and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited and is not used for commercial purposes.","copyright":["© 2025 The Author(s). Molecular Genetics & Genomic Medicine published by Wiley Periodicals LLC."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11880773/","doi":"10.1002/mgg3.70087","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [clinical_exam]: 3岁女童主诉牙齿变色与严重磨耗；口内检查见乳牙呈半透明蓝灰色（opalescent）色泽、广泛釉质缺损与重度磨耗，部分牙已露髓\n- E2 [opg]: 乳牙根尖片/全景片显示牙本质菲薄、髓腔异常扩大，呈‘壳状牙’（shell teeth）影像特征\n- E3 [rgb]: 母亲（II-2）有相似临床表现：牙齿变色与严重磨耗；其全景片显示牙根短而锥形、根管闭锁\n- E4 [history]: 无系统性表现（如成骨不全、听力损失）\n- E5 [demographics]: 家系中仅母女发病，父亲表型正常，符合常染色体显性遗传模式\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的OPG细节。\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Clinical presentation of II‐2. (A–E) Intraoral photographs of II‐2. (F) Panoramic photograph of II‐2.\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的临床照片，未提供可独立核对的诊断前放射影像。\n","think":"\n1. 3岁女童主诉牙齿变色与严重磨耗；口内检查见乳牙呈半透明蓝灰色色泽、广泛釉质缺损与重度磨耗，部分牙已露髓。 诊断意义：支持牙本质发育不全III型的诊断\n\n2. 乳牙根尖片/全景片显示牙本质菲薄、髓腔异常扩大，呈‘壳状牙’影像特征。 诊断意义：进一步支持牙本质发育不全III型的诊断\n\n3. 母亲（II-2）有相似临床表现：牙齿变色与严重磨耗；其全景片显示牙根短而锥形、根管闭锁。 诊断意义：提示家族遗传背景，符合牙本质发育不全III型的特点\n\n4. 家系中仅母女发病，父亲表型正常，符合常染色体显性遗传模式。 诊断意义：支持该病按常染色体显性方式遗传的可能性，与牙本质发育不全III型一致\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者及其母亲的典型临床表现和影像学特征，并结合家族遗传模式，支持牙本质发育不全III型的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无系统性表现如成骨不全、听力损失等，这与其他类型的牙本质发育不全区分有限。\n","answer":"\n牙本质发育不全III型（Dentinogenesis Imperfecta Type III）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的OPG细节。\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Clinical presentation of II‐2. (A–E) Intraoral photographs of II‐2. (F) Panoramic photograph of II‐2.\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的临床照片，未提供可独立核对的诊断前放射影像。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 3岁女童主诉牙齿变色与严重磨耗；口内检查见乳牙呈半透明蓝灰色色泽、广泛釉质缺损与重度磨耗，部分牙已露髓。 诊断意义：支持牙本质发育不全III型的诊断\n\n2. 乳牙根尖片/全景片显示牙本质菲薄、髓腔异常扩大，呈‘壳状牙’影像特征。 诊断意义：进一步支持牙本质发育不全III型的诊断\n\n3. 母亲（II-2）有相似临床表现：牙齿变色与严重磨耗；其全景片显示牙根短而锥形、根管闭锁。 诊断意义：提示家族遗传背景，符合牙本质发育不全III型的特点\n\n4. 家系中仅母女发病，父亲表型正常，符合常染色体显性遗传模式。 诊断意义：支持该病按常染色体显性方式遗传的可能性，与牙本质发育不全III型一致\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者及其母亲的典型临床表现和影像学特征，并结合家族遗传模式，支持牙本质发育不全III型的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无系统性表现如成骨不全、听力损失等，这与其他类型的牙本质发育不全区分有限。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n牙本质发育不全III型（Dentinogenesis Imperfecta Type III）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC11880773/MGG3-13-e70087-g004.jpg","name":"MGG3-13-e70087-g004.jpg","caption":"Clinical presentation of II‐2. (A–E) Intraoral photographs of II‐2. (F) Panoramic photograph of II‐2.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"da37e0852d77f80dbc16cb801976753b19dbc88aae7d265492a6d5ef46a2905b","width":709,"height":584}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC11909402","title":"Calcifying Odontogenic Cyst in Posterior Maxilla: A Case Report.","category":"odontogenic_cyst_tumor","license":"cc by","authors":["Farhad Ghorbani","Mohammad Amin Amiri","Mohammad Mehdi Farahmand","Saeed Afzoun","Maryam Paknahad"],"journal":"Journal of dentistry (Shiraz, Iran)","year":"2025","citation":"Farhad Ghorbani, Mohammad Amin Amiri, Mohammad Mehdi Farahmand, Saeed Afzoun, Maryam Paknahad. Calcifying Odontogenic Cyst in Posterior Maxilla: A Case Report. Journal of dentistry (Shiraz, Iran). 2025. doi: 10.30476/dentjods.2024.102636.2375.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, ( http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ ) which permits reusers to copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format if the original work is properly cited, and attribution is given to the creator. The license also permits for commercial use.","copyright":["Copyright: © Journal of Dentistry"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11909402/","doi":"10.30476/dentjods.2024.102636.2375","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 66岁女性，左上颌后区肿胀伴疼痛病史\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查见病变质地硬，部分区域有波动感\n- E3 [clinical_exam]: 左上颌第一、二前磨牙及第一磨牙冷测活力阳性\n- E4 [opg]: OPG示左上颌自第一前磨牙至第三磨牙区见边界清楚、含骨皮质的混合密度病灶\n- E5 [other_imaging]: CBCT示病灶致颊/腭侧骨皮质变薄、连续性中断，左上颌窦底抬高，鼻腔及中鼻道阻塞，左上颌第一、二磨牙缺失\n- E6 [other_imaging]: 影像学鉴别诊断包括长期存在的囊肿、骨化性纤维瘤及COC\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic view of the patient before surgery\n- [cbct/ct/radiograph] a and b: The coronal views and, c: cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) axial sections with measurement of the anteroposterior and mediolateral extensions of the cyst\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n","think":"\n1. 患者为66岁女性，左上颌后区有肿胀伴疼痛病史。 诊断意义：支持存在局部病变\n\n2. 口内检查显示病变质地硬，部分区域有波动感。 诊断意义：支持囊性或混合性质的病变\n\n3. OPG示左上颌自第一前磨牙至第三磨牙区见边界清楚、含骨皮质的混合密度病灶。 诊断意义：支持囊肿或其他局限性病变\n\n4. CBCT进一步显示病灶致颊/腭侧骨皮质变薄、连续性中断，左上颌窦底抬高，鼻腔及中鼻道阻塞，以及左上颌第一、二磨牙缺失。 诊断意义：提供更详细的解剖变化，支持COC等鉴别诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床表现和影像学特征，初步考虑为牙源性钙化囊肿，但需通过病理检查以最终确诊。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；影像学鉴别诊断包括长期存在的囊肿、骨化性纤维瘤及COC（E6），因此单凭现有证据不能完全排除其他可能。\n","answer":"\n牙源性钙化囊肿（Calcifying Odontogenic Cyst (COC)）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic view of the patient before surgery\n- [cbct/ct/radiograph] a and b: The coronal views and, c: cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) axial sections with measurement of the anteroposterior and mediolateral extensions of the cyst\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者为66岁女性，左上颌后区有肿胀伴疼痛病史。 诊断意义：支持存在局部病变\n\n2. 口内检查显示病变质地硬，部分区域有波动感。 诊断意义：支持囊性或混合性质的病变\n\n3. OPG示左上颌自第一前磨牙至第三磨牙区见边界清楚、含骨皮质的混合密度病灶。 诊断意义：支持囊肿或其他局限性病变\n\n4. CBCT进一步显示病灶致颊/腭侧骨皮质变薄、连续性中断，左上颌窦底抬高，鼻腔及中鼻道阻塞，以及左上颌第一、二磨牙缺失。 诊断意义：提供更详细的解剖变化，支持COC等鉴别诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床表现和影像学特征，初步考虑为牙源性钙化囊肿，但需通过病理检查以最终确诊。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；影像学鉴别诊断包括长期存在的囊肿、骨化性纤维瘤及COC（E6），因此单凭现有证据不能完全排除其他可能。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n牙源性钙化囊肿（Calcifying Odontogenic Cyst (COC)）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC11909402/JDS-26-88-g002.jpg","name":"JDS-26-88-g002.jpg","caption":"Panoramic view of the patient before surgery","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"0bfe32176df57ebd812d438212f046a53e1eb7a1b7ea4054030ccb4301c0eaeb","width":712,"height":300},{"src":"assets/PMC11909402/JDS-26-88-g003.jpg","name":"JDS-26-88-g003.jpg","caption":"a and b: The coronal views and, c: cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) axial sections with measurement of the anteroposterior and mediolateral extensions of the cyst","types":["cbct","ct","radiograph"],"sha256":"137ae59c4548fd5e51fb286fcde528f9de70b7e116758c378d9f26b26a41072b","width":659,"height":854}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12939484","title":"Extranodal NK/T-Cell Lymphoma, Nasal Type, Presenting as an Isolated Oral Manifestation.","category":"oral_maxillofacial_other","license":"cc by","authors":["Andrea Kanizsai","Ágnes Bán","László Kereskai","Árpád Szomor"],"journal":"Dentistry journal","year":"2026","citation":"Andrea Kanizsai, Ágnes Bán, László Kereskai, Árpád Szomor. Extranodal NK/T-Cell Lymphoma, Nasal Type, Presenting as an Isolated Oral Manifestation. Dentistry journal. 2026. doi: 10.3390/dj14020129.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland. This article is an open access article distributed under the terms and conditions of the Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) license.","copyright":["© 2026 by the authors."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12939484/","doi":"10.3390/dj14020129","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E3 [opg]: 全景片显示多发残根、严重龋坏、广泛牙槽骨吸收，以及左侧上颌牙槽突不规则溶骨性改变，对应临床受累区；影像学最初支持牙源性/炎症性病因，但无法解释进行性软组织破坏\n- E4 [symptom]: 初诊1月内出现非故意体重下降约4 kg及新发盗汗；病损持续进展且对治疗无反应，引发恶性肿瘤怀疑\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] (A) Overview of the oral cavity demonstrating severe dental neglect and inflammatory changes. (B) Close-up view of the left palatal region showing a destructive ulcerative lesion with irregular margins, pseudomembranous covering, and hemorrhagic surface, representing the primary manifestation of extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma in this case. Please note that several severely compromised maxillary teeth visible on the initial panoramic radiograph were extracted during acute dental management prior to photographic documentation; therefore, the intraoral images reflect the clinical status after initial emergency interventions.\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph (dental orthopantomogram, DOP) demonstrating extensive dental pathology and maxillary involvement. The image shows multiple residual roots, advanced carious destruction, generalized periodontal bone loss, and irregular osteolytic changes in the left maxillary alveolar process, corresponding to the clinically affected region. These findings initially supported an odontogenic and inflammatory etiology but did not fully explain the progressive, destructive soft tissue lesion.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] (A) Overview of the oral cavity demonstrating severe dental neglect and inflammatory changes. (B) Close-up view of the left palatal region showing a destructive ulcerative lesion with irregular margins, pseudomembranous covering, and hemorrhagic surface, representing the primary manifestation of extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma in this case. Please note that several severely compromised maxillary teeth visible on the initial panoramic radiograph were extracted during acute dental management prior to photographic documentation; therefore, the intraoral images reflect the clinical status after initial emergency interventions.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 全景片显示左侧上颌牙槽突不规则溶骨性改变，尽管影像学最初支持牙源性/炎症性病因，但无法解释进行性软组织破坏。 诊断意义：支持进一步考虑非典型病因，如恶性肿瘤\n\n2. 患者在初诊1月内出现非故意体重下降约4 kg及新发盗汗，提示系统性疾病或恶性肿瘤的可能。 诊断意义：支持恶性肿瘤的可能性\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者存在左侧上颌牙槽突不规则溶骨性改变且对治疗无反应，同时伴有非故意体重下降和盗汗，这些特征指向恶性肿瘤。根据临床表现和影像学特征，结外NK/T细胞淋巴瘤，鼻型是一个需要考虑的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；当前证据不足以特异性地确诊为结外NK/T细胞淋巴瘤，鼻型，仍需进一步病理检查以明确诊断\n","answer":"\n结外NK/T细胞淋巴瘤，鼻型（Extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma, nasal type (ENKTCL-NT)）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] (A) Overview of the oral cavity demonstrating severe dental neglect and inflammatory changes. (B) Close-up view of the left palatal region showing a destructive ulcerative lesion with irregular margins, pseudomembranous covering, and hemorrhagic surface, representing the primary manifestation of extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma in this case. Please note that several severely compromised maxillary teeth visible on the initial panoramic radiograph were extracted during acute dental management prior to photographic documentation; therefore, the intraoral images reflect the clinical status after initial emergency interventions.\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph (dental orthopantomogram, DOP) demonstrating extensive dental pathology and maxillary involvement. The image shows multiple residual roots, advanced carious destruction, generalized periodontal bone loss, and irregular osteolytic changes in the left maxillary alveolar process, corresponding to the clinically affected region. These findings initially supported an odontogenic and inflammatory etiology but did not fully explain the progressive, destructive soft tissue lesion.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] (A) Overview of the oral cavity demonstrating severe dental neglect and inflammatory changes. (B) Close-up view of the left palatal region showing a destructive ulcerative lesion with irregular margins, pseudomembranous covering, and hemorrhagic surface, representing the primary manifestation of extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma in this case. Please note that several severely compromised maxillary teeth visible on the initial panoramic radiograph were extracted during acute dental management prior to photographic documentation; therefore, the intraoral images reflect the clinical status after initial emergency interventions.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 全景片显示左侧上颌牙槽突不规则溶骨性改变，尽管影像学最初支持牙源性/炎症性病因，但无法解释进行性软组织破坏。 诊断意义：支持进一步考虑非典型病因，如恶性肿瘤\n\n2. 患者在初诊1月内出现非故意体重下降约4 kg及新发盗汗，提示系统性疾病或恶性肿瘤的可能。 诊断意义：支持恶性肿瘤的可能性\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者存在左侧上颌牙槽突不规则溶骨性改变且对治疗无反应，同时伴有非故意体重下降和盗汗，这些特征指向恶性肿瘤。根据临床表现和影像学特征，结外NK/T细胞淋巴瘤，鼻型是一个需要考虑的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；当前证据不足以特异性地确诊为结外NK/T细胞淋巴瘤，鼻型，仍需进一步病理检查以明确诊断\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n结外NK/T细胞淋巴瘤，鼻型（Extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma, nasal type (ENKTCL-NT)）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12939484/dentistry-14-00129-g001.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00129-g001.jpg","caption":"(A) Overview of the oral cavity demonstrating severe dental neglect and inflammatory changes. (B) Close-up view of the left palatal region showing a destructive ulcerative lesion with irregular margins, pseudomembranous covering, and hemorrhagic surface, representing the primary manifestation of extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma in this case. Please note that several severely compromised maxillary teeth visible on the initial panoramic radiograph were extracted during acute dental management prior to photographic documentation; therefore, the intraoral images reflect the clinical status after initial emergency interventions.","types":["intraoral_photo","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"c19f202f2f198b749eb54de407d08be0e368205a4fe1ef6b659c797a608d6a91","width":779,"height":1427},{"src":"assets/PMC12939484/dentistry-14-00129-g002.jpg","name":"dentistry-14-00129-g002.jpg","caption":"Panoramic radiograph (dental orthopantomogram, DOP) demonstrating extensive dental pathology and maxillary involvement. The image shows multiple residual roots, advanced carious destruction, generalized periodontal bone loss, and irregular osteolytic changes in the left maxillary alveolar process, corresponding to the clinically affected region. These findings initially supported an odontogenic and inflammatory etiology but did not fully explain the progressive, destructive soft tissue lesion.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"8104eab4fd90709487d418d80e897aac50d5eda1fec36b868357b7a8a33c0be1","width":790,"height":405}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12397749","title":"Cleidocranial Dysplasia With Multiple Impacted Teeth and Dentigerous Cysts: A Case Report of a Rare Entity.","category":"developmental_eruption","license":"cc by","authors":["Manhar Shinh"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2025","citation":"Manhar Shinh. Cleidocranial Dysplasia With Multiple Impacted Teeth and Dentigerous Cysts: A Case Report of a Rare Entity. Cureus. 2025. doi: 10.7759/cureus.89098.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025, Shinh et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12397749/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.89098","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 27岁男性，主诉上颌前牙区自幼缺牙，近5月伴脓性分泌物\n- E8 [laboratory]: 血常规正常；碱性磷酸酶轻度升高；钙、维生素D正常，排除低磷血症性佝偻病等代谢性骨病\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic features(A) Orthopantomogram (OPG) revealing multiple retained deciduous, impacted permanent, and supernumerary teeth (white arrows), with radiolucency (red arrows) indicating cystic changes. (B) Paranasal sinus (PNS) view showing underdeveloped sinuses and increased sutural markings on the skull. (C) Lateral cephalogram displaying a hypoplastic maxilla, prognathic mandible, numerous impacted teeth, and delayed cranial suture closure (white arrow). (D) Posteroanterior skull radiograph showing open cranial sutures and fontanelles (white arrow)\n- [radiograph] Chest X-ray showing bilateral hypoplastic clavicles (white arrows), a characteristic feature of cleidocranial dysplasia\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral examination(A) Maxillary arch showing multiple missing teeth. (B) Mandibular arch with multiple missing teeth\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 27岁男性，主诉上颌前牙区自幼缺牙，近5月伴脓性分泌物。 诊断意义：支持锁骨颅骨发育不全的诊断，因为该病常伴有牙齿发育异常。\n\n2. 血常规正常；碱性磷酸酶轻度升高；钙、维生素D正常，排除低磷血症性佝偻病等代谢性骨病。 诊断意义：进一步排除其他可能引起类似症状的代谢性骨病，支持锁骨颅骨发育不全的诊断。\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者自幼存在上颌前牙区缺牙，结合实验室检查结果排除了其他代谢性骨病，支持锁骨颅骨发育不全的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有证据不足以完全区分所有可能导致牙齿缺失的原因，需要更多影像学及家族史信息来明确诊断。\n","answer":"\n锁骨颅骨发育不全（Cleidocranial Dysplasia）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic features(A) Orthopantomogram (OPG) revealing multiple retained deciduous, impacted permanent, and supernumerary teeth (white arrows), with radiolucency (red arrows) indicating cystic changes. (B) Paranasal sinus (PNS) view showing underdeveloped sinuses and increased sutural markings on the skull. (C) Lateral cephalogram displaying a hypoplastic maxilla, prognathic mandible, numerous impacted teeth, and delayed cranial suture closure (white arrow). (D) Posteroanterior skull radiograph showing open cranial sutures and fontanelles (white arrow)\n- [radiograph] Chest X-ray showing bilateral hypoplastic clavicles (white arrows), a characteristic feature of cleidocranial dysplasia\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral examination(A) Maxillary arch showing multiple missing teeth. (B) Mandibular arch with multiple missing teeth\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 27岁男性，主诉上颌前牙区自幼缺牙，近5月伴脓性分泌物。 诊断意义：支持锁骨颅骨发育不全的诊断，因为该病常伴有牙齿发育异常。\n\n2. 血常规正常；碱性磷酸酶轻度升高；钙、维生素D正常，排除低磷血症性佝偻病等代谢性骨病。 诊断意义：进一步排除其他可能引起类似症状的代谢性骨病，支持锁骨颅骨发育不全的诊断。\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者自幼存在上颌前牙区缺牙，结合实验室检查结果排除了其他代谢性骨病，支持锁骨颅骨发育不全的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有证据不足以完全区分所有可能导致牙齿缺失的原因，需要更多影像学及家族史信息来明确诊断。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n锁骨颅骨发育不全（Cleidocranial Dysplasia）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12397749/cureus-0017-00000089098-i03.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000089098-i03.jpg","caption":"Radiographic features(A) Orthopantomogram (OPG) revealing multiple retained deciduous, impacted permanent, and supernumerary teeth (white arrows), with radiolucency (red arrows) indicating cystic changes. (B) Paranasal sinus (PNS) view showing underdeveloped sinuses and increased sutural markings on the skull. (C) Lateral cephalogram displaying a hypoplastic maxilla, prognathic mandible, numerous impacted teeth, and delayed cranial suture closure (white arrow). (D) Posteroanterior skull radiograph showing open cranial sutures and fontanelles (white arrow)","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"be8bee57a0e5173585fa17eeb092aabf59fbb5bff7b645aaa0855999810277f3","width":750,"height":654},{"src":"assets/PMC12397749/cureus-0017-00000089098-i02.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000089098-i02.jpg","caption":"Intraoral examination(A) Maxillary arch showing multiple missing teeth. (B) Mandibular arch with multiple missing teeth","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"b13aee956802e327fa096d92b7d023459da4a11dba707de8b4c200507c165cfa","width":750,"height":240},{"src":"assets/PMC12397749/cureus-0017-00000089098-i04.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000089098-i04.jpg","caption":"Chest X-ray showing bilateral hypoplastic clavicles (white arrows), a characteristic feature of cleidocranial dysplasia","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"0df7f8a19961d26e67d33aa567634403c230684702e70475e17b9e3d38c45545","width":750,"height":843}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12263011","title":"Generalized gingival enlargement, periodontitis, and osteonecrosis of the jaw as manifestations of IgG4-related disease: A rare case report.","category":"periodontal","license":"cc by","authors":["Jie Zhao","Yufeng Ling","Lingying Niu","Lei Zhang","Liangyuan Lin","Juan Wu"],"journal":"Medicine","year":"2025","citation":"Jie Zhao, Yufeng Ling, Lingying Niu, Lei Zhang, Liangyuan Lin, Juan Wu. Generalized gingival enlargement, periodontitis, and osteonecrosis of the jaw as manifestations of IgG4-related disease: A rare case report. Medicine. 2025. doi: 10.1097/md.0000000000043260.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License 4.0 (CCBY), which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025 the Author(s). Published by Wolters Kluwer Health, Inc."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12263011/","doi":"10.1097/md.0000000000043260","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 44岁男性，主诉5年进行性牙龈增生与牙齿松动；既往多次牙周非手术与手术治疗（包括多轮龈切除术），但牙龈增生反复复发\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [ct/opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram and spiral computed tomography images of the patient. (A, B) Images obtained at different times demonstrate rapidly progressing alveolar bone resorption and missing teeth. (C, D) Alveolar bone necrosis on teeth 33 to 35. Yellow arrow: Alveolar bone necrosis.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Oral photographs of the patient taken at different times. (A, B, C) Oral photographs taken before he was referred to our hospital. (D, E) Oral photographs taken after he was referred to our department. (A) Generalized gingival enlargement (February 2019) that appeared spherical, sessile, and involved marginal and attached gingiva and papilla. The involved gingivae were edematous, rubbery, pink, soft, elastic, and bled easily. (B, C) At 6 and 7 mo, after periodontal flap surgery and gingivectomy on teeth 34 to 47, significant gingival hyperplasia recurrence was noted on teeth 43 to 47. (D) Intraoral photographs of the patient at first examination: oral hygiene was extremely poor, with a mass of dental plaque and calculus covering almost all remaining teeth. Generalized gingival enlargement presented as dusky red, swollen, soft, and bled easily. (E) After most of the supragingival and subgingival calculus had been removed, intraoral examination revealed localized alveolar bone necrosis in the mandible (teeth 33–35 area). Yellow arrow: Alveolar bone necrosis.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 44岁男性，主诉5年进行性牙龈增生与牙齿松动 诊断意义：支持IgG4相关疾病（累及牙龈、牙周及颌骨）\n\n2. 既往多次牙周非手术与手术治疗（包括多轮龈切除术），但牙龈增生反复复发 诊断意义：支持IgG4相关疾病（累及牙龈、牙周及颌骨）\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者长期存在牙龈增生与牙齿松动症状，并且在经过多种牙周治疗方法后仍反复复发，提示可能为IgG4相关疾病。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有证据不足以特异性区分IgG4相关疾病与其他可能导致牙龈增生和牙齿松动的疾病\n","answer":"\nIgG4相关疾病（累及牙龈、牙周及颌骨）（IgG4-related disease）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [ct/opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram and spiral computed tomography images of the patient. (A, B) Images obtained at different times demonstrate rapidly progressing alveolar bone resorption and missing teeth. (C, D) Alveolar bone necrosis on teeth 33 to 35. Yellow arrow: Alveolar bone necrosis.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Oral photographs of the patient taken at different times. (A, B, C) Oral photographs taken before he was referred to our hospital. (D, E) Oral photographs taken after he was referred to our department. (A) Generalized gingival enlargement (February 2019) that appeared spherical, sessile, and involved marginal and attached gingiva and papilla. The involved gingivae were edematous, rubbery, pink, soft, elastic, and bled easily. (B, C) At 6 and 7 mo, after periodontal flap surgery and gingivectomy on teeth 34 to 47, significant gingival hyperplasia recurrence was noted on teeth 43 to 47. (D) Intraoral photographs of the patient at first examination: oral hygiene was extremely poor, with a mass of dental plaque and calculus covering almost all remaining teeth. Generalized gingival enlargement presented as dusky red, swollen, soft, and bled easily. (E) After most of the supragingival and subgingival calculus had been removed, intraoral examination revealed localized alveolar bone necrosis in the mandible (teeth 33–35 area). Yellow arrow: Alveolar bone necrosis.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 44岁男性，主诉5年进行性牙龈增生与牙齿松动 诊断意义：支持IgG4相关疾病（累及牙龈、牙周及颌骨）\n\n2. 既往多次牙周非手术与手术治疗（包括多轮龈切除术），但牙龈增生反复复发 诊断意义：支持IgG4相关疾病（累及牙龈、牙周及颌骨）\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者长期存在牙龈增生与牙齿松动症状，并且在经过多种牙周治疗方法后仍反复复发，提示可能为IgG4相关疾病。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有证据不足以特异性区分IgG4相关疾病与其他可能导致牙龈增生和牙齿松动的疾病\n</Think>\n<Answer>\nIgG4相关疾病（累及牙龈、牙周及颌骨）（IgG4-related disease）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12263011/medi-104-e43260-g001.jpg","name":"medi-104-e43260-g001.jpg","caption":"Orthopantomogram and spiral computed tomography images of the patient. (A, B) Images obtained at different times demonstrate rapidly progressing alveolar bone resorption and missing teeth. (C, D) Alveolar bone necrosis on teeth 33 to 35. Yellow arrow: Alveolar bone necrosis.","types":["ct","opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"e289594ed49473038bff2c5273f55a57a1f50ae7ad85f3c04c9909464d0c1a72","width":800,"height":618},{"src":"assets/PMC12263011/medi-104-e43260-g002.jpg","name":"medi-104-e43260-g002.jpg","caption":"Oral photographs of the patient taken at different times. (A, B, C) Oral photographs taken before he was referred to our hospital. (D, E) Oral photographs taken after he was referred to our department. (A) Generalized gingival enlargement (February 2019) that appeared spherical, sessile, and involved marginal and attached gingiva and papilla. The involved gingivae were edematous, rubbery, pink, soft, elastic, and bled easily. (B, C) At 6 and 7 mo, after periodontal flap surgery and gingivectomy on teeth 34 to 47, significant gingival hyperplasia recurrence was noted on teeth 43 to 47. (D) Intraoral photographs of the patient at first examination: oral hygiene was extremely poor, with a mass of dental plaque and calculus covering almost all remaining teeth. Generalized gingival enlargement presented as dusky red, swollen, soft, and bled easily. (E) After most of the supragingival and subgingival calculus had been removed, intraoral examination revealed localized alveolar bone necrosis in the mandible (teeth 33–35 area). Yellow arrow: Alveolar bone necrosis.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"9281262428e249643872710946c55d61154f16c55a3e585337895c82ed213b86","width":800,"height":450}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC7714592","title":"Multimodular Assessment of a Traumatic Bone Cyst Overlapped with Apical Periodontitis.","category":"endodontic_periapical","license":"cc by","authors":["Davide Musu","Giulia Bardini","Hagay Shemesh","Claudia Dettori","Elisabetta Cotti"],"journal":"Case reports in dentistry","year":"2020","citation":"Davide Musu, Giulia Bardini, Hagay Shemesh, Claudia Dettori, Elisabetta Cotti. Multimodular Assessment of a Traumatic Bone Cyst Overlapped with Apical Periodontitis. Case reports in dentistry. 2020. doi: 10.1155/2020/8829305.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2020 Davide Musu et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7714592/","doi":"10.1155/2020/8829305","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 临床检查：无颊舌侧骨膨隆、无淋巴结肿大、黏膜完整；右下第一磨牙无症状；右下第二磨牙无症状、冠完整、冷热测试正常\n- E3 [opg]: 全景片显示：右下第一、二磨牙间见边界清楚单房溶骨性病变，伴硬化边缘，累及下牙槽神经走行区；第一磨牙根管治疗不完善，远中根尖1/3有吸收并位于病变内\n- E6 [other_imaging]: 术前诊断：右下颌非根尖源性囊性病变（第一、二磨牙区）+ 第一磨牙根尖周炎（既往治疗失败伴根尖穿孔）\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph/ultrasound] Images of the 27-year-old patient presenting an extensive asymptomatic lesion of the right posterior mandible. (a) The panoramic radiograph shows a well-defined unilocular osteolytic lesion with sclerotic margins located between the two molar teeth and superimposed on the alveolar inferior nerve. (b) The periapical radiograph of the first molar depicting inadequate root canal treatment with signs of perforation in the apical third of the distal root involved in the osteolytic lesion. (c) B-mode ultrasound examination showing a transonic lesion (arrows). (d) Power-Doppler image showing the presence of peripheral vascularity.\n- [cbct] (a) CBCT revealing a well-defined unilocular lesion between the second and first right mandibular molars. (b) Sagittal view showing the expansion of the lesion toward the lingual wall and the consequent thinning of the lingual plate. (c) Axial section showing a perforation in the distal and lingual aspects of the apical third of the distal root of the right first molar. (d) The main osteolytic lesion appears in continuity with the perforation in the distal root of the right mandibular first molar.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n","think":"\n1. 右下第一、二磨牙间见边界清楚单房溶骨性病变，伴硬化边缘，累及下牙槽神经走行区。 诊断意义：支持创伤性骨囊肿的诊断\n\n2. 第一磨牙根管治疗不完善，远中根尖1/3有吸收并位于病变内。 诊断意义：支持合并根尖周炎的诊断\n\n3. 临床检查未见明显症状或异常体征，如颊舌侧骨膨隆、淋巴结肿大等。 诊断意义：进一步支持创伤性骨囊肿而非其他更具侵袭性的病变\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据影像学表现和临床检查结果，患者右下颌存在非根尖源性囊性病变（符合创伤性骨囊肿特征），同时伴有因既往治疗失败导致的第一磨牙根尖周炎。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无法通过现有证据完全排除其他类型的非根尖源性囊性病变\n","answer":"\n创伤性骨囊肿合并根尖周炎（Traumatic bone cyst overlapping with apical periodontitis）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph/ultrasound] Images of the 27-year-old patient presenting an extensive asymptomatic lesion of the right posterior mandible. (a) The panoramic radiograph shows a well-defined unilocular osteolytic lesion with sclerotic margins located between the two molar teeth and superimposed on the alveolar inferior nerve. (b) The periapical radiograph of the first molar depicting inadequate root canal treatment with signs of perforation in the apical third of the distal root involved in the osteolytic lesion. (c) B-mode ultrasound examination showing a transonic lesion (arrows). (d) Power-Doppler image showing the presence of peripheral vascularity.\n- [cbct] (a) CBCT revealing a well-defined unilocular lesion between the second and first right mandibular molars. (b) Sagittal view showing the expansion of the lesion toward the lingual wall and the consequent thinning of the lingual plate. (c) Axial section showing a perforation in the distal and lingual aspects of the apical third of the distal root of the right first molar. (d) The main osteolytic lesion appears in continuity with the perforation in the distal root of the right mandibular first molar.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 右下第一、二磨牙间见边界清楚单房溶骨性病变，伴硬化边缘，累及下牙槽神经走行区。 诊断意义：支持创伤性骨囊肿的诊断\n\n2. 第一磨牙根管治疗不完善，远中根尖1/3有吸收并位于病变内。 诊断意义：支持合并根尖周炎的诊断\n\n3. 临床检查未见明显症状或异常体征，如颊舌侧骨膨隆、淋巴结肿大等。 诊断意义：进一步支持创伤性骨囊肿而非其他更具侵袭性的病变\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据影像学表现和临床检查结果，患者右下颌存在非根尖源性囊性病变（符合创伤性骨囊肿特征），同时伴有因既往治疗失败导致的第一磨牙根尖周炎。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无法通过现有证据完全排除其他类型的非根尖源性囊性病变\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n创伤性骨囊肿合并根尖周炎（Traumatic bone cyst overlapping with apical periodontitis）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC7714592/CRID2020-8829305.001.jpg","name":"CRID2020-8829305.001.jpg","caption":"Images of the 27-year-old patient presenting an extensive asymptomatic lesion of the right posterior mandible. (a) The panoramic radiograph shows a well-defined unilocular osteolytic lesion with sclerotic margins located between the two molar teeth and superimposed on the alveolar inferior nerve. (b) The periapical radiograph of the first molar depicting inadequate root canal treatment with signs of perforation in the apical third of the distal root involved in the osteolytic lesion. (c) B-mode ultrasound examination showing a transonic lesion (arrows). (d) Power-Doppler image showing the presence of peripheral vascularity.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph","ultrasound"],"sha256":"987a2e4b0e920f177bb933d43bab700f749dde966ec62e9ef487713876c86328","width":697,"height":504},{"src":"assets/PMC7714592/CRID2020-8829305.002.jpg","name":"CRID2020-8829305.002.jpg","caption":"(a) CBCT revealing a well-defined unilocular lesion between the second and first right mandibular molars. (b) Sagittal view showing the expansion of the lesion toward the lingual wall and the consequent thinning of the lingual plate. (c) Axial section showing a perforation in the distal and lingual aspects of the apical third of the distal root of the right first molar. (d) The main osteolytic lesion appears in continuity with the perforation in the distal root of the right mandibular first molar.","types":["cbct"],"sha256":"b8808ff221b55933add51c6fc1bdc5b01da877292e8b2d066961620d718ccc72","width":602,"height":434}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12575408","title":"Interim Acrylic Plug-Type Obturator Prosthesis Following Marsupialization of a Maxillary Dentigerous Cyst in an Adolescent: A Case Report.","category":"implant_prosthetic","license":"cc by","authors":["Chandrama Pratap","Rishabh Khare","Chingkheinganbi Nameirakpam","Sarjubala Nongthombam"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2025","citation":"Chandrama Pratap, Rishabh Khare, Chingkheinganbi Nameirakpam, Sarjubala Nongthombam. Interim Acrylic Plug-Type Obturator Prosthesis Following Marsupialization of a Maxillary Dentigerous Cyst in an Adolescent: A Case Report. Cureus. 2025. doi: 10.7759/cureus.93603.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025, Pratap et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12575408/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.93603","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history|demographics|symptom|clinical_exam]: 16岁男性，主诉左侧上颌前部无痛性肿胀；临床见左上唇区轻度面部不对称、质硬肿胀，口内左侧上颌尖牙区颊侧骨板膨隆，黏膜完整\n- E2 [opg]: OPG显示左侧上颌区边界清晰的单房透射影，包绕未萌出的左上尖牙牙冠，伴皮质缘、邻牙移位及累及上颌窦底\n- E3 [laboratory]: 细针穿刺细胞学（FNAC）示良性囊性病变，含上皮细胞簇与黏液样背景\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram (OPG) showing well-defined unilocular radiolucency in the left maxillary regionA well-defined unilocular radiolucency in the left maxillary region, associated with an unerupted maxillary canine. The lesion shows corticated borders, displacement of adjacent teeth, and extension into the floor of the maxillary sinus, consistent with the features of a dentigerous cyst in the upper left tooth region.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n","think":"\n1. 患者主诉左侧上颌前部无痛性肿胀，临床检查发现左上唇区轻度面部不对称、质硬肿胀，口内左侧上颌尖牙区颊侧骨板膨隆，提示该区域存在局部病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. OPG影像学显示左侧上颌区边界清晰的单房透射影，包绕未萌出的左上尖牙牙冠，并伴有皮质缘及邻牙移位现象，这是含牙囊肿常见的影像学特征。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 细针穿刺细胞学（FNAC）结果示良性囊性病变，包含上皮细胞簇与黏液样背景，进一步指向了囊性病变为非恶性性质，符合含牙囊肿的病理表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的临床症状、影像学特点以及细胞学检查结果，可以推断出含牙囊肿的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏组织病理学确诊，不能完全排除其他类型的囊肿\n","answer":"\n含牙囊肿（dentigerous cyst）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram (OPG) showing well-defined unilocular radiolucency in the left maxillary regionA well-defined unilocular radiolucency in the left maxillary region, associated with an unerupted maxillary canine. The lesion shows corticated borders, displacement of adjacent teeth, and extension into the floor of the maxillary sinus, consistent with the features of a dentigerous cyst in the upper left tooth region.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者主诉左侧上颌前部无痛性肿胀，临床检查发现左上唇区轻度面部不对称、质硬肿胀，口内左侧上颌尖牙区颊侧骨板膨隆，提示该区域存在局部病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. OPG影像学显示左侧上颌区边界清晰的单房透射影，包绕未萌出的左上尖牙牙冠，并伴有皮质缘及邻牙移位现象，这是含牙囊肿常见的影像学特征。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 细针穿刺细胞学（FNAC）结果示良性囊性病变，包含上皮细胞簇与黏液样背景，进一步指向了囊性病变为非恶性性质，符合含牙囊肿的病理表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的临床症状、影像学特点以及细胞学检查结果，可以推断出含牙囊肿的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏组织病理学确诊，不能完全排除其他类型的囊肿\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n含牙囊肿（dentigerous cyst）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12575408/cureus-0017-00000093603-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000093603-i01.jpg","caption":"Orthopantomogram (OPG) showing well-defined unilocular radiolucency in the left maxillary regionA well-defined unilocular radiolucency in the left maxillary region, associated with an unerupted maxillary canine. The lesion shows corticated borders, displacement of adjacent teeth, and extension into the floor of the maxillary sinus, consistent with the features of a dentigerous cyst in the upper left tooth region.","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"8ed066b37c411be2d6effeec991c8def7c5ea3f8b2ea02db96522e99329fa164","width":750,"height":494}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC4319327","title":"Hypohidrotic ectodermal dysplasia with ankylosis of temporomandibular joint and cleft palate: A rare presentation.","category":"mucosal_oral_lesion","license":"cc by-nc-sa","authors":["Manisha Goyal","Gaurav Pradhan","Sunita Gupta","Seema Kapoor"],"journal":"Contemporary clinical dentistry","year":"2015","citation":"Manisha Goyal, Gaurav Pradhan, Sunita Gupta, Seema Kapoor. Hypohidrotic ectodermal dysplasia with ankylosis of temporomandibular joint and cleft palate: A rare presentation. Contemporary clinical dentistry. 2015. doi: 10.4103/0976-237x.149304.","license_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0","licenseUrls":["http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution-Noncommercial-Share Alike 3.0 Unported, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright: © Contemporary Clinical Dentistry"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4319327/","doi":"10.4103/0976-237x.149304","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口腔检查见双侧颞下颌关节强直、后部腭裂；术前已行双侧TMJ融合松解术及部分腭裂修复术\n- E4 [clinical_exam]: 眼干、泪液减少；角膜干燥\n- E7 [history]: 婴儿期多次高热史；母亲观察到夏季体温升高、出汗不足\n- E10 [laboratory]: 家族中无类似病史；常规生化、骨骼摄片、心脏超声、腹部超声均正常\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram shows malformed and impacted incisors and molars with true partial anodontia\n- [ct] Computed tomography face and neck shows posterior cleft palate. (a) Coronal reconstruction image (b) sagittal section\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo/intraoral_photo] (a) Extraoral photograph showing characteristic features of ectodermal dysplasia. (b) Intraoral view shows hypodontia and cleft palate\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 口腔检查见双侧颞下颌关节强直、后部腭裂，支持无汗型外胚层发育不良伴颞下颌关节强直及腭裂的诊断。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 眼干、泪液减少以及角膜干燥符合无汗型外胚层发育不良的眼部表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 婴儿期多次高热史和夏季体温升高、出汗不足提示患者存在汗腺功能障碍，与无汗型外胚层发育不良相符。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据口腔检查发现的颞下颌关节强直和腭裂（E2），结合眼部症状（E4）和汗腺功能异常的历史（E7），支持无汗型外胚层发育不良（X连锁隐性遗传型）伴颞下颌关节强直及腭裂的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；家族中无类似病史（E10），未能通过家族史进一步确认遗传模式。\n","answer":"\n无汗型外胚层发育不良（X连锁隐性遗传型）伴颞下颌关节强直及腭裂（Hypohidrotic ectodermal dysplasia with ankylosis of temporomandibular joint and cleft palate）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram shows malformed and impacted incisors and molars with true partial anodontia\n- [ct] Computed tomography face and neck shows posterior cleft palate. (a) Coronal reconstruction image (b) sagittal section\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo/intraoral_photo] (a) Extraoral photograph showing characteristic features of ectodermal dysplasia. (b) Intraoral view shows hypodontia and cleft palate\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 口腔检查见双侧颞下颌关节强直、后部腭裂，支持无汗型外胚层发育不良伴颞下颌关节强直及腭裂的诊断。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 眼干、泪液减少以及角膜干燥符合无汗型外胚层发育不良的眼部表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 婴儿期多次高热史和夏季体温升高、出汗不足提示患者存在汗腺功能障碍，与无汗型外胚层发育不良相符。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据口腔检查发现的颞下颌关节强直和腭裂（E2），结合眼部症状（E4）和汗腺功能异常的历史（E7），支持无汗型外胚层发育不良（X连锁隐性遗传型）伴颞下颌关节强直及腭裂的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；家族中无类似病史（E10），未能通过家族史进一步确认遗传模式。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n无汗型外胚层发育不良（X连锁隐性遗传型）伴颞下颌关节强直及腭裂（Hypohidrotic ectodermal dysplasia with ankylosis of temporomandibular joint and cleft palate）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC4319327/CCD-6-110-g003.jpg","name":"CCD-6-110-g003.jpg","caption":"Orthopantomogram shows malformed and impacted incisors and molars with true partial anodontia","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"ca30a12d090d1804328703f71a5ebfb5c90aa913a94bab85b205537f06f7058d","width":539,"height":231},{"src":"assets/PMC4319327/CCD-6-110-g002.jpg","name":"CCD-6-110-g002.jpg","caption":"(a) Extraoral photograph showing characteristic features of ectodermal dysplasia. (b) Intraoral view shows hypodontia and cleft palate","types":["extraoral_photo","intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"2247c90496351a9287f44476c241525cb81bcac86fc909d608cf84342850a965","width":539,"height":362},{"src":"assets/PMC4319327/CCD-6-110-g001.jpg","name":"CCD-6-110-g001.jpg","caption":"Computed tomography face and neck shows posterior cleft palate. (a) Coronal reconstruction image (b) sagittal section","types":["ct"],"sha256":"9d31a59c13177f0a1f7fc77b8044286c826f0add4166e7a021460e745fc8fa09","width":539,"height":225}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC13124219","title":"Microstructures and mechanical characteristics of primary teeth affected by regional odontodysplasia.","category":"oral_maxillofacial_other","license":"cc by","authors":["Wenxiang Jiang","Minjian Shen","Jian Wang","Mengyao Bian","Haiyan Zheng","Zihuai Zhou","Ying Shi","Zhifang Wu"],"journal":"Journal of applied oral science : revista FOB","year":"2026","citation":"Wenxiang Jiang, Minjian Shen, Jian Wang, Mengyao Bian, Haiyan Zheng, Zihuai Zhou, Ying Shi, Zhifang Wu. Microstructures and mechanical characteristics of primary teeth affected by regional odontodysplasia. Journal of applied oral science : revista FOB. 2026. doi: 10.1590/1678-7765-2025-0499.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ This is an Open Access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":[],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13124219/","doi":"10.1590/1678-7765-2025-0499","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 4岁女童主诉牙齿松动与疼痛；父母报告下颌右侧前牙萌出延迟、反复牙龈肿胀1年；无家族牙异常史；母亲孕期早期曾使用避孕药（具体药物不详）\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查：下颌右侧乳前牙（81–83）呈黄染、冠小、表面粗糙；81与82度III级松动伴牙龈瘘管\n- E3 [opg]: 曲面断层片与根尖片显示81–84牙釉质与牙本质薄而低矿化、髓腔宽大、牙根短；84曾行活髓切断术并充填；恒牙胚（41–45）发育延迟；右侧下颌骨密度降低\n- E5 [opg]: 曲面断层片与CBCT显示54、55牙根吸收及根尖周透射影；恒牙14–17冠径减小、釉质与牙本质层变薄、矿化度降低、髓腔扩大、发育迟缓（较对侧）\n- E6 [rgb]: 图1a-b中白箭头标示受累乳牙，箭头标示可能受累恒牙胚；图2c显示16腭侧黄染与发育不良，为ROD特征性表现\n- E7 [rgb]: 图2c Palatal view highlighting the hypoplastic and yellowish discoloration of tooth 16, a characteristic ROD feature.\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [cbct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic and clinical presentation of a 9-year-old girl with ROD in the maxillary right quadrant. (a-c) Intraoral findings: (a) Buccal view showing severe caries and gingival inflammation associated with teeth 54 and 55. (b) Frontal occlusal view showing the overall dental status. (c) Palatal view highlighting the hypoplastic and yellowish discoloration of tooth 16, a characteristic ROD feature. (d, e) Radiographic evaluation: (d) Panoramic radiograph and (e) CBCT scan revealing root resorption and periapical radiolucency in primary teeth 54 and 55 (indicated by arrows). Permanent teeth 14 to 17 exhibit reduced crown size, thinner enamel and dentin layers, lower mineral density, and delayed developmental stages compared with their contralateral counterparts.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [cbct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic and clinical presentation of a 9-year-old girl with ROD in the maxillary right quadrant. (a-c) Intraoral findings: (a) Buccal view showing severe caries and gingival inflammation associated with teeth 54 and 55. (b) Frontal occlusal view showing the overall dental status. (c) Palatal view highlighting the hypoplastic and yellowish discoloration of tooth 16, a characteristic ROD feature. (d, e) Radiographic evaluation: (d) Panoramic radiograph and (e) CBCT scan revealing root resorption and periapical radiolucency in primary teeth 54 and 55 (indicated by arrows). Permanent teeth 14 to 17 exhibit reduced crown size, thinner enamel and dentin layers, lower mineral density, and delayed developmental stages compared with their contralateral counterparts.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 4岁女童主诉牙齿松动与疼痛，下颌右侧前牙萌出延迟、反复牙龈肿胀1年。 诊断意义：支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断\n\n2. 口内检查发现下颌右侧乳前牙（81–83）呈黄染、冠小、表面粗糙；81与82度III级松动伴牙龈瘘管。 诊断意义：支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断\n\n3. 影像学显示81–84牙釉质与牙本质薄而低矿化、髓腔宽大、牙根短；恒牙胚（41–45）发育延迟；右侧下颌骨密度降低。 诊断意义：支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断\n\n4. 图2c显示16腭侧黄染与发育不良，为ROD特征性表现。 诊断意义：支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据病史、临床检查及影像学特征，支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无家族牙异常史，但不能排除遗传因素\n","answer":"\n局灶性牙发育不全（Regional odontodysplasia）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [cbct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic and clinical presentation of a 9-year-old girl with ROD in the maxillary right quadrant. (a-c) Intraoral findings: (a) Buccal view showing severe caries and gingival inflammation associated with teeth 54 and 55. (b) Frontal occlusal view showing the overall dental status. (c) Palatal view highlighting the hypoplastic and yellowish discoloration of tooth 16, a characteristic ROD feature. (d, e) Radiographic evaluation: (d) Panoramic radiograph and (e) CBCT scan revealing root resorption and periapical radiolucency in primary teeth 54 and 55 (indicated by arrows). Permanent teeth 14 to 17 exhibit reduced crown size, thinner enamel and dentin layers, lower mineral density, and delayed developmental stages compared with their contralateral counterparts.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [cbct/intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic and clinical presentation of a 9-year-old girl with ROD in the maxillary right quadrant. (a-c) Intraoral findings: (a) Buccal view showing severe caries and gingival inflammation associated with teeth 54 and 55. (b) Frontal occlusal view showing the overall dental status. (c) Palatal view highlighting the hypoplastic and yellowish discoloration of tooth 16, a characteristic ROD feature. (d, e) Radiographic evaluation: (d) Panoramic radiograph and (e) CBCT scan revealing root resorption and periapical radiolucency in primary teeth 54 and 55 (indicated by arrows). Permanent teeth 14 to 17 exhibit reduced crown size, thinner enamel and dentin layers, lower mineral density, and delayed developmental stages compared with their contralateral counterparts.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 4岁女童主诉牙齿松动与疼痛，下颌右侧前牙萌出延迟、反复牙龈肿胀1年。 诊断意义：支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断\n\n2. 口内检查发现下颌右侧乳前牙（81–83）呈黄染、冠小、表面粗糙；81与82度III级松动伴牙龈瘘管。 诊断意义：支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断\n\n3. 影像学显示81–84牙釉质与牙本质薄而低矿化、髓腔宽大、牙根短；恒牙胚（41–45）发育延迟；右侧下颌骨密度降低。 诊断意义：支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断\n\n4. 图2c显示16腭侧黄染与发育不良，为ROD特征性表现。 诊断意义：支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据病史、临床检查及影像学特征，支持局灶性牙发育不全的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无家族牙异常史，但不能排除遗传因素\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n局灶性牙发育不全（Regional odontodysplasia）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC13124219/1678-7757-jaos-34-e20250499-gf02.jpg","name":"1678-7757-jaos-34-e20250499-gf02.jpg","caption":"Radiographic and clinical presentation of a 9-year-old girl with ROD in the maxillary right quadrant. (a-c) Intraoral findings: (a) Buccal view showing severe caries and gingival inflammation associated with teeth 54 and 55. (b) Frontal occlusal view showing the overall dental status. (c) Palatal view highlighting the hypoplastic and yellowish discoloration of tooth 16, a characteristic ROD feature. (d, e) Radiographic evaluation: (d) Panoramic radiograph and (e) CBCT scan revealing root resorption and periapical radiolucency in primary teeth 54 and 55 (indicated by arrows). Permanent teeth 14 to 17 exhibit reduced crown size, thinner enamel and dentin layers, lower mineral density, and delayed developmental stages compared with their contralateral counterparts.","types":["cbct","intraoral_photo","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"b92e2251e2586ba5a2c19c69142f289faaacc4630c4f4fa4ca08535f448d7e78","width":600,"height":331}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12413892","title":"Ectopic Supernumerary Fourth Molar in the Mandibular Notch: A Report of an Atypical Case With Literature Review.","category":"developmental_eruption","license":"cc by","authors":["Sara Macho-Lopez","Jose-Francisco Montes-Carmona","Alberto Garcia-Perla-Garcia","Rafael Martinez-De-Fuentes","Pedro Infante-Cossio"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2025","citation":"Sara Macho-Lopez, Jose-Francisco Montes-Carmona, Alberto Garcia-Perla-Garcia, Rafael Martinez-De-Fuentes, Pedro Infante-Cossio. Ectopic Supernumerary Fourth Molar in the Mandibular Notch: A Report of an Atypical Case With Literature Review. Cureus. 2025. doi: 10.7759/cureus.89557.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025, Macho-Lopez et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12413892/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.89557","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [symptom]: 33岁男性，左侧面颊持续钝痛及间歇性肿胀3个月\n- E2 [opg]: 10年前全景片显示左侧上下颌各有一颗阻生、形态幼稚的第四磨牙（箭头所示）\n- E3 [opg]: 当前全景片显示一颗形态完整（eumorphic）的下颌第四磨牙异位位于乙状切迹区（箭头），并见一自阻生第三磨牙向上延伸至乙状切迹的透射影\n- E4 [other_imaging]: CT显示该异位第四磨牙冠周见边界清晰的单房透射影，提示含牙囊肿形成\n- E5 [history]: 患者10年前曾行上颌第四磨牙拔除术，下颌第四磨牙当时计划拔除但患者拒绝并失访\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Conventional panoramic radiograph views. (A) Previous panoramic radiograph taken 10 years earlier showing two impacted rudimentary fourth molars (upper and lower) on the left side (arrows). (B) Current panoramic radiograph showing the ectopically positioned, eumorphic mandibular fourth molar in the sigmoid notch (arrow). An ascending radiolucent image was seen extending from the impacted third molar to the sigmoid notch.\n- [ct] Computed tomography with coronal, sagittal, and axial slices. (A) Coronal and (B) axial CT scans showing a well-defined radiolucency around the crown, suggesting the formation of a dentigerous cyst (arrows).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n","think":"\n1. 患者存在左侧面部持续钝痛及间歇性肿胀，提示可能存在口腔或颌面区的病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 当前全景片显示下颌乙状切迹区有一颗异位且形态完整的第四磨牙，并伴有自阻生第三磨牙向上延伸至乙状切迹的透射影。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. CT进一步确认了该异位第四磨牙冠周存在一个边界清晰的单房透射影，符合含牙囊肿的表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的症状、影像学发现以及既往病史，可以推断出存在位于下颌乙状切迹区的异位第四磨牙及其伴随的含牙囊肿。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无法从现有证据直接确定含牙囊肿的具体病因。\n","answer":"\n下颌乙状切迹区异位第四磨牙伴含牙囊肿（Ectopic supernumerary fourth molar in the mandibular sigmoid notch associated with a dentigerous cyst）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Conventional panoramic radiograph views. (A) Previous panoramic radiograph taken 10 years earlier showing two impacted rudimentary fourth molars (upper and lower) on the left side (arrows). (B) Current panoramic radiograph showing the ectopically positioned, eumorphic mandibular fourth molar in the sigmoid notch (arrow). An ascending radiolucent image was seen extending from the impacted third molar to the sigmoid notch.\n- [ct] Computed tomography with coronal, sagittal, and axial slices. (A) Coronal and (B) axial CT scans showing a well-defined radiolucency around the crown, suggesting the formation of a dentigerous cyst (arrows).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者存在左侧面部持续钝痛及间歇性肿胀，提示可能存在口腔或颌面区的病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 当前全景片显示下颌乙状切迹区有一颗异位且形态完整的第四磨牙，并伴有自阻生第三磨牙向上延伸至乙状切迹的透射影。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. CT进一步确认了该异位第四磨牙冠周存在一个边界清晰的单房透射影，符合含牙囊肿的表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的症状、影像学发现以及既往病史，可以推断出存在位于下颌乙状切迹区的异位第四磨牙及其伴随的含牙囊肿。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无法从现有证据直接确定含牙囊肿的具体病因。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n下颌乙状切迹区异位第四磨牙伴含牙囊肿（Ectopic supernumerary fourth molar in the mandibular sigmoid notch associated with a dentigerous cyst）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12413892/cureus-0017-00000089557-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000089557-i01.jpg","caption":"Conventional panoramic radiograph views. (A) Previous panoramic radiograph taken 10 years earlier showing two impacted rudimentary fourth molars (upper and lower) on the left side (arrows). (B) Current panoramic radiograph showing the ectopically positioned, eumorphic mandibular fourth molar in the sigmoid notch (arrow). An ascending radiolucent image was seen extending from the impacted third molar to the sigmoid notch.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"50caeec4b40df390327ca5130b8c8d29df9bb1562dc0b370e75e4173846022aa","width":750,"height":318},{"src":"assets/PMC12413892/cureus-0017-00000089557-i02.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000089557-i02.jpg","caption":"Computed tomography with coronal, sagittal, and axial slices. (A) Coronal and (B) axial CT scans showing a well-defined radiolucency around the crown, suggesting the formation of a dentigerous cyst (arrows).","types":["ct"],"sha256":"d8405d605a4a693966811725c6b10db862a7af281a3cffe0b987bba42fd0ad00","width":750,"height":319}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC8003149","title":"An Orthodontic Approach for Garre's Sclerosing Osteomyelitis of the Mandible.","category":"infection","license":"cc by","authors":["Ioan Barbur","Simion Bran","Mihaela Baciut","Gabriel Armencea","Alexandra Iulia Aghiorghiesei","Tudor-Sergiu Suciu","Adina Maria Barbur","Horia Opris","Grigore Baciut","Cristian Dinu"],"journal":"International journal of environmental research and public health","year":"2021","citation":"Ioan Barbur, Simion Bran, Mihaela Baciut, Gabriel Armencea, Alexandra Iulia Aghiorghiesei, Tudor-Sergiu Suciu, Adina Maria Barbur, Horia Opris, Grigore Baciut, Cristian Dinu. An Orthodontic Approach for Garre's Sclerosing Osteomyelitis of the Mandible. International journal of environmental research and public health. 2021. doi: 10.3390/ijerph18063159.","license_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland. This article is an open access article distributed under the terms and conditions of the Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).","copyright":["© 2021 by the authors."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8003149/","doi":"10.3390/ijerph18063159","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history|symptom|clinical_exam]: 9岁女性，主诉下颌快速疼痛、肿胀及进食困难；临床检查无脓液、脓肿或瘘管\n- E2 [opg|other_imaging]: 影像学显示下颌体全程多发边界不清的透光区伴弥漫性高密度影，呈‘洋葱皮样’骨膜反应\n- E3 [laboratory]: 骨活检组织学（Masson三色、HE、免疫组化）证实为慢性硬化性骨髓炎\n- E4 [laboratory|symptom]: 微生物培养无明确致病菌；广谱抗生素治疗后症状部分缓解但复发\n- E5 [rgb|clinical_exam]: 初诊时面部表现为下脸高度增加、直面型、唇闭合不全（3 mm）、中线对称\n- E6 [clinical_exam]: 口内见乳牙侧方支持区部分破坏致双侧间隙丧失、双牙弓缩短、Spee曲线加深、口腔卫生差\n- E7 [clinical_exam]: 咬合关系：右侧下尖牙远中移位半颗牙尖，左侧尖牙I类，双侧磨牙I类；存在舌 thrust 及咬甲习惯\n- E8 [other_imaging]: CBCT与MRI显示双侧关节盘萎缩、右盘穿孔伴前外移位、左盘前外移位、双侧髁突吸收伴活动性侵蚀\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph showing the “onion-skin” appearance of the bone at full length of the mandible.\n- [cbct/ct] Initial Cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) examination shows osteolytic and sclerosis lesions (“onion skin”); A—sagittal sections through the body and ramus of the mandible; B—cross sections through the body of the mandible.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] Pre-treatment extra-oral photographs; (A)—Frontal view; (B)—Smile; (C)—lateral view.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 9岁女性，主诉下颌快速疼痛、肿胀及进食困难；临床检查无脓液、脓肿或瘘管。 诊断意义：支持加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断\n\n2. 影像学显示下颌体全程多发边界不清的透光区伴弥漫性高密度影，呈‘洋葱皮样’骨膜反应。 诊断意义：支持加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断\n\n3. 骨活检组织学（Masson三色、HE、免疫组化）证实为慢性硬化性骨髓炎。 诊断意义：支持加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断\n\n4. 微生物培养无明确致病菌；广谱抗生素治疗后症状部分缓解但复发。 诊断意义：支持加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者有典型临床表现（E1），影像学特征（E2），病理确诊（E3）以及对抗生素治疗的反应（E4），均指向加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无法通过现有证据完全排除其他类型的骨髓炎。\n","answer":"\n加雷硬化性骨髓炎（下颌骨）（Garre’s sclerosing osteomyelitis of the mandible）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph showing the “onion-skin” appearance of the bone at full length of the mandible.\n- [cbct/ct] Initial Cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) examination shows osteolytic and sclerosis lesions (“onion skin”); A—sagittal sections through the body and ramus of the mandible; B—cross sections through the body of the mandible.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] Pre-treatment extra-oral photographs; (A)—Frontal view; (B)—Smile; (C)—lateral view.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 9岁女性，主诉下颌快速疼痛、肿胀及进食困难；临床检查无脓液、脓肿或瘘管。 诊断意义：支持加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断\n\n2. 影像学显示下颌体全程多发边界不清的透光区伴弥漫性高密度影，呈‘洋葱皮样’骨膜反应。 诊断意义：支持加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断\n\n3. 骨活检组织学（Masson三色、HE、免疫组化）证实为慢性硬化性骨髓炎。 诊断意义：支持加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断\n\n4. 微生物培养无明确致病菌；广谱抗生素治疗后症状部分缓解但复发。 诊断意义：支持加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者有典型临床表现（E1），影像学特征（E2），病理确诊（E3）以及对抗生素治疗的反应（E4），均指向加雷硬化性骨髓炎的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；无法通过现有证据完全排除其他类型的骨髓炎。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n加雷硬化性骨髓炎（下颌骨）（Garre’s sclerosing osteomyelitis of the mandible）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC8003149/ijerph-18-03159-g002.jpg","name":"ijerph-18-03159-g002.jpg","caption":"Panoramic radiograph showing the “onion-skin” appearance of the bone at full length of the mandible.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"b463e597d24dc53a4bd8a9fa9b4a18c44d91e330587f92d113cb91f5cf6a0e65","width":780,"height":481},{"src":"assets/PMC8003149/ijerph-18-03159-g004.jpg","name":"ijerph-18-03159-g004.jpg","caption":"Pre-treatment extra-oral photographs; (A)—Frontal view; (B)—Smile; (C)—lateral view.","types":["extraoral_photo"],"sha256":"b25c4ae3f2ba5f6ea2e74114bca29b18348d1e79c57a564468755908f1267cb6","width":744,"height":328},{"src":"assets/PMC8003149/ijerph-18-03159-g001.jpg","name":"ijerph-18-03159-g001.jpg","caption":"Initial Cone beam computed tomography (CBCT) examination shows osteolytic and sclerosis lesions (“onion skin”); A—sagittal sections through the body and ramus of the mandible; B—cross sections through the body of the mandible.","types":["cbct","ct"],"sha256":"00e74b8ba0598c0a405d6f4042173133544c90002729d0baa4034263eed86549","width":771,"height":475}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12478033","title":"Late mandibular fracture after third molar extraction: a malpractice case or not?","category":"trauma_resorption","license":"cc by","authors":["Sara Bernardi","Eleonora Ricciuti","Sara Trichilo","Davide Gerardi","Fabiola Rinaldi","Giuseppe Varvara","Stefano Mummolo","Guido Macchiarelli","Serena Bianchi"],"journal":"The Journal of forensic odonto-stomatology","year":"2025","citation":"Sara Bernardi, Eleonora Ricciuti, Sara Trichilo, Davide Gerardi, Fabiola Rinaldi, Giuseppe Varvara, Stefano Mummolo, Guido Macchiarelli, Serena Bianchi. Late mandibular fracture after third molar extraction: a malpractice case or not?. The Journal of forensic odonto-stomatology. 2025. doi: 10.5281/zenodo.15564456.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) 4.0 License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright 2025 International Organization for Forensic Odonto-Stomatology - IOFOS"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12478033/","doi":"10.5281/zenodo.15564456","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history|demographics|opg]: 40岁男性，主诉左下颌半侧炎症；术前OPG显示3.8牙半阻生（Pell & Gregory IB类），牙周囊致3.7远中根骨吸收\n- E2 [symptom]: 拔牙术后7天进食时突发‘碎玻璃样’响声，伴左下颌关节区剧痛及麻木\n- E3 [opg|clinical_exam]: 症状出现当日行OPG，初诊误判为髁突脱位\n- E4 [rgb]: 体表无明显不对称（图2a,b,c）；口内见牙槽嵴骨吸收；下颌运动功能正常\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Pre operative OPG. The circle and the arrow indicated the 3.8 tooth\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo/intraoral_photo] a.b.c. Extraoral images showing the absence of visible asymmetries\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者有左下颌半侧炎症病史，术前OPG显示3.8牙半阻生及3.7远中根骨吸收。 诊断意义：支持左侧下颌存在潜在病理状态\n\n2. 拔牙术后7天进食时出现‘碎玻璃样’响声、剧痛及麻木感。 诊断意义：提示可能的骨折发生\n\n3. 症状出现后立即进行了OPG检查，但初诊误判为髁突脱位。 诊断意义：间接表明影像学检查发现了异常但未能正确诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者左下颌半侧存在炎症和牙齿问题，术后突发剧痛和麻木，结合影像学检查发现异常，支持左侧下颌角不完全/近完全性骨折的可能性。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏直接影像学证据明确指出骨折的具体位置和类型；体表无明显不对称且下颌运动功能正常，降低了临床直观判断骨折的特异性。\n","answer":"\n左侧下颌角不完全/近完全性骨折（fracture of the left mandibular angle）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Pre operative OPG. The circle and the arrow indicated the 3.8 tooth\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo/intraoral_photo] a.b.c. Extraoral images showing the absence of visible asymmetries\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者有左下颌半侧炎症病史，术前OPG显示3.8牙半阻生及3.7远中根骨吸收。 诊断意义：支持左侧下颌存在潜在病理状态\n\n2. 拔牙术后7天进食时出现‘碎玻璃样’响声、剧痛及麻木感。 诊断意义：提示可能的骨折发生\n\n3. 症状出现后立即进行了OPG检查，但初诊误判为髁突脱位。 诊断意义：间接表明影像学检查发现了异常但未能正确诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者左下颌半侧存在炎症和牙齿问题，术后突发剧痛和麻木，结合影像学检查发现异常，支持左侧下颌角不完全/近完全性骨折的可能性。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏直接影像学证据明确指出骨折的具体位置和类型；体表无明显不对称且下颌运动功能正常，降低了临床直观判断骨折的特异性。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n左侧下颌角不完全/近完全性骨折（fracture of the left mandibular angle）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12478033/JFOS-43-2-02-f5.jpg","name":"JFOS-43-2-02-f5.jpg","caption":"Pre operative OPG. The circle and the arrow indicated the 3.8 tooth","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"7889cef9e58e7a9c28789fd28c1c769eda2b635eea8b2db11df14e98b59e1895","width":752,"height":366},{"src":"assets/PMC12478033/JFOS-43-2-02-f2.jpg","name":"JFOS-43-2-02-f2.jpg","caption":"a.b.c. Extraoral images showing the absence of visible asymmetries","types":["extraoral_photo","intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"b5e4b1ca2348240cb2b4bff40c1932bf9262a06a3476c5921f083bf7854e1ea3","width":674,"height":254}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC6738723","title":"Primary molar with chronic periapical abscess showing atypical presentation of simultaneous extraoral and intraoral sinus tract with multiple stomata.","category":"endodontic_periapical","license":"cc by-nc","authors":["Abul Khair Mohammad Bashar","Khaleda Akter","Govind Kumar Chaudhary","Asifur Rahman"],"journal":"BMJ case reports","year":"2019","citation":"Abul Khair Mohammad Bashar, Khaleda Akter, Govind Kumar Chaudhary, Asifur Rahman. Primary molar with chronic periapical abscess showing atypical presentation of simultaneous extraoral and intraoral sinus tract with multiple stomata. BMJ case reports. 2019. doi: 10.1136/bcr-2018-229039.","license_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/","licenseUrls":["http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/This is an open access article distributed in accordance with the Creative Commons Attribution Non Commercial (CC BY-NC 4.0) license, which permits others to distribute, remix, adapt, build upon this work non-commercially, and license their derivative works on different terms, provided the original work is properly cited and the use is non-commercial. See: http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/","copyright":["© BMJ Publishing Group Limited 2019. Re-use permitted under CC BY-NC. No commercial re-use. See rights and permissions. Published by BMJ."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6738723/","doi":"10.1136/bcr-2018-229039","question":"\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E5 [other_imaging]: 窦道探针（牙胶尖）追踪证实来源为乳牙85根分叉区\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的OPG细节。\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例没有可与诊断时间点可靠对应的非病理图片，诊断推理仅依据病例文字信息。\n","think":"\n1. 窦道探针（牙胶尖）追踪证实来源为乳牙85根分叉区。 诊断意义：支持诊断乳牙85慢性根尖周脓肿伴口外与口内双通道多孔窦道。\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 通过窦道探针追踪确认了病变位置在乳牙85的根分叉区，提示存在该牙的慢性根尖周脓肿伴有窦道形成。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不足于明确区分口外与口内窦道的具体表现及多孔情况；仅能确认窦道来源于患牙。\n","answer":"\n乳牙85慢性根尖周脓肿伴口外与口内双通道多孔窦道（Chronic periapical abscess of primary tooth no. 85 with simultaneous extraoral and intraoral sinus tract with multiple stomata）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的OPG细节。\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例没有可与诊断时间点可靠对应的非病理图片，诊断推理仅依据病例文字信息。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 窦道探针（牙胶尖）追踪证实来源为乳牙85根分叉区。 诊断意义：支持诊断乳牙85慢性根尖周脓肿伴口外与口内双通道多孔窦道。\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 通过窦道探针追踪确认了病变位置在乳牙85的根分叉区，提示存在该牙的慢性根尖周脓肿伴有窦道形成。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不足于明确区分口外与口内窦道的具体表现及多孔情况；仅能确认窦道来源于患牙。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n乳牙85慢性根尖周脓肿伴口外与口内双通道多孔窦道（Chronic periapical abscess of primary tooth no. 85 with simultaneous extraoral and intraoral sinus tract with multiple stomata）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[],"english":null},{"id":"PMC8891407","title":"Squamous cell carcinoma around a subperiosteal implant in the maxilla and the association of chronic mechanical irritation and peri-implantitis: a case report.","category":"implant_prosthetic","license":"cc by","authors":["Takuma Watanabe","Dai Kawahara","Ryo Inoue","Tomoki Kato","Noboru Ishihara","Hidemichi Kamiya","Kazuhisa Bessho"],"journal":"International journal of implant dentistry","year":"2022","citation":"Takuma Watanabe, Dai Kawahara, Ryo Inoue, Tomoki Kato, Noboru Ishihara, Hidemichi Kamiya, Kazuhisa Bessho. Squamous cell carcinoma around a subperiosteal implant in the maxilla and the association of chronic mechanical irritation and peri-implantitis: a case report. International journal of implant dentistry. 2022. doi: 10.1186/s40729-022-00409-3.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"Open AccessThis article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, which permits use, sharing, adaptation, distribution and reproduction in any medium or format, as long as you give appropriate credit to the original author(s) and the source, provide a link to the Creative Commons licence, and indicate if changes were made. The images or other third party material in this article are included in the article's Creative Commons licence, unless indicated otherwise in a credit line to the material. If material is not included in the article's Creative Commons licence and your intended use is not permitted by statutory regulation or exceeds the permitted use, you will need to obtain permission directly from the copyright holder. To view a copy of this licence, visit http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.","copyright":["© The Author(s) 2022"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8891407/","doi":"10.1186/s40729-022-00409-3","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history|symptom|clinical_exam]: 74岁男性，无吸烟饮酒史，20年前植入上颌亚骨膜种植体（SI），1枚固位螺钉术后即脱落；近2年出现腭部剧烈疼痛、鼻塞、SI严重松动、腭侧瘘管伴金属支架暴露及潜行性溃疡伴硬结\n- E2 [clinical_exam|rgb]: 口内检查见SI贴合不良、严重松动，腭侧潜行性溃疡伴硬结，瘘管形成，金属支架暴露（图1A,B）\n- E4 [other_imaging]: CT显示种植体金属支架周围显著上颌骨吸收、固位螺钉几近脱落、双侧上颌窦炎（图3A,B）\n- E5 [clinical_exam]: 基于恶性肿瘤怀疑行切取活检\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph showing a maxillary subperiosteal implant and retaining screw\n- [ct] Axial (A) and coronal (B) computed tomography images showing major maxillary bone resorption around the metal framework, the retaining screw that almost fell off, and bilateral maxillary sinusitis\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Frontal view of an intraoral photograph showing a molar prosthesis attached to the metal framework (A). Palatal view of an intraoral photograph showing the metal framework exposed through the fistula with an undermined ulcer (B)\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者有上颌亚骨膜种植体植入史，近2年出现腭部剧烈疼痛、鼻塞、种植体严重松动及瘘管形成等症状。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查发现种植体贴合不良、严重松动，伴有腭侧潜行性溃疡和硬结以及金属支架暴露。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. CT影像显示种植体周围显著的上颌骨吸收、固位螺钉几近脱落，并伴有双侧上颌窦炎。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 基于上述临床表现和影像学特征，存在恶性肿瘤的可能性，因此进行了切取活检。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据病史中提及的症状（如腭部疼痛、鼻塞、种植体松动等）结合口腔检查发现（如种植体松动、溃疡、瘘管形成等），以及CT影像显示的上颌骨吸收情况，怀疑为恶性肿瘤并进行了活检。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理结果以明确诊断\n","answer":"\n上颌骨亚骨膜种植体周围鳞状细胞癌（Squamous cell carcinoma around a subperiosteal implant in the maxilla）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph showing a maxillary subperiosteal implant and retaining screw\n- [ct] Axial (A) and coronal (B) computed tomography images showing major maxillary bone resorption around the metal framework, the retaining screw that almost fell off, and bilateral maxillary sinusitis\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Frontal view of an intraoral photograph showing a molar prosthesis attached to the metal framework (A). Palatal view of an intraoral photograph showing the metal framework exposed through the fistula with an undermined ulcer (B)\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者有上颌亚骨膜种植体植入史，近2年出现腭部剧烈疼痛、鼻塞、种植体严重松动及瘘管形成等症状。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查发现种植体贴合不良、严重松动，伴有腭侧潜行性溃疡和硬结以及金属支架暴露。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. CT影像显示种植体周围显著的上颌骨吸收、固位螺钉几近脱落，并伴有双侧上颌窦炎。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 基于上述临床表现和影像学特征，存在恶性肿瘤的可能性，因此进行了切取活检。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据病史中提及的症状（如腭部疼痛、鼻塞、种植体松动等）结合口腔检查发现（如种植体松动、溃疡、瘘管形成等），以及CT影像显示的上颌骨吸收情况，怀疑为恶性肿瘤并进行了活检。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理结果以明确诊断\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n上颌骨亚骨膜种植体周围鳞状细胞癌（Squamous cell carcinoma around a subperiosteal implant in the maxilla）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC8891407/40729_2022_409_Fig2_HTML.jpg","name":"40729_2022_409_Fig2_HTML.jpg","caption":"Panoramic radiograph showing a maxillary subperiosteal implant and retaining screw","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"6217225bcc0cd91eb4891508d3aa2efb8740517246b0e133ebf5f7dfd4baa305","width":598,"height":335},{"src":"assets/PMC8891407/40729_2022_409_Fig1_HTML.jpg","name":"40729_2022_409_Fig1_HTML.jpg","caption":"Frontal view of an intraoral photograph showing a molar prosthesis attached to the metal framework (A). Palatal view of an intraoral photograph showing the metal framework exposed through the fistula with an undermined ulcer (B)","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"104565717361cf922d7ac7f6493fb47b26be9a6849e48fe70c845ba5c5723ca4","width":708,"height":263},{"src":"assets/PMC8891407/40729_2022_409_Fig3_HTML.jpg","name":"40729_2022_409_Fig3_HTML.jpg","caption":"Axial (A) and coronal (B) computed tomography images showing major maxillary bone resorption around the metal framework, the retaining screw that almost fell off, and bilateral maxillary sinusitis","types":["ct"],"sha256":"8bedf106f34d755f755766a5067e67686a1293e697ef55abb618945441d22beb","width":708,"height":321}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC10642913","title":"Radicular Cyst: A Cystic Lesion Involving the Hard Palate.","category":"mucosal_oral_lesion","license":"cc by","authors":["Nishant Rathi","Amit Reche","Sakshi Agrawal"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2023","citation":"Nishant Rathi, Amit Reche, Sakshi Agrawal. Radicular Cyst: A Cystic Lesion Involving the Hard Palate. Cureus. 2023. doi: 10.7759/cureus.47030.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2023, Rathi et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10642913/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.47030","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 42岁男性，左上颌前牙区疼痛1个月，伴肿胀10天；曾用阿育吠陀药物，有出血及脓液排出约1月；疼痛锐利、间歇性，咀嚼加重，用药可缓解；伴发热、局部麻木感及弯腰不适8天；肿胀渐进性增大。\n- E2 [extraoral_photo]: 口外检查无面部不对称（图1）。\n- E3 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查见左上颌前牙区（22-24）单发肿物，约2.5×2 cm，椭圆形，表面光滑，边界弥散，质软，无压痛；触诊温度升高，与深部结构固定。\n- E4 [opg]: OPG显示22-24根尖区类椭圆形、边界清晰皮质化的透射影，约2.5×2 cm（图3）。\n- E5 [clinical_exam]: 患牙22-24牙髓活力丧失，根尖诊断为慢性根尖周脓肿急性发作。\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram (OPG)\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] Extraoral examination of the patient.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者有左上颌前牙区疼痛及肿胀，伴有发热、局部麻木感等症状，提示存在根尖周病。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查发现左上颌前牙区（22-24）单发肿物，边界弥散，质软，触诊温度升高，进一步指向根尖周病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. OPG影像显示22-24根尖区类椭圆形、边界清晰皮质化的透射影，符合根尖囊肿的影像学表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 患牙22-24牙髓活力丧失，结合临床诊断为慢性根尖周脓肿急性发作，支持根尖囊肿的存在。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的症状史、口腔检查和影像学发现，支持根尖囊肿的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不足以完全排除其他类型的根尖周病变。\n","answer":"\n根尖囊肿（Radicular cyst）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram (OPG)\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] Extraoral examination of the patient.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者有左上颌前牙区疼痛及肿胀，伴有发热、局部麻木感等症状，提示存在根尖周病。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查发现左上颌前牙区（22-24）单发肿物，边界弥散，质软，触诊温度升高，进一步指向根尖周病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. OPG影像显示22-24根尖区类椭圆形、边界清晰皮质化的透射影，符合根尖囊肿的影像学表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 患牙22-24牙髓活力丧失，结合临床诊断为慢性根尖周脓肿急性发作，支持根尖囊肿的存在。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于患者的症状史、口腔检查和影像学发现，支持根尖囊肿的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不足以完全排除其他类型的根尖周病变。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n根尖囊肿（Radicular cyst）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC10642913/cureus-0015-00000047030-i03.jpg","name":"cureus-0015-00000047030-i03.jpg","caption":"Orthopantomogram (OPG)","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"41840887ee30ae7c494622afbe2632ca95681039dd64010fe94ab728f042ccdf","width":750,"height":423},{"src":"assets/PMC10642913/cureus-0015-00000047030-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0015-00000047030-i01.jpg","caption":"Extraoral examination of the patient.","types":["extraoral_photo"],"sha256":"9126e9e9845455a3230b75fcb63dd2dfab8651f372b6446ffa129cbeb212e6cc","width":750,"height":663}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12011459","title":"Rapidly Expanding Odontogenic Myxoma: An Entity With Diagnostic Challenges-A Case Report.","category":"odontogenic_cyst_tumor","license":"cc by","authors":["Suwarna Dangore-Khasbage","Rajanikanth Kambala","Hanadi Sabban","Aakanksha Tiwari","Monika Khubchandani"],"journal":"Case reports in dentistry","year":"2025","citation":"Suwarna Dangore-Khasbage, Rajanikanth Kambala, Hanadi Sabban, Aakanksha Tiwari, Monika Khubchandani. Rapidly Expanding Odontogenic Myxoma: An Entity With Diagnostic Challenges-A Case Report. Case reports in dentistry. 2025. doi: 10.1155/crid/5741422.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits use, distribution and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025 Suwarna Dangore-Khasbage et al. Case Reports in Dentistry published by John Wiley & Sons Ltd."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12011459/","doi":"10.1155/crid/5741422","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 18岁女性，左下颌后区无痛性肿胀4个月，渐进性增大\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 面型不对称，左下颌后区弥漫性、质韧至硬、无压痛肿块，约4×5 cm\n- E4 [opg]: 曲面体层片示左下颌角及升支区单发、边界清楚、多房状透射影，伴左下第三磨牙阻生，累及范围从第一磨牙近中至升支后缘，致骨皮质变薄扩张\n- E5 [other_imaging]: 头颅正位片与CT轴位像显示颊舌侧骨皮质明显膨隆伴变薄，无骨皮质穿破\n- E6 [laboratory]: 术前活检低倍镜见疏松黏液样细胞，高倍镜见黏液样细胞与梭形/胖形成纤维细胞，HE染色支持OM\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram showing well-defined, multilocular, radiolucent lesion involving the angle and ramus of the mandible on the left side.\n- [ct/radiograph] (A) Posteroanterior radiograph of the skull and (B) axial view of computed tomography showing expansion of the buccal and lingual cortical plates with thinning.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] (A) Diffuse extraoral swelling in the left mandibular body. (B) Mild expansion in the posterior buccal self-area in 36–38 regions.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者为18岁女性，左下颌后区出现无痛性肿胀4个月，并且逐渐增大。 诊断意义：支持牙源性黏液瘤的临床病史\n\n2. 临床检查发现面型不对称，左下颌后区有弥漫性、质韧至硬、无压痛肿块，大小约4×5 cm。 诊断意义：支持牙源性黏液瘤的体征\n\n3. 影像学检查显示左下颌角及升支区存在单发、边界清楚、多房状透射影，伴有骨皮质变薄扩张，颊舌侧骨皮质明显膨隆但未穿破。 诊断意义：支持牙源性黏液瘤的影像学特征\n\n4. 术前活检低倍镜观察到疏松黏液样细胞，高倍镜下可见黏液样细胞与梭形/胖形成纤维细胞，HE染色结果支持OM诊断。 诊断意义：病理学证据支持牙源性黏液瘤的最终诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的病史、体检、影像学表现以及组织病理学检查，支持牙源性黏液瘤的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；这些证据虽然指向牙源性黏液瘤，但不能完全排除其他具有类似表现的肿瘤性疾病。\n","answer":"\n牙源性黏液瘤（Odontogenic Myxoma）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram showing well-defined, multilocular, radiolucent lesion involving the angle and ramus of the mandible on the left side.\n- [ct/radiograph] (A) Posteroanterior radiograph of the skull and (B) axial view of computed tomography showing expansion of the buccal and lingual cortical plates with thinning.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo] (A) Diffuse extraoral swelling in the left mandibular body. (B) Mild expansion in the posterior buccal self-area in 36–38 regions.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者为18岁女性，左下颌后区出现无痛性肿胀4个月，并且逐渐增大。 诊断意义：支持牙源性黏液瘤的临床病史\n\n2. 临床检查发现面型不对称，左下颌后区有弥漫性、质韧至硬、无压痛肿块，大小约4×5 cm。 诊断意义：支持牙源性黏液瘤的体征\n\n3. 影像学检查显示左下颌角及升支区存在单发、边界清楚、多房状透射影，伴有骨皮质变薄扩张，颊舌侧骨皮质明显膨隆但未穿破。 诊断意义：支持牙源性黏液瘤的影像学特征\n\n4. 术前活检低倍镜观察到疏松黏液样细胞，高倍镜下可见黏液样细胞与梭形/胖形成纤维细胞，HE染色结果支持OM诊断。 诊断意义：病理学证据支持牙源性黏液瘤的最终诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的病史、体检、影像学表现以及组织病理学检查，支持牙源性黏液瘤的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；这些证据虽然指向牙源性黏液瘤，但不能完全排除其他具有类似表现的肿瘤性疾病。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n牙源性黏液瘤（Odontogenic Myxoma）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12011459/CRID2025-5741422.002.jpg","name":"CRID2025-5741422.002.jpg","caption":"Orthopantomogram showing well-defined, multilocular, radiolucent lesion involving the angle and ramus of the mandible on the left side.","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"b776edffad793cb6d303ec5fb41db75222297cb4bb741c9623c97736abb1ce3a","width":515,"height":251},{"src":"assets/PMC12011459/CRID2025-5741422.001.jpg","name":"CRID2025-5741422.001.jpg","caption":"(A) Diffuse extraoral swelling in the left mandibular body. (B) Mild expansion in the posterior buccal self-area in 36–38 regions.","types":["extraoral_photo"],"sha256":"ec8e1e62de5999669ec6ff53011db82678b6250d5a7abf1e1f6e6163d1c184ab","width":355,"height":510},{"src":"assets/PMC12011459/CRID2025-5741422.003.jpg","name":"CRID2025-5741422.003.jpg","caption":"(A) Posteroanterior radiograph of the skull and (B) axial view of computed tomography showing expansion of the buccal and lingual cortical plates with thinning.","types":["ct","radiograph"],"sha256":"ba5e13b85468f927d2d4057e487ba87335ac9f390c29e1d52a2d98e636bfa4bd","width":709,"height":419}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC8983254","title":"Nonsyndromic Generalized Radiculomegaly of Permanent Dentition: A Rare Case Report.","category":"other_dental","license":"cc by","authors":["Mohammed Alhussain","Naif Almosa","Hourya Alnofaie"],"journal":"Case reports in dentistry","year":"2022","citation":"Mohammed Alhussain, Naif Almosa, Hourya Alnofaie. Nonsyndromic Generalized Radiculomegaly of Permanent Dentition: A Rare Case Report. Case reports in dentistry. 2022. doi: 10.1155/2022/3548370.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2022 Mohammed Alhussain et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983254/","doi":"10.1155/2022/3548370","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口外检查：中面型、凹面型侧貌、对称颏部、唇闭合正常\n- E4 [opg]: 曲面断层片显示几乎所有恒牙根极长且较宽；上颌第二磨牙根干极长；下颌牙根接近下颌下缘；第三磨牙牙根位于下牙槽神经管内\n- E6 [other_imaging]: 侧位头影测量示骨性III类（ANB -2.1°），上颌轻度后缩，上下前牙轴倾异常\n- E7 [other_imaging]: 眼科与心脏检查（视力、眼外肌、视野、眼压、听诊、ECG、超声心动图）均未见异常；无眼/心家族史\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] A panoramic radiograph showing the elongated roots of the teeth.\n- [radiograph] Periapical radiograph shows long roots of teeth #35, 36, 37 (a) and lateral cephalometric radiograph of the patient (b).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo/intraoral_photo] A clinical frontal view of the patient's face and neck (a), lateral profile view (b), intraoral lateral view of the patient's left side (c), IO right side (d), IO frontal view (e), IO upper occlusal view (f), and IO lower occlusal view (g).\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 曲面断层片显示几乎所有恒牙根极长且较宽，提示存在广泛的牙根异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 上颌第二磨牙根干极长以及下颌牙根接近下颌下缘进一步表明牙根长度显著超出正常范围。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 眼科与心脏检查均未见异常，排除了该症状是由已知的综合征引起的可能。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 广泛性牙根巨长症基于X光影像学发现，并通过排除其他系统性疾病得到支持。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不足以完全排除所有可能引起类似表现的罕见遗传综合症。\n","answer":"\n非综合征性广泛性牙根巨长症（Nonsyndromic generalized radiculomegaly）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] A panoramic radiograph showing the elongated roots of the teeth.\n- [radiograph] Periapical radiograph shows long roots of teeth #35, 36, 37 (a) and lateral cephalometric radiograph of the patient (b).\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [extraoral_photo/intraoral_photo] A clinical frontal view of the patient's face and neck (a), lateral profile view (b), intraoral lateral view of the patient's left side (c), IO right side (d), IO frontal view (e), IO upper occlusal view (f), and IO lower occlusal view (g).\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 曲面断层片显示几乎所有恒牙根极长且较宽，提示存在广泛的牙根异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 上颌第二磨牙根干极长以及下颌牙根接近下颌下缘进一步表明牙根长度显著超出正常范围。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 眼科与心脏检查均未见异常，排除了该症状是由已知的综合征引起的可能。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 广泛性牙根巨长症基于X光影像学发现，并通过排除其他系统性疾病得到支持。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不足以完全排除所有可能引起类似表现的罕见遗传综合症。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n非综合征性广泛性牙根巨长症（Nonsyndromic generalized radiculomegaly）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC8983254/CRID2022-3548370.002.jpg","name":"CRID2022-3548370.002.jpg","caption":"A panoramic radiograph showing the elongated roots of the teeth.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"596106ced1ea2662b6bb9514911ab690e343cc62ddc73d27bdcfc00f82f814e5","width":474,"height":218},{"src":"assets/PMC8983254/CRID2022-3548370.001.jpg","name":"CRID2022-3548370.001.jpg","caption":"A clinical frontal view of the patient's face and neck (a), lateral profile view (b), intraoral lateral view of the patient's left side (c), IO right side (d), IO frontal view (e), IO upper occlusal view (f), and IO lower occlusal view (g).","types":["extraoral_photo","intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"91b6c4e3a6df52e906e62fd4225096f0246e07a8768f9f2c852ffa64101a877e","width":744,"height":1372},{"src":"assets/PMC8983254/CRID2022-3548370.003.jpg","name":"CRID2022-3548370.003.jpg","caption":"Periapical radiograph shows long roots of teeth #35, 36, 37 (a) and lateral cephalometric radiograph of the patient (b).","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"a6ecb4f7722ed9055cdc01253b924109ee84a0a9f9ad02ce1da661d3014bb71f","width":602,"height":296}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12225767","title":"Ligneous periodontitis: A molecularly confirmed case of type I plasminogen deficiency.","category":"periodontal","license":"cc by","authors":["Atanur Sarioglu","Kubra Ugurlu","Meltem Karaman","Taner Karakaya","Tugrul Kirtiloglu","Ayse Zeynep Zengin"],"journal":"Journal of clinical and experimental dentistry","year":"2025","citation":"Atanur Sarioglu, Kubra Ugurlu, Meltem Karaman, Taner Karakaya, Tugrul Kirtiloglu, Ayse Zeynep Zengin. Ligneous periodontitis: A molecularly confirmed case of type I plasminogen deficiency. Journal of clinical and experimental dentistry. 2025. doi: 10.4317/jced.62773.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright: © 2025 Medicina Oral S.L."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12225767/","doi":"10.4317/jced.62773","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 23岁男性，主诉广泛性牙龈增生伴出血；既往史包括脑积水出生、乳牙滞留、恒牙萌出延迟及反复牙龈问题\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查见全口牙龈弥漫性增生与红斑，后牙区尤著；病变呈带蒂状，可用牙周探针分离，触之敏感\n- E3 [opg]: 全景片显示上下颌广泛骨吸收，后牙区严重根分叉病变\n- E4 [laboratory]: 血浆纤溶酶原水平显著降低至27%（参考范围70–130%）\n- E5 [other_imaging]: 活检组织病理示局灶性上皮糜烂、增生、角化不全，固有层见均质嗜酸性物质沉积、慢性活动性炎症及血管增生\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的OPG细节。\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] A,B,C,D: Intraoral view of the patient showing abnormal hyperplastic lesions with pedunculated appearance on the buccal surfaces of all four quadrants, separable with the help of a periodontal probe.\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的临床照片，未提供可独立核对的诊断前放射影像。\n","think":"\n1. 23岁男性患者有广泛的牙龈增生和出血，既往史包括脑积水出生、乳牙滞留、恒牙萌出延迟及反复牙龈问题。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查发现全口牙龈弥漫性增生与红斑，后牙区尤著；病变呈带蒂状，可用牙周探针分离，触之敏感。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 全景片显示上下颌广泛骨吸收，后牙区严重根分叉病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 血浆纤溶酶原水平显著降低至27%（参考范围70–130%），提示凝血功能异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的病史、临床表现、影像学检查以及实验室检查结果，符合木样性牙周炎的诊断标准。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；病理结果未特异性指出木样性牙周炎，但结合其他证据可以指向该诊断。\n","answer":"\n木样性牙周炎（ ligneous periodontitis）（Ligneous periodontitis）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的OPG细节。\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] A,B,C,D: Intraoral view of the patient showing abnormal hyperplastic lesions with pedunculated appearance on the buccal surfaces of all four quadrants, separable with the help of a periodontal probe.\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的临床照片，未提供可独立核对的诊断前放射影像。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 23岁男性患者有广泛的牙龈增生和出血，既往史包括脑积水出生、乳牙滞留、恒牙萌出延迟及反复牙龈问题。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 口内检查发现全口牙龈弥漫性增生与红斑，后牙区尤著；病变呈带蒂状，可用牙周探针分离，触之敏感。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 全景片显示上下颌广泛骨吸收，后牙区严重根分叉病变。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 血浆纤溶酶原水平显著降低至27%（参考范围70–130%），提示凝血功能异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的病史、临床表现、影像学检查以及实验室检查结果，符合木样性牙周炎的诊断标准。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；病理结果未特异性指出木样性牙周炎，但结合其他证据可以指向该诊断。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n木样性牙周炎（ ligneous periodontitis）（Ligneous periodontitis）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12225767/jced-17-06-e752-g001.jpg","name":"jced-17-06-e752-g001.jpg","caption":"A,B,C,D: Intraoral view of the patient showing abnormal hyperplastic lesions with pedunculated appearance on the buccal surfaces of all four quadrants, separable with the help of a periodontal probe.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"ad07d7192a296b2f4dfb4266677c37b3762213e4455bab6ce65eb59070853a43","width":732,"height":445}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12638139","title":"Maxillary Canine Substitution for a Central Incisor With Severe Root Resorption: A Case Report.","category":"trauma_resorption","license":"cc by","authors":["Hoda Rahimi","Anil P Ardeshna"],"journal":"Case reports in dentistry","year":"2025","citation":"Hoda Rahimi, Anil P Ardeshna. Maxillary Canine Substitution for a Central Incisor With Severe Root Resorption: A Case Report. Case reports in dentistry. 2025. doi: 10.1155/crid/4904301.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits use, distribution and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025 Hoda Rahimi and Anil P. Ardeshna. Case Reports in Dentistry published by John Wiley & Sons Ltd."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12638139/","doi":"10.1155/crid/4904301","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history|demographics]: 10岁5个月女性，无全身疾病或外伤史，主诉上颌右侧尖牙阻生\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 临床检查见上颌右侧中切牙Ⅰ度松动，活力测试阳性；鼻棘下方黏膜触及膨隆\n- E5 [other_imaging]: CBCT显示上颌右侧尖牙阻生于颊侧骨板，位于邻牙根中1/3处，右侧中切牙牙根严重吸收，吸收边界呈斜行、近远中及唇舌向广泛进展\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [cbct/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Pretreatment radiographic images demonstrating the maxillary right canine: (a) CBCT, (b) periapical X-ray, and (c) panoramic radiograph.\n- [radiograph] Pretreatment digitized lateral cephalometric radiograph.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Pretreatment facial and intraoral photographs.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者为10岁5个月女性，主诉上颌右侧尖牙阻生。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 临床检查发现上颌右侧中切牙Ⅰ度松动，活力测试阳性；鼻棘下方黏膜触及膨隆。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. CBCT显示上颌右侧尖牙阻生于颊侧骨板，位于邻牙根中1/3处，右侧中切牙牙根严重吸收，吸收边界呈斜行、近远中及唇舌向广泛进展。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据病史、临床检查和影像学检查结果，可以诊断上颌右侧尖牙异位萌出致右侧中切牙严重牙根吸收，考虑进行尖牙替代中切牙治疗。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；未提供其他可能引起牙齿松动的原因排除信息。\n","answer":"\n上颌右侧尖牙异位萌出致右侧中切牙严重牙根吸收，行尖牙替代中切牙治疗（Maxillary canine substitution for a central incisor with severe root resorption）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [cbct/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Pretreatment radiographic images demonstrating the maxillary right canine: (a) CBCT, (b) periapical X-ray, and (c) panoramic radiograph.\n- [radiograph] Pretreatment digitized lateral cephalometric radiograph.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Pretreatment facial and intraoral photographs.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者为10岁5个月女性，主诉上颌右侧尖牙阻生。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 临床检查发现上颌右侧中切牙Ⅰ度松动，活力测试阳性；鼻棘下方黏膜触及膨隆。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. CBCT显示上颌右侧尖牙阻生于颊侧骨板，位于邻牙根中1/3处，右侧中切牙牙根严重吸收，吸收边界呈斜行、近远中及唇舌向广泛进展。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据病史、临床检查和影像学检查结果，可以诊断上颌右侧尖牙异位萌出致右侧中切牙严重牙根吸收，考虑进行尖牙替代中切牙治疗。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；未提供其他可能引起牙齿松动的原因排除信息。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n上颌右侧尖牙异位萌出致右侧中切牙严重牙根吸收，行尖牙替代中切牙治疗（Maxillary canine substitution for a central incisor with severe root resorption）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12638139/CRID2025-4904301.002.jpg","name":"CRID2025-4904301.002.jpg","caption":"Pretreatment radiographic images demonstrating the maxillary right canine: (a) CBCT, (b) periapical X-ray, and (c) panoramic radiograph.","types":["cbct","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"c1c849e145d214b7cd47408fdfb1859a2dc9a17fbdd76b5e0d18a21a34bab963","width":659,"height":816},{"src":"assets/PMC12638139/CRID2025-4904301.001.jpg","name":"CRID2025-4904301.001.jpg","caption":"Pretreatment facial and intraoral photographs.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"03ba52c9149d7039dd75dbf1e5ddf5ffb055009006f23a6016c1858e42efcc98","width":570,"height":405},{"src":"assets/PMC12638139/CRID2025-4904301.003.jpg","name":"CRID2025-4904301.003.jpg","caption":"Pretreatment digitized lateral cephalometric radiograph.","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"d123a34eb21e03674e4197cb7aae8fe77a12a33df11867a848eca56c755ac95d","width":709,"height":573}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC11864335","title":"Maxillary mucormycosis masquerading as an endodontic-periodontal lesion.","category":"endodontic_periapical","license":"cc by-nc-sa","authors":["Abubacker Afreen Jannath","Krishnan Viswanathan","Sambanthan Thiruneelakandan","Rajasekar Sundaram","Srinivasan Sivapragasam"],"journal":"Journal of Indian Society of Periodontology","year":"2024","citation":"Abubacker Afreen Jannath, Krishnan Viswanathan, Sambanthan Thiruneelakandan, Rajasekar Sundaram, Srinivasan Sivapragasam. Maxillary mucormycosis masquerading as an endodontic-periodontal lesion. Journal of Indian Society of Periodontology. 2024. doi: 10.4103/jisp.jisp_89_24.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/This is an open access journal, and articles are distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 License, which allows others to remix, tweak, and build upon the work non-commercially, as long as appropriate credit is given and the new creations are licensed under the identical terms.","copyright":["Copyright: © 2025 Indian Society of Periodontology"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11864335/","doi":"10.4103/jisp.jisp_89_24","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 43岁男性，主诉左上后牙区疼痛伴牙齿松动3周\n- E2 [history]: 2型糖尿病史（随机血糖256 mg/dL），1月前曾行#36拔除术\n- E4 [opg]: 术前OPG示#21–#25根尖区边界不清低密度影\n- E5 [opg]: 术前根尖片示#21与#22根尖区边界不清低密度影\n- E6 [opg]: 术前咬合片示#21与#22腭侧边界清楚低密度影\n- E7 [symptom]: 根管治疗2周后出现面部中三分之一左侧肿胀\n- E8 [clinical_exam]: 术中见#22根尖区颊侧皮质骨缺损，取出坏死骨碎片、肉芽组织及囊性内容物送检\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Preoperative orthopantomogram revealing ill-defined radiolucency in the periapical region of #21 to #25\n- [intraoral_photo/radiograph] Preoperative intraoral periapical radiographic view revealing ill-defined radiolucency in the periapical region of #21 and #22\n- [radiograph] Preoperative occlusal radiograph revealing well-defined radiolucency in palatal aspect of #21 and #22\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/radiograph] Preoperative intraoral periapical radiographic view revealing ill-defined radiolucency in the periapical region of #21 and #22\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 43岁男性，主诉左上后牙区疼痛伴牙齿松动3周 诊断意义：支持上颌毛霉菌病的临床症状\n\n2. 2型糖尿病史（随机血糖256 mg/dL），1月前曾行#36拔除术 诊断意义：提示存在免疫抑制状态，为毛霉菌感染的风险因素\n\n3. 术前OPG及根尖片示#21–#25根尖区边界不清低密度影，咬合片示#21与#22腭侧边界清楚低密度影 诊断意义：影像学表现符合上颌骨病变特征\n\n4. 根管治疗2周后出现面部中三分之一左侧肿胀；术中见#22根尖区颊侧皮质骨缺损，取出坏死骨碎片、肉芽组织及囊性内容物送检 诊断意义：临床进展和手术所见进一步支持诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者有典型的临床症状、风险因素以及影像学和手术发现，支持上颌毛霉菌病的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理结果直接证实毛霉菌感染\n","answer":"\n上颌毛霉菌病（Maxillary mucormycosis）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Preoperative orthopantomogram revealing ill-defined radiolucency in the periapical region of #21 to #25\n- [intraoral_photo/radiograph] Preoperative intraoral periapical radiographic view revealing ill-defined radiolucency in the periapical region of #21 and #22\n- [radiograph] Preoperative occlusal radiograph revealing well-defined radiolucency in palatal aspect of #21 and #22\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/radiograph] Preoperative intraoral periapical radiographic view revealing ill-defined radiolucency in the periapical region of #21 and #22\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 43岁男性，主诉左上后牙区疼痛伴牙齿松动3周 诊断意义：支持上颌毛霉菌病的临床症状\n\n2. 2型糖尿病史（随机血糖256 mg/dL），1月前曾行#36拔除术 诊断意义：提示存在免疫抑制状态，为毛霉菌感染的风险因素\n\n3. 术前OPG及根尖片示#21–#25根尖区边界不清低密度影，咬合片示#21与#22腭侧边界清楚低密度影 诊断意义：影像学表现符合上颌骨病变特征\n\n4. 根管治疗2周后出现面部中三分之一左侧肿胀；术中见#22根尖区颊侧皮质骨缺损，取出坏死骨碎片、肉芽组织及囊性内容物送检 诊断意义：临床进展和手术所见进一步支持诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 患者有典型的临床症状、风险因素以及影像学和手术发现，支持上颌毛霉菌病的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理结果直接证实毛霉菌感染\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n上颌毛霉菌病（Maxillary mucormycosis）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC11864335/JISP-28-484-g002.jpg","name":"JISP-28-484-g002.jpg","caption":"Preoperative orthopantomogram revealing ill-defined radiolucency in the periapical region of #21 to #25","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"01a93618ad14f53cdf61730a9de3a402dac7f1bc6855ef8912e9ec8ba97f0143","width":493,"height":367},{"src":"assets/PMC11864335/JISP-28-484-g003.jpg","name":"JISP-28-484-g003.jpg","caption":"Preoperative intraoral periapical radiographic view revealing ill-defined radiolucency in the periapical region of #21 and #22","types":["intraoral_photo","radiograph"],"sha256":"63282c7002173b15f5a4a8c6f25ebb145b8cae0020245d43e704aa942357de1b","width":298,"height":366},{"src":"assets/PMC11864335/JISP-28-484-g004.jpg","name":"JISP-28-484-g004.jpg","caption":"Preoperative occlusal radiograph revealing well-defined radiolucency in palatal aspect of #21 and #22","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"5419038020858ca3da666023d50f6b5d094bbc00ed689af100ed95a0224f2d60","width":350,"height":367}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC6969963","title":"Transoral surgical approach to solitary fibrous tumors in buccal space with infratemporal tumor extension: A case report.","category":"mucosal_oral_lesion","license":"cc by","authors":["Andra Rizqiawan","Anindita Zahratur-Rasyida","Indra Mulyawan"],"journal":"Journal of clinical and experimental dentistry","year":"2020","citation":"Andra Rizqiawan, Anindita Zahratur-Rasyida, Indra Mulyawan. Transoral surgical approach to solitary fibrous tumors in buccal space with infratemporal tumor extension: A case report. Journal of clinical and experimental dentistry. 2020. doi: 10.4317/medoral.55736.","license_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/","licenseUrls":["http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright: © 2020 Medicina Oral S.L."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6969963/","doi":"10.4317/medoral.55736","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 25岁女性，左颊部无痛性肿块9个月，无牙痛或麻木，无既往病史\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 面部左侧不对称（图1A黑箭头所示），无红肿；触诊为深部、质韧、活动、无压痛肿块，直径约4 cm，位于颊间隙并延伸至左颧骨下方\n- E3 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查见左侧颊黏膜膨隆；触诊确认深部界限清楚、质韧、无压痛肿块\n- E4 [opg]: 曲面体层片（OPG）显示上、下颌骨无骨质破坏，36区有拔牙窝（2月前拔除）\n- E6 [other_imaging]: 增强CT显示轻度强化、边界清楚的软组织肿瘤（冠状、轴位、矢状位）\n- E7 [laboratory]: 细针穿刺活检示低细胞区伴红细胞及炎性细胞，无恶性证据；切取活检示广泛成纤维细胞增生，类似纤维瘤\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [ct/extraoral_photo/opg_panoramic] (A) Extra oral picture showed an asymmetry on the left cheek (black arrow) and (B) Orthopantomogram revealed no bone destruction of maxilla and mandible, (C) USG showed a hypoechoid solid mass on the left parotid area. (D) CT scan with contrast enhancement from coronal, axial, and sagital view revealed a slight enhancing soft tissue tumor with well border.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [ct/extraoral_photo/opg_panoramic] (A) Extra oral picture showed an asymmetry on the left cheek (black arrow) and (B) Orthopantomogram revealed no bone destruction of maxilla and mandible, (C) USG showed a hypoechoid solid mass on the left parotid area. (D) CT scan with contrast enhancement from coronal, axial, and sagital view revealed a slight enhancing soft tissue tumor with well border.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 25岁女性，左颊部无痛性肿块9个月，无牙痛或麻木，无既往病史 诊断意义：支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断\n\n2. 面部左侧不对称，触诊为深部、质韧、活动、无压痛肿块，直径约4 cm，位于颊间隙并延伸至左颧骨下方 诊断意义：支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断\n\n3. 口内检查见左侧颊黏膜膨隆；触诊确认深部界限清楚、质韧、无压痛肿块 诊断意义：支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断\n\n4. 增强CT显示轻度强化、边界清楚的软组织肿瘤，细针穿刺活检示低细胞区伴红细胞及炎性细胞，无恶性证据；切取活检示广泛成纤维细胞增生，类似纤维瘤 诊断意义：支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的病史、临床检查和影像学表现，以及病理结果，支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；病理结果未能提供特异性诊断依据以完全排除其他类型的良性肿瘤\n","answer":"\n孤立性纤维瘤（Solitary fibrous tumor）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [ct/extraoral_photo/opg_panoramic] (A) Extra oral picture showed an asymmetry on the left cheek (black arrow) and (B) Orthopantomogram revealed no bone destruction of maxilla and mandible, (C) USG showed a hypoechoid solid mass on the left parotid area. (D) CT scan with contrast enhancement from coronal, axial, and sagital view revealed a slight enhancing soft tissue tumor with well border.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [ct/extraoral_photo/opg_panoramic] (A) Extra oral picture showed an asymmetry on the left cheek (black arrow) and (B) Orthopantomogram revealed no bone destruction of maxilla and mandible, (C) USG showed a hypoechoid solid mass on the left parotid area. (D) CT scan with contrast enhancement from coronal, axial, and sagital view revealed a slight enhancing soft tissue tumor with well border.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 25岁女性，左颊部无痛性肿块9个月，无牙痛或麻木，无既往病史 诊断意义：支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断\n\n2. 面部左侧不对称，触诊为深部、质韧、活动、无压痛肿块，直径约4 cm，位于颊间隙并延伸至左颧骨下方 诊断意义：支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断\n\n3. 口内检查见左侧颊黏膜膨隆；触诊确认深部界限清楚、质韧、无压痛肿块 诊断意义：支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断\n\n4. 增强CT显示轻度强化、边界清楚的软组织肿瘤，细针穿刺活检示低细胞区伴红细胞及炎性细胞，无恶性证据；切取活检示广泛成纤维细胞增生，类似纤维瘤 诊断意义：支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的病史、临床检查和影像学表现，以及病理结果，支持孤立性纤维瘤的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；病理结果未能提供特异性诊断依据以完全排除其他类型的良性肿瘤\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n孤立性纤维瘤（Solitary fibrous tumor）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC6969963/jced-12-e93-g001.jpg","name":"jced-12-e93-g001.jpg","caption":"(A) Extra oral picture showed an asymmetry on the left cheek (black arrow) and (B) Orthopantomogram revealed no bone destruction of maxilla and mandible, (C) USG showed a hypoechoid solid mass on the left parotid area. (D) CT scan with contrast enhancement from coronal, axial, and sagital view revealed a slight enhancing soft tissue tumor with well border.","types":["ct","extraoral_photo","opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"3ac1a644a7c394c0602092337dac203d3349093ac6ad3fa1a20448276a93694e","width":726,"height":649}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12349912","title":"Asymptomatic Glandular Odontogenic Cyst of the Right Posterior Maxilla Involving the Maxillary Sinus: Case Report With Literature Review.","category":"odontogenic_cyst_tumor","license":"cc by","authors":["Mohammed H Albodbaij","Bander Y Alkarri","Israa A Alameer"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2025","citation":"Mohammed H Albodbaij, Bander Y Alkarri, Israa A Alameer. Asymptomatic Glandular Odontogenic Cyst of the Right Posterior Maxilla Involving the Maxillary Sinus: Case Report With Literature Review. Cureus. 2025. doi: 10.7759/cureus.87924.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025, Albodbaij et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12349912/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.87924","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 41岁男性，无症状，常规X线检查偶然发现右上颌后区透射影\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 无面部不对称、无面肿、无区域淋巴结肿大；口内检查无肿胀；#15–#17叩诊无痛；电活力测试示牙髓活力正常\n- E3 [rgb]: 口内照片显示右上颌后区无肿胀或感染征象\n- E5 [other_imaging]: CT示右上颌3.0×3.5×2.5 cm低密度病灶，边界清楚，累及#18，向近中延伸至#16、#17根尖区，侵犯上颌窦后外侧壁并致窦底黏膜增厚\n- E6 [other_imaging]: 初始影像学诊断倾向为角化囊性瘤（OKC）\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram showing well defined radiolucency with impacted #18\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral clinical photograph showing the right posterior maxilla with no evidence of swelling or signs of infection\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 41岁男性，无症状，常规X线检查偶然发现右上颌后区透射影。 诊断意义：支持存在囊性病变的可能\n\n2. CT示右上颌3.0×3.5×2.5 cm低密度病灶，边界清楚，累及#18，向近中延伸至#16、#17根尖区，侵犯上颌窦后外侧壁并致窦底黏膜增厚。 诊断意义：进一步支持了存在牙源性囊肿的可能性\n\n3. 无面部不对称、无面肿、无区域淋巴结肿大；口内检查无肿胀；#15–#17叩诊无痛；电活力测试示牙髓活力正常。 诊断意义：排除了感染或急性炎症的可能\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者无症状且偶然发现的右上颌后区透射影（E1），结合CT显示的具体影像特征（E5）和临床检查未见异常（E2），考虑腺性牙源性囊肿。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；初始影像学诊断倾向为角化囊性瘤（OKC）（E6），需通过病理确诊以区分腺性牙源性囊肿与其他类似病变\n","answer":"\n腺性牙源性囊肿（Glandular odontogenic cyst (GOC)）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram showing well defined radiolucency with impacted #18\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral clinical photograph showing the right posterior maxilla with no evidence of swelling or signs of infection\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 41岁男性，无症状，常规X线检查偶然发现右上颌后区透射影。 诊断意义：支持存在囊性病变的可能\n\n2. CT示右上颌3.0×3.5×2.5 cm低密度病灶，边界清楚，累及#18，向近中延伸至#16、#17根尖区，侵犯上颌窦后外侧壁并致窦底黏膜增厚。 诊断意义：进一步支持了存在牙源性囊肿的可能性\n\n3. 无面部不对称、无面肿、无区域淋巴结肿大；口内检查无肿胀；#15–#17叩诊无痛；电活力测试示牙髓活力正常。 诊断意义：排除了感染或急性炎症的可能\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者无症状且偶然发现的右上颌后区透射影（E1），结合CT显示的具体影像特征（E5）和临床检查未见异常（E2），考虑腺性牙源性囊肿。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；初始影像学诊断倾向为角化囊性瘤（OKC）（E6），需通过病理确诊以区分腺性牙源性囊肿与其他类似病变\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n腺性牙源性囊肿（Glandular odontogenic cyst (GOC)）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12349912/cureus-0017-00000087924-i02.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000087924-i02.jpg","caption":"Orthopantomogram showing well defined radiolucency with impacted #18","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"2db61c3d755c258e32a350eed81d2423b6439525e03f2685fe5977fc27598188","width":750,"height":390},{"src":"assets/PMC12349912/cureus-0017-00000087924-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000087924-i01.jpg","caption":"Intraoral clinical photograph showing the right posterior maxilla with no evidence of swelling or signs of infection","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"5ce76a60bf8fbab255c11c57e1175fb81030088d2cf380223b71aabc0742b3c1","width":750,"height":378}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12840320","title":"Digital Technologies in Diagnosing Solitary Median Maxillary Central Incisor Syndrome.","category":"oral_maxillofacial_other","license":"cc by","authors":["Katarzyna Cieślińska","Karolina Karbowska","Katarzyna Zaborowicz","Barbara Biedziak"],"journal":"Children (Basel, Switzerland)","year":"2025","citation":"Katarzyna Cieślińska, Karolina Karbowska, Katarzyna Zaborowicz, Barbara Biedziak. Digital Technologies in Diagnosing Solitary Median Maxillary Central Incisor Syndrome. Children (Basel, Switzerland). 2025. doi: 10.3390/children13010011.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland. This article is an open access article distributed under the terms and conditions of the Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) license.","copyright":["© 2025 by the authors."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12840320/","doi":"10.3390/children13010011","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E3 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查见上唇系带与切牙乳头发育不良、上颌缩窄、腭中线嵴明显、上牙弓呈V形（图9）\n- E4 [clinical_exam]: 单中切牙冠形态对称，尺寸9.8×8.1 mm，无Mühlreiter角（图10、11）\n- E5 [opg]: OPG显示上颌正中单颗中切牙，根尖发育正常，单根管腔（图17）\n- E6 [rgb]: 临床照片显示鼻部外观（图1），结合病史提示鼻腔通道狭窄；患者表现为混合型口-鼻呼吸、口轮匝肌张力减低\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph of the patient.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Clinical image showing the patient’s nostrils.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 口内检查见上唇系带与切牙乳头发育不良、上颌缩窄、腭中线嵴明显、上牙弓呈V形。 诊断意义：支持单中切牙综合征的诊断\n\n2. 单中切牙冠形态对称，尺寸9.8×8.1 mm，无Mühlreiter角。 诊断意义：支持单中切牙综合征的诊断\n\n3. OPG显示上颌正中单颗中切牙，根尖发育正常，单根管腔。 诊断意义：支持单中切牙综合征的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 口内检查发现上唇系带与切牙乳头发育不良、上颌缩窄、腭中线嵴明显及上牙弓呈V形；结合单中切牙冠形态对称且无Mühlreiter角以及OPG影像学特征，支持单中切牙综合征的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；鼻部外观和呼吸方式异常可能与其他疾病相关，这些证据不能单独用于确诊单中切牙综合征。\n","answer":"\n单中切牙综合征（Solitary Median Maxillary Central Incisor Syndrome）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph of the patient.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Clinical image showing the patient’s nostrils.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 口内检查见上唇系带与切牙乳头发育不良、上颌缩窄、腭中线嵴明显、上牙弓呈V形。 诊断意义：支持单中切牙综合征的诊断\n\n2. 单中切牙冠形态对称，尺寸9.8×8.1 mm，无Mühlreiter角。 诊断意义：支持单中切牙综合征的诊断\n\n3. OPG显示上颌正中单颗中切牙，根尖发育正常，单根管腔。 诊断意义：支持单中切牙综合征的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 口内检查发现上唇系带与切牙乳头发育不良、上颌缩窄、腭中线嵴明显及上牙弓呈V形；结合单中切牙冠形态对称且无Mühlreiter角以及OPG影像学特征，支持单中切牙综合征的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；鼻部外观和呼吸方式异常可能与其他疾病相关，这些证据不能单独用于确诊单中切牙综合征。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n单中切牙综合征（Solitary Median Maxillary Central Incisor Syndrome）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12840320/children-13-00011-g017.jpg","name":"children-13-00011-g017.jpg","caption":"Panoramic radiograph of the patient.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"0a046f9e4d92f69a9e1282ca8ed01fcf89978a20aabc718ff39753ae8304d49b","width":768,"height":370},{"src":"assets/PMC12840320/children-13-00011-g001.jpg","name":"children-13-00011-g001.jpg","caption":"Clinical image showing the patient’s nostrils.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"c13a67aabd755a324ee77a2244a4c8cae3907e3f170a6e8ccb39615a9d774d08","width":789,"height":1138}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC11178394","title":"External Cervical Resorption Detected by Cone Beam Computed Tomography on an Immature, Unerupted Maxillary Second Premolar.","category":"developmental_eruption","license":"cc by","authors":["Karen Berrigan","Bradly Gettleman","Sabita Rao","Janet Jordan","Mark Stieg","Lawrence Johns"],"journal":"Case reports in dentistry","year":"2024","citation":"Karen Berrigan, Bradly Gettleman, Sabita Rao, Janet Jordan, Mark Stieg, Lawrence Johns. External Cervical Resorption Detected by Cone Beam Computed Tomography on an Immature, Unerupted Maxillary Second Premolar. Case reports in dentistry. 2024. doi: 10.1155/2024/6590778.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2024 Karen Berrigan et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11178394/","doi":"10.1155/2024/6590778","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E4 [other_imaging]: CBCT由口腔颌面放射科医师判读，根管专科医师会诊认为该透射影最可能为牙颈部外吸收（ECR）\n- E6 [clinical_exam]: 牙髓活力测试：电测法46/80，冷测短时阳性，提示牙髓无炎症性改变\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Initial screening panoramic radiograph.\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Progress panoramic radiograph eleven months into orthodontic treatment, # A still retained.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n","think":"\n1. CBCT由口腔颌面放射科医师判读，根管专科医师会诊认为该透射影最可能为牙颈部外吸收（ECR）。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 牙髓活力测试：电测法46/80，冷测短时阳性，提示牙髓无炎症性改变。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据CBCT影像及专家会诊意见，以及牙髓活力测试结果，考虑存在牙颈部外吸收。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有证据不足以区分具体的Patel或Heithersay分类。\n","answer":"\n重度牙颈部外吸收（Patel 3Cd / Heithersay IV型）（Patel Classification 3Cd/Class 4 Heithersay ECR）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Initial screening panoramic radiograph.\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Progress panoramic radiograph eleven months into orthodontic treatment, # A still retained.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例保留诊断阶段的放射影像证据，未提供可独立核对的诊断前临床照片。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. CBCT由口腔颌面放射科医师判读，根管专科医师会诊认为该透射影最可能为牙颈部外吸收（ECR）。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 牙髓活力测试：电测法46/80，冷测短时阳性，提示牙髓无炎症性改变。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据CBCT影像及专家会诊意见，以及牙髓活力测试结果，考虑存在牙颈部外吸收。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有证据不足以区分具体的Patel或Heithersay分类。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n重度牙颈部外吸收（Patel 3Cd / Heithersay IV型）（Patel Classification 3Cd/Class 4 Heithersay ECR）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC11178394/CRID2024-6590778.001.jpg","name":"CRID2024-6590778.001.jpg","caption":"Initial screening panoramic radiograph.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"a21f327ebe215d75be0a7e5f5a84afbe90d2f1567eab36616fc6a49027dd12dc","width":355,"height":170},{"src":"assets/PMC11178394/CRID2024-6590778.002.jpg","name":"CRID2024-6590778.002.jpg","caption":"Progress panoramic radiograph eleven months into orthodontic treatment, # A still retained.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"a13614bb19b2e5638c987c4638478036c8da8320d362707706e1c2192a8874de","width":355,"height":171}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC9126466","title":"A novel approach in diagnosing multiple dentigerous cysts using CBCT illustration indicative of Mucopolysaccharidosis VI - a case report.","category":"other_dental","license":"cc by","authors":["Shalu Rai","Deepankar Misra","Akansha Misra","Ankit Jain","Ashish Verma","Dimple Grover","Ayesha Haris"],"journal":"Journal of medicine and life","year":"2022","citation":"Shalu Rai, Deepankar Misra, Akansha Misra, Ankit Jain, Ashish Verma, Dimple Grover, Ayesha Haris. A novel approach in diagnosing multiple dentigerous cysts using CBCT illustration indicative of Mucopolysaccharidosis VI - a case report. Journal of medicine and life. 2022. doi: 10.25122/jml-2021-0288.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/This article is distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/), which permits unrestricted use and redistribution provided that the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["©2022 JOURNAL of MEDICINE and LIFE"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9126466/","doi":"10.25122/jml-2021-0288","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 18岁男性，主诉左上颌前牙区面部肿胀伴脓性分泌物6个月\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 体征：巨头、左眼角膜混浊、鼻梁扁平、浓眉、眼距过宽\n- E3 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查：巨舌、厚唇、腺样体肥大、恒牙萌出延迟、高拱腭\n- E6 [opg]: 曲面断层片显示上下颌多发与未萌牙相关的囊样透射影\n- E8 [laboratory]: 尿GAG升高（134 mg/g Cr，正常19.97–110.53），ARSB酶活性降低（83.26 nmol/mg/h，正常>121）\n- E9 [other_imaging]: 胸片与头颈正位片未见锁骨缺如、颅缝增宽、蝶鞍钙化或颈椎融合等特征性骨异常\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph showing multiple cyst-like lesions associated with unerupted teeth in the jaws.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Clinical photograph showing corneal opacity.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者存在左上颌前牙区面部肿胀伴脓性分泌物6个月，提示可能有局部感染或发育异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 体征如巨头、角膜混浊、鼻梁扁平及口内巨舌等特征符合黏多糖贮积症的临床表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 曲面断层片显示上下颌多发与未萌牙相关的囊样透射影，进一步支持了骨骼系统受累的可能性。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 尿GAG升高及ARSB酶活性降低直接指向了黏多糖贮积症VI型的诊断。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床症状、体征以及实验室检查结果，支持黏多糖贮积症VI型（Maroteaux-Lamy综合征）的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；胸片与头颈正位片未见特定骨异常，但不影响主要诊断依据。\n","answer":"\n黏多糖贮积症VI型（Maroteaux-Lamy综合征）（Mucopolysaccharidosis VI (Maroteaux-Lamy syndrome)）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Panoramic radiograph showing multiple cyst-like lesions associated with unerupted teeth in the jaws.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Clinical photograph showing corneal opacity.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者存在左上颌前牙区面部肿胀伴脓性分泌物6个月，提示可能有局部感染或发育异常。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 体征如巨头、角膜混浊、鼻梁扁平及口内巨舌等特征符合黏多糖贮积症的临床表现。 诊断意义：支持\n\n3. 曲面断层片显示上下颌多发与未萌牙相关的囊样透射影，进一步支持了骨骼系统受累的可能性。 诊断意义：支持\n\n4. 尿GAG升高及ARSB酶活性降低直接指向了黏多糖贮积症VI型的诊断。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的临床症状、体征以及实验室检查结果，支持黏多糖贮积症VI型（Maroteaux-Lamy综合征）的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；胸片与头颈正位片未见特定骨异常，但不影响主要诊断依据。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n黏多糖贮积症VI型（Maroteaux-Lamy综合征）（Mucopolysaccharidosis VI (Maroteaux-Lamy syndrome)）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC9126466/JMedLife-15-579-g004.jpg","name":"JMedLife-15-579-g004.jpg","caption":"Panoramic radiograph showing multiple cyst-like lesions associated with unerupted teeth in the jaws.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"8fa071c98d773dbb3509cb605c810247430a4506c32ff6e73b431fa598754e33","width":669,"height":343},{"src":"assets/PMC9126466/JMedLife-15-579-g001.jpg","name":"JMedLife-15-579-g001.jpg","caption":"Clinical photograph showing corneal opacity.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"3861a8f74ae6259f5381ab6a4c619b189a27f0ed2995387748572241b265fb11","width":709,"height":407}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC11297549","title":"Metastatic Sarcomatoid Renal Cell Carcinoma: A Journey From the Kidney to the Gingiva.","category":"periodontal","license":"cc by","authors":["Zainab Kamal","Chandergupt Singh","Shruti Tandon","Arundeep K Lamba","Aadithya B Urs","Shivangni Rajoria"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2024","citation":"Zainab Kamal, Chandergupt Singh, Shruti Tandon, Arundeep K Lamba, Aadithya B Urs, Shivangni Rajoria. Metastatic Sarcomatoid Renal Cell Carcinoma: A Journey From the Kidney to the Gingiva. Cureus. 2024. doi: 10.7759/cureus.63827.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2024, Kamal et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11297549/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.63827","question":"\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E3 [opg]: OPG及根尖片显示44、45牙周间隙增宽，44、45、46牙槽嵴顶骨吸收；46牙根分叉区轻度透射影，提示咬合创伤\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的OPG细节。\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例没有可与诊断时间点可靠对应的非病理图片，诊断推理仅依据病例文字信息。\n","think":"\n1. OPG及根尖片显示44、45牙周间隙增宽，44、45、46牙槽嵴顶骨吸收；46牙根分叉区轻度透射影，提示咬合创伤。 诊断意义：这些影像学发现指向了局部的口腔疾病或损伤，但不直接支持转移性肉瘤样肾细胞癌的诊断。\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据当前提供的证据，主要观察到的是与牙齿相关的结构性变化和潜在的咬合创伤迹象，缺乏特异性指向转移性肉瘤样肾细胞癌的信息。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有的影像学证据仅反映了局部口腔状况的变化，并不足以区分最终诊断为转移性肉瘤样肾细胞癌。\n","answer":"\n转移性肉瘤样肾细胞癌（Metastatic sarcomatoid renal cell carcinoma）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的OPG细节。\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- 原记录未提供可保留的RGB细节。\nCross-modal summary: 本例没有可与诊断时间点可靠对应的非病理图片，诊断推理仅依据病例文字信息。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. OPG及根尖片显示44、45牙周间隙增宽，44、45、46牙槽嵴顶骨吸收；46牙根分叉区轻度透射影，提示咬合创伤。 诊断意义：这些影像学发现指向了局部的口腔疾病或损伤，但不直接支持转移性肉瘤样肾细胞癌的诊断。\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据当前提供的证据，主要观察到的是与牙齿相关的结构性变化和潜在的咬合创伤迹象，缺乏特异性指向转移性肉瘤样肾细胞癌的信息。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；现有的影像学证据仅反映了局部口腔状况的变化，并不足以区分最终诊断为转移性肉瘤样肾细胞癌。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n转移性肉瘤样肾细胞癌（Metastatic sarcomatoid renal cell carcinoma）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[],"english":null},{"id":"PMC6150708","title":"Canine transposition as an alternative to trauma of the maxillary incisors: case report.","category":"trauma_resorption","license":"cc by","authors":["María Salcedo Lara","Rocío Briones Rodríguez","María Biedma Perea","Beatriz Solano Mendoza"],"journal":"Dental press journal of orthodontics","year":"2018","citation":"María Salcedo Lara, Rocío Briones Rodríguez, María Biedma Perea, Beatriz Solano Mendoza. Canine transposition as an alternative to trauma of the maxillary incisors: case report. Dental press journal of orthodontics. 2018. doi: 10.1590/2177-6709.23.4.055-063.oar.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License","copyright":["© 2018 Dental Press Journal of Orthodontics"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6150708/","doi":"10.1590/2177-6709.23.4.055-063.oar","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [demographics|symptom]: 9岁女性，第二期混合牙列，主诉左上中切牙萌出延迟\n- E2 [history]: 2岁时曾有外伤史，致乳上颌左侧中切牙嵌入性脱位\n- E3 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查：上颌左侧中切牙缺失；双侧磨牙I类关系；覆𬌗为对刃；中线左偏3mm\n- E4 [opg]: 全景片显示：上颌左侧中切牙异位，冠位于右侧中切牙根尖水平，根尖位于左侧尖牙水平；左侧侧切牙冠移向中切牙间隙；左侧尖牙未按正常顺序萌出，位于侧切牙根尖水平\n- E5 [other_imaging]: 侧位头影测量示轻度骨性II类（上颌型），SNA=87°，SNB=81°，ANB=6°；下颌平面角增大（SN.GoGn=39°）；上下前牙唇倾\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Pre-treatment panoramic radiograph.\n- [radiograph] Pre-treatment lateral cephalometric radiograph and tracing.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Pre-treatment facial and intraoral photographs, and pretreatment dental casts.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 9岁女性处于第二期混合牙列阶段，且主诉左上中切牙萌出延迟。 诊断意义：支持诊断\n\n2. 患者有2岁时的外伤史，导致乳上颌左侧中切牙发生嵌入性脱位。 诊断意义：支持诊断\n\n3. 全景片显示上颌左侧中切牙异位，冠部位于右侧中切牙根尖水平，而其根尖则位于左侧尖牙区域，同时左侧尖牙未按正常顺序萌出，这表明了牙位交换的可能性。 诊断意义：支持诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的年龄、牙齿发育阶段以及主诉（E1），结合早期外伤史（E2）和影像学检查发现的牙齿位置异常（E4），提示上颌左侧中切牙因乳牙创伤性嵌入导致异位萌出，并继发左侧尖牙与中切牙位置互换。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏直接证据证明当前牙齿排列异常与早年外伤之间的确切因果关系。\n","answer":"\n上颌左侧中切牙因乳牙创伤性嵌入导致异位萌出，继发左侧尖牙与中切牙位置互换（牙位交换）（Canine transposition secondary to traumatic intrusion of deciduous maxillary left central incisor resulting in ectopic permanent central incisor）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic/radiograph] Pre-treatment panoramic radiograph.\n- [radiograph] Pre-treatment lateral cephalometric radiograph and tracing.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Pre-treatment facial and intraoral photographs, and pretreatment dental casts.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 9岁女性处于第二期混合牙列阶段，且主诉左上中切牙萌出延迟。 诊断意义：支持诊断\n\n2. 患者有2岁时的外伤史，导致乳上颌左侧中切牙发生嵌入性脱位。 诊断意义：支持诊断\n\n3. 全景片显示上颌左侧中切牙异位，冠部位于右侧中切牙根尖水平，而其根尖则位于左侧尖牙区域，同时左侧尖牙未按正常顺序萌出，这表明了牙位交换的可能性。 诊断意义：支持诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据患者的年龄、牙齿发育阶段以及主诉（E1），结合早期外伤史（E2）和影像学检查发现的牙齿位置异常（E4），提示上颌左侧中切牙因乳牙创伤性嵌入导致异位萌出，并继发左侧尖牙与中切牙位置互换。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏直接证据证明当前牙齿排列异常与早年外伤之间的确切因果关系。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n上颌左侧中切牙因乳牙创伤性嵌入导致异位萌出，继发左侧尖牙与中切牙位置互换（牙位交换）（Canine transposition secondary to traumatic intrusion of deciduous maxillary left central incisor resulting in ectopic permanent central incisor）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC6150708/2176-9451-dpjo-23-04-00055-gf2.jpg","name":"2176-9451-dpjo-23-04-00055-gf2.jpg","caption":"Pre-treatment panoramic radiograph.","types":["opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"0fd53ac86a192677693b5bec0761cf7113c4e63496eda08a88a5e241835baab8","width":557,"height":250},{"src":"assets/PMC6150708/2176-9451-dpjo-23-04-00055-gf1.jpg","name":"2176-9451-dpjo-23-04-00055-gf1.jpg","caption":"Pre-treatment facial and intraoral photographs, and pretreatment dental casts.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"24027ddabb358f177afdd2d50566fb24c9cc07d853dd9f0ffd6693853d02de7a","width":568,"height":710},{"src":"assets/PMC6150708/2176-9451-dpjo-23-04-00055-gf3.jpg","name":"2176-9451-dpjo-23-04-00055-gf3.jpg","caption":"Pre-treatment lateral cephalometric radiograph and tracing.","types":["radiograph"],"sha256":"29cfbb6632ee7e77e6139e620de9563b90dd1e6a1e434b49a8233c13ef849caf","width":557,"height":323}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC9241206","title":"A rare case of multiple brain abscesses caused by apical periodontitis of deciduous teeth in congenital heart disease: a case report.","category":"endodontic_periapical","license":"cc by","authors":["Shizuka Takahashi","Hisato Segoe","Takashi Kikuiri","Yuji Maruo","Tomonobu Sato","Yutaka Watanabe","Zhao Jimei","Yoshitaka Yoshimura","Misa Ishiyama","Atsuhito Takeda","Yasutaka Yawaka","Tetsuo Shirakawa"],"journal":"BMC oral health","year":"2022","citation":"Shizuka Takahashi, Hisato Segoe, Takashi Kikuiri, Yuji Maruo, Tomonobu Sato, Yutaka Watanabe, Zhao Jimei, Yoshitaka Yoshimura, Misa Ishiyama, Atsuhito Takeda, Yasutaka Yawaka, Tetsuo Shirakawa. A rare case of multiple brain abscesses caused by apical periodontitis of deciduous teeth in congenital heart disease: a case report. BMC oral health. 2022. doi: 10.1186/s12903-022-02294-z.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/Open AccessThis article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, which permits use, sharing, adaptation, distribution and reproduction in any medium or format, as long as you give appropriate credit to the original author(s) and the source, provide a link to the Creative Commons licence, and indicate if changes were made. The images or other third party material in this article are included in the article's Creative Commons licence, unless indicated otherwise in a credit line to the material. If material is not included in the article's Creative Commons licence and your intended use is not permitted by statutory regulation or exceeds the permitted use, you will need to obtain permission directly from the copyright holder. To view a copy of this licence, visit http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. The Creative Commons Public Domain Dedication waiver (http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/) applies to the data made available in this article, unless otherwise stated in a credit line to the data.","copyright":["© The Author(s) 2022"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9241206/","doi":"10.1186/s12903-022-02294-z","question":"<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [demographics]: 7岁8个月男性，患有复杂先天性心脏病（完全型房室间隔缺损、肺动脉闭锁等）\n- E3 [laboratory]: 血培养检出中间链球菌与金黄色葡萄球菌\n- E7 [history]: 既往牙科检查认为无需牙科治疗\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical and radiographic findings of the patient at the initial visit. Intraoral photograph (A and B) and panoramic radiograph (C). Yellow arrows indicate apical periodontitis\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical and radiographic findings of the patient at the initial visit. Intraoral photograph (A and B) and panoramic radiograph (C). Yellow arrows indicate apical periodontitis\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者为7岁8个月男性，患有复杂先天性心脏病（完全型房室间隔缺损、肺动脉闭锁等），表明存在易感因素。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 血培养检出中间链球菌与金黄色葡萄球菌，提示细菌感染的存在。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 该患儿具有复杂先心病史，且血培养结果阳性，符合由口腔源性感染引发的多发性脑脓肿诊断条件。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不足以直接证实乳牙根尖周炎是引起脑脓肿的具体原因；既往牙科检查认为无需治疗，但不能排除潜在的感染源。\n","answer":"\n由乳牙根尖周炎引起的多发性脑脓肿（Multiple brain abscesses caused by apical periodontitis of deciduous teeth）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical and radiographic findings of the patient at the initial visit. Intraoral photograph (A and B) and panoramic radiograph (C). Yellow arrows indicate apical periodontitis\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Clinical and radiographic findings of the patient at the initial visit. Intraoral photograph (A and B) and panoramic radiograph (C). Yellow arrows indicate apical periodontitis\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者为7岁8个月男性，患有复杂先天性心脏病（完全型房室间隔缺损、肺动脉闭锁等），表明存在易感因素。 诊断意义：支持\n\n2. 血培养检出中间链球菌与金黄色葡萄球菌，提示细菌感染的存在。 诊断意义：支持\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 该患儿具有复杂先心病史，且血培养结果阳性，符合由口腔源性感染引发的多发性脑脓肿诊断条件。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；证据不足以直接证实乳牙根尖周炎是引起脑脓肿的具体原因；既往牙科检查认为无需治疗，但不能排除潜在的感染源。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n由乳牙根尖周炎引起的多发性脑脓肿（Multiple brain abscesses caused by apical periodontitis of deciduous teeth）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC9241206/12903_2022_2294_Fig3_HTML.jpg","name":"12903_2022_2294_Fig3_HTML.jpg","caption":"Clinical and radiographic findings of the patient at the initial visit. Intraoral photograph (A and B) and panoramic radiograph (C). Yellow arrows indicate apical periodontitis","types":["intraoral_photo","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"bb578f9a2c69e58fa8f6b2464f0ca2e9527a88a57bf01d80bc4b16ecd65ddcca","width":896,"height":814}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12815613","title":"Central Odontogenic Fibroma of the Mandible: A Case Report.","category":"odontogenic_cyst_tumor","license":"cc by","authors":["Nivetha D","Christeffi Mabel","Abimathi R","Chamundeeswari P","Sakthi Sreedevi"],"journal":"Cureus","year":"2025","citation":"Nivetha D, Christeffi Mabel, Abimathi R, Chamundeeswari P, Sakthi Sreedevi. Central Odontogenic Fibroma of the Mandible: A Case Report. Cureus. 2025. doi: 10.7759/cureus.99735.","license_url":null,"licenseUrls":[],"licenseText":"This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License CC-BY 4.0., which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.","copyright":["Copyright © 2025, D et al."],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12815613/","doi":"10.7759/cureus.99735","question":"<image>\n<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 19岁男性，主诉左下面部疼痛5天，伴张口时下颌锁结2个月；无相关全身及口腔病史\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查见47未萌出，覆盖黏膜正常，无肿胀或黏膜异常\n- E3 [rgb]: 口内照片显示47区域黏膜正常，无可见黏膜异常（图1）\n- E4 [opg]: OPG示47阻生，冠周见约1×1 cm边界清晰、单房、皮质缘的透射影，包绕CEJ（图2）\n- E5 [other_imaging]: CBCT示47冠周见边界清晰低密度影，伴一灶性高密度影，病变限于牙冠区，邻近下牙槽神经管上壁（图3）\n- E6 [other_imaging]: 影像学鉴别诊断包括：含牙囊肿、牙源性角化囊肿、单囊型成釉细胞瘤；因存在内部高密度影，另考虑COF、牙源性黏液瘤、钙化上皮瘤\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram (OPG) showing impacted 47 with lesionOrthopantomogram demonstrating an unerupted mandibular right second molar (47) with a well-defined radiolucency surrounding the coronal portion of the tooth (red arrow). The radiolucent area appears unilocular with a corticated margin and is confined to the crown region of 47.\n- [cbct/ct] CBCT view showing impacted 47 with hypodense lesion Cone-Beam Computed Tomography (CBCT) sagittal section showing an impacted mandibular right second molar (47) associated with a well-defined pericoronal hypodense area. A small focal speck of internal radiopacity is noted within the hypodensity (blue arrow), with the lesion confined to the coronal aspect of the impacted tooth 47. CBCT was used for three‑dimensional assessment as recommended for precise localization of odontogenic lesions.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral image showing unerupted 47Preoperative intraoral clinical photograph showing normal oral mucosa overlying the region of the unerupted mandibular right second molar (47) (blue arrow), with no visible mucosal abnormality.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者主诉左下面部疼痛5天，伴张口时下颌锁结2个月。 诊断意义：支持存在局部病变\n\n2. OPG显示47阻生，冠周见约1×1 cm边界清晰、单房、皮质缘的透射影，包绕CEJ。 诊断意义：支持中央性牙源性纤维瘤的影像学表现\n\n3. CBCT进一步示47冠周见边界清晰低密度影，伴一灶性高密度影，病变限于牙冠区。 诊断意义：支持中央性牙源性纤维瘤的影像学特征\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于病史及影像学检查，考虑为中央性牙源性纤维瘤。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；影像学鉴别诊断包括含牙囊肿、牙源性角化囊肿、单囊型成釉细胞瘤等，需结合病理结果以确诊。\n","answer":"\n中央性牙源性纤维瘤（Central Odontogenic Fibroma）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [opg_panoramic] Orthopantomogram (OPG) showing impacted 47 with lesionOrthopantomogram demonstrating an unerupted mandibular right second molar (47) with a well-defined radiolucency surrounding the coronal portion of the tooth (red arrow). The radiolucent area appears unilocular with a corticated margin and is confined to the crown region of 47.\n- [cbct/ct] CBCT view showing impacted 47 with hypodense lesion Cone-Beam Computed Tomography (CBCT) sagittal section showing an impacted mandibular right second molar (47) associated with a well-defined pericoronal hypodense area. A small focal speck of internal radiopacity is noted within the hypodensity (blue arrow), with the lesion confined to the coronal aspect of the impacted tooth 47. CBCT was used for three‑dimensional assessment as recommended for precise localization of odontogenic lesions.\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral image showing unerupted 47Preoperative intraoral clinical photograph showing normal oral mucosa overlying the region of the unerupted mandibular right second molar (47) (blue arrow), with no visible mucosal abnormality.\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者主诉左下面部疼痛5天，伴张口时下颌锁结2个月。 诊断意义：支持存在局部病变\n\n2. OPG显示47阻生，冠周见约1×1 cm边界清晰、单房、皮质缘的透射影，包绕CEJ。 诊断意义：支持中央性牙源性纤维瘤的影像学表现\n\n3. CBCT进一步示47冠周见边界清晰低密度影，伴一灶性高密度影，病变限于牙冠区。 诊断意义：支持中央性牙源性纤维瘤的影像学特征\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 基于病史及影像学检查，考虑为中央性牙源性纤维瘤。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；影像学鉴别诊断包括含牙囊肿、牙源性角化囊肿、单囊型成釉细胞瘤等，需结合病理结果以确诊。\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n中央性牙源性纤维瘤（Central Odontogenic Fibroma）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12815613/cureus-0017-00000099735-i02.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000099735-i02.jpg","caption":"Orthopantomogram (OPG) showing impacted 47 with lesionOrthopantomogram demonstrating an unerupted mandibular right second molar (47) with a well-defined radiolucency surrounding the coronal portion of the tooth (red arrow). The radiolucent area appears unilocular with a corticated margin and is confined to the crown region of 47.","types":["opg_panoramic"],"sha256":"4373f98b83ea14f3a91fb1591d86eea7ac37236de728315c66c66ebee379ae90","width":750,"height":390},{"src":"assets/PMC12815613/cureus-0017-00000099735-i01.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000099735-i01.jpg","caption":"Intraoral image showing unerupted 47Preoperative intraoral clinical photograph showing normal oral mucosa overlying the region of the unerupted mandibular right second molar (47) (blue arrow), with no visible mucosal abnormality.","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"d6340b24db242b57f9ba18afc6f2fbcb5f75d6807c8cbbbd3f8fa313a7e63f05","width":750,"height":542},{"src":"assets/PMC12815613/cureus-0017-00000099735-i03.jpg","name":"cureus-0017-00000099735-i03.jpg","caption":"CBCT view showing impacted 47 with hypodense lesion Cone-Beam Computed Tomography (CBCT) sagittal section showing an impacted mandibular right second molar (47) associated with a well-defined pericoronal hypodense area. A small focal speck of internal radiopacity is noted within the hypodensity (blue arrow), with the lesion confined to the coronal aspect of the impacted tooth 47. CBCT was used for three‑dimensional assessment as recommended for precise localization of odontogenic lesions.","types":["cbct","ct"],"sha256":"98a133fb87a444dbc0fb4110fb0cf22107901244970431772657349ac904a3b8","width":750,"height":879}],"english":null},{"id":"PMC12606825","title":"Unveiling the mandibular mystery: a case of central giant cell granuloma in posterior mandibular region-a case report.","category":"oral_maxillofacial_other","license":"cc by","authors":["Aakanksha Tiwari","Suwarna Dangore-Khasbage"],"journal":"Journal of medical case reports","year":"2025","citation":"Aakanksha Tiwari, Suwarna Dangore-Khasbage. Unveiling the mandibular mystery: a case of central giant cell granuloma in posterior mandibular region-a case report. Journal of medical case reports. 2025. doi: 10.1186/s13256-025-05613-4.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","licenseUrls":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"licenseText":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/Open Access This article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, which permits use, sharing, adaptation, distribution and reproduction in any medium or format, as long as you give appropriate credit to the original author(s) and the source, provide a link to the Creative Commons licence, and indicate if changes were made. The images or other third party material in this article are included in the article's Creative Commons licence, unless indicated otherwise in a credit line to the material. If material is not included in the article's Creative Commons licence and your intended use is not permitted by statutory regulation or exceeds the permitted use, you will need to obtain permission directly from the copyright holder. To view a copy of this licence, visit http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.","copyright":["© The Author(s) 2025"],"sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12606825/","doi":"10.1186/s13256-025-05613-4","question":"<image>\n<image>\nKnown case information (available during the diagnostic work-up):\n- E1 [history]: 37岁印度女性，左下后牙区疼痛性进行性膨隆4个月，伴左侧下颌面部麻木感\n- E2 [clinical_exam]: 口内检查见36至38区弥漫性肿胀，累及颊舌侧，36远中根缺失、37与38松动\n- E3 [clinical_exam]: 口外检查见左下颌4×6 cm质韧、压痛性弥漫性肿胀，范围从颏旁联合至下颌角\n- E4 [opg]: OPG示左侧下颌体部大型多房透射影，伴37、38牙根吸收及下颌下缘皮质变薄\n- E5 [other_imaging]: CT三维重建示左下颌体部边界不清的骨破坏；轴位像见病变膨胀性生长并穿破颊侧皮质板；冠状位见下颌下缘变薄\n- E6 [laboratory]: 血清钙、磷、碱性磷酸酶正常，排除甲状旁腺功能亢进\n- E7 [other_imaging]: 细针穿刺细胞学（FNAC）阴性，提示为实性病变\n- E8 [history]: 既往2月前同区域有牙折史，否认近期外伤史\n\n请结合实际提供的牙科图像与病例信息完成诊断。先在 <Caption> 中按实际提供的模态分别描述可见表现，不得臆造未提供的 OPG、RGB 或 CBCT；再在 <Think> 中按证据顺序给出简洁诊断推理、比较合理鉴别诊断，并说明现有证据不能确定的内容；最后在 <Answer> 中给出最终诊断。不得添加病例中没有的患者事实。","caption":"\nOPG:\n- [ct/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic findings: A Cropped orthopantomogram showing a large, multilocular radiolucency in the left mandible with resorption of the roots of teeth 37 and 38. B Three-dimensional computed tomography reconstruction illustrating ill-defined bone destruction. C Axial computed tomography view demonstrating the expansile nature of the lesion and perforation of the buccal cortical plate (arrowhead). D Coronal computed tomography view showing thinning of the inferior border (arrow)\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral swelling on buccal and lingual aspect in 36 to 38 region denoted by black arrow\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n","think":"\n1. 患者左下后牙区疼痛性进行性膨隆4个月，伴左侧下颌面部麻木感。 诊断意义：支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断\n\n2. 口内检查见36至38区弥漫性肿胀，累及颊舌侧，36远中根缺失、37与38松动。 诊断意义：支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断\n\n3. OPG示左侧下颌体部大型多房透射影，伴37、38牙根吸收及下颌下缘皮质变薄。 诊断意义：支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断\n\n4. CT三维重建示左下颌体部边界不清的骨破坏；轴位像见病变膨胀性生长并穿破颊侧皮质板；冠状位见下颌下缘变薄。 诊断意义：支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据病史（E1）、临床检查（E2）以及影像学表现（E4, E5），支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理结果以最终确诊\n","answer":"\n中央性巨细胞肉芽肿（central giant cell granuloma）\n","rawResponse":"<Caption>\nOPG:\n- [ct/opg_panoramic/radiograph] Radiographic findings: A Cropped orthopantomogram showing a large, multilocular radiolucency in the left mandible with resorption of the roots of teeth 37 and 38. B Three-dimensional computed tomography reconstruction illustrating ill-defined bone destruction. C Axial computed tomography view demonstrating the expansile nature of the lesion and perforation of the buccal cortical plate (arrowhead). D Coronal computed tomography view showing thinning of the inferior border (arrow)\nRGB clinical photograph:\n- [intraoral_photo] Intraoral swelling on buccal and lingual aspect in 36 to 38 region denoted by black arrow\nCross-modal summary: 放射影像用于评估牙位、病变边界及骨性改变，临床照片用于评估对应的牙体或软组织外观；两类证据需与病史和检查结果联合解释。\n</Caption>\n<Think>\n1. 患者左下后牙区疼痛性进行性膨隆4个月，伴左侧下颌面部麻木感。 诊断意义：支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断\n\n2. 口内检查见36至38区弥漫性肿胀，累及颊舌侧，36远中根缺失、37与38松动。 诊断意义：支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断\n\n3. OPG示左侧下颌体部大型多房透射影，伴37、38牙根吸收及下颌下缘皮质变薄。 诊断意义：支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断\n\n4. CT三维重建示左下颌体部边界不清的骨破坏；轴位像见病变膨胀性生长并穿破颊侧皮质板；冠状位见下颌下缘变薄。 诊断意义：支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断\n\nDifferential diagnosis comparison:\n- 原病例记录未保留可追溯的具体鉴别诊断，不额外编造。\n\nDiagnostic chain: 根据病史（E1）、临床检查（E2）以及影像学表现（E4, E5），支持中央性巨细胞肉芽肿的诊断。\nLimitations: 视觉证据字段仅复述原文图注；未把模型直接看图所得细节作为已验证事实。；缺乏病理结果以最终确诊\n</Think>\n<Answer>\n中央性巨细胞肉芽肿（central giant cell granuloma）\n</Answer>","language":"zh","images":[{"src":"assets/PMC12606825/13256_2025_5613_Fig2_HTML.jpg","name":"13256_2025_5613_Fig2_HTML.jpg","caption":"Radiographic findings: A Cropped orthopantomogram showing a large, multilocular radiolucency in the left mandible with resorption of the roots of teeth 37 and 38. B Three-dimensional computed tomography reconstruction illustrating ill-defined bone destruction. C Axial computed tomography view demonstrating the expansile nature of the lesion and perforation of the buccal cortical plate (arrowhead). D Coronal computed tomography view showing thinning of the inferior border (arrow)","types":["ct","opg_panoramic","radiograph"],"sha256":"da4ccfec1c6d4d90d4d2e52f7e7e9a581937e04c366d434e89620e4dc6a55e38","width":896,"height":768},{"src":"assets/PMC12606825/13256_2025_5613_Fig1_HTML.jpg","name":"13256_2025_5613_Fig1_HTML.jpg","caption":"Intraoral swelling on buccal and lingual aspect in 36 to 38 region denoted by black arrow","types":["intraoral_photo"],"sha256":"00297aea4d9191014338e03fe47830f68ded7e4140cdcc5cfc9796f09561e53e","width":707,"height":773}],"english":null}],"caseCount":47,"imageCount":95,"assetCount":96,"englishVariantCount":3,"englishImageCount":9,"textOnlyCount":2,"textOnlyIds":["PMC6738723","PMC11297549"],"categoryCounts":{"developmental_eruption":5,"endodontic_periapical":6,"implant_prosthetic":2,"infection":3,"mucosal_oral_lesion":5,"odontogenic_cyst_tumor":6,"oral_maxillofacial_other":6,"orthodontic_craniofacial":2,"other_dental":2,"periodontal":4,"salivary":2,"trauma_resorption":4},"licenseCounts":{"cc by":42,"cc by-nc":2,"cc by-nc-sa":3},"languageNote":"The 47 original source samples retain their Chinese text. Three separately identified earlier English samples are also available, with their original image sets."};
